      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"The +3 starts here (and on a reset): interrupts off, a delay of $6C03 rounds, then\nRAM_CLEAR.","comment":"No interrupts during start-up"},
        "1": {"comment":"$6C03 rounds"},
        "4": {"synopsis":"The delay.","comment":"One round"},
        "9": {"comment":"Every RAM bank cleared, then tested"},
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: ROM 3's RST $10 (CALL_ROM3), which prints A through the current channel.","comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A: A printed through the current channel"},
        "24": {"synopsis":"RST $18: ROM 3's RST $18 (CALL_ROM3): the character at CH_ADD.","comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "32": {"synopsis":"RST $20: ROM 3's RST $20 (CALL_ROM3): the next character at CH_ADD.","comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP: A = the next character at CH_ADD"},
        "40": {"synopsis":"RST $28: calls the routine in ROM 3 whose address is the word after the RST, then returns\npast the word:\n1. HL = that address; $5B5A = the place after the word, the return point.\n2. CALL_ROM3_GO keeps the address in $5B58, stacks $5B21 (ROM3_RETURN's copy) as the\n   routine's return, then the address, and jumps to $5B00 (SWAP_ROM's copy), whose RET\n   enters ROM 3 there with HL as it was.\n3. When the routine returns, $5B21 swaps back to this ROM and returns to $5B5A. Keeps every\n   register for the routine; interrupts are on afterwards (SWAP_ROM ends with EI).","comment":"HL = the return address, the word's place"},
        "41": {"comment":"A kept"},
        "42": {"comment":"The routine address's low byte"},
        "43": {"comment":"Past the word"},
        "45": {"comment":"$5B5A = the return point after the call"},
        "48": {"comment":"HL = the routine's address"},
        "51": {"comment":"A back"},
        "52": {"comment":"On in CALL_ROM3_GO"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"INT (interrupt mode 1): runs ROM 3's interrupt routine at $0038: the stack gets INT_RETURN,\n$5B00 (SWAP_ROM's copy, to come back) and $0038, then $5B00 swaps the ROMs and returns into\nROM 3's $0038. Keeps HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "57": {"comment":"INT_RETURN, for the end"},
        "61": {"comment":"SWAP_ROM's copy, to swap back after the routine"},
        "65": {"comment":"ROM 3's interrupt routine, entered by the swap's RET"},
        "69": {"comment":"Swap the ROMs: on in ROM 3 at $0038"},
        "72": {"synopsis":"Where the interrupt comes back to: HL back, the disk motor's time-out counted\n(MOTOR_TIMEOUT, interrupts off), interrupts on, and return.","comment":"HL back"},
        "73": {"comment":"The disk motor's time-out, interrupts off"},
        "77": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "102": {"synopsis":"The NMI handler: when NMIADD ($5CB0) is not zero it jumps there (JP (HL), with AF and HL\nstill on the stack); when it is zero it returns at once (NMI_RETURN).","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "104": {"comment":"HL = NMIADD"},
        "107": {"comment":"Is it 0?"},
        "111": {"comment":"No: jump there (AF and HL still stacked)"},
        "112": {"synopsis":"AF and HL back; RETN.","comment":"0: registers back"},
        "114": {"comment":"Return from the NMI"},
        "116": {"synopsis":"Counts the disk motor's time-out down: with bank 7 paged in (the paging byte $5B5C with bits\n0-2 set, to port $7FFD), when the count at $E600 is not 0 and FRAMES is even, the count goes\ndown by one; when it reaches 0, bit 3 of port $1FFD is cleared (its copy at $5B67 too),\nwhich turns the motor off. Then port $7FFD gets $5B5C back. The same job as ROM 2's\nMOTOR_TIMEOUT. Keeps AF, BC.","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "118": {"comment":"Bank 7 paged in: the count is at $E600"},
        "128": {"comment":"Is the motor's count running?"},
        "134": {"comment":"FRAMES even?"},
        "141": {"comment":"One less"},
        "145": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "148": {"comment":"Not 0 yet?"},
        "150": {"comment":"0: bit 3 of port $1FFD cleared, the motor off"},
        "153": {"comment":"Its copy with bit 3 cleared"},
        "161": {"comment":"Port $1FFD written"},
        "163": {"synopsis":"Port $7FFD gets the paging byte $5B5C back.","comment":"The paging byte back into port $7FFD"},
        "171": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "172": {"comment":"Return"},
        "174": {"synopsis":"CALL_ROM3's second half: the routine's address kept in $5B58; the stack gets ROM3_RETURN's\ncopy ($5B21) and the routine's address, HL as it was, then SWAP_ROM's copy at $5B00.","comment":"The routine's address kept"},
        "177": {"comment":"ROM3_RETURN's copy as the routine's return"},
        "180": {"comment":"ROM3_RETURN under it, HL back"},
        "181": {"comment":"The routine's address on top, HL back"},
        "182": {"comment":"The routine's address"},
        "186": {"comment":"Swap the ROMs: the RET enters ROM 3 at the routine"},
        "189": {"synopsis":"Copied to $5B00 at start-up with the routines after it ($00BD-$010E to $5B00-$5B51) and run\nfrom there: flips bit 4 of port $7FFD and bit 2 of port $1FFD (the ROM number's low and high\nbits; their copies at $5B5C and $5B67), with interrupts off, so that ROM 0 and ROM 3 change\nplaces (and ROM 1 and ROM 2); interrupts on, and a RET made with an address on the stack\ncontinues in the other ROM. Keeps every register.","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "191": {"comment":"Port $7FFD: bit 4, the ROM's low bit, flipped"},
        "194": {"comment":"The paging byte with bit 4 flipped"},
        "199": {"comment":"Interrupts off while paging"},
        "200": {"comment":"Stored and written"},
        "205": {"synopsis":"At $5B10: SWAP_ROM's second half, entered on its own by SWAP_HIGH_GO with AF and BC already\nstacked: only bit 2 of port $1FFD (the ROM's high bit) flipped, then interrupts on, BC and\nAF back and RET.","comment":"Port $1FFD: bit 2, the ROM's high bit, flipped"},
        "208": {"comment":"The other paging byte with bit 2 flipped"},
        "213": {"comment":"Stored and written"},
        "218": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "219": {"comment":"Registers back; the RET goes on in the other ROM"},
        "222": {"synopsis":"At $5B21: where a ROM 3 routine called by CALL_ROM3 returns to: the ROMs swapped back\n(SWAP_ROM), then on at the address in $5B5A, past the RST's word. Keeps every register.","comment":"Swap back to this ROM"},
        "225": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "226": {"comment":"The return point at $5B5A on the stack, HL back"},
        "230": {"comment":"On past the RST's word"},
        "231": {"synopsis":"At $5B2A: flips only the ROM's high bit (SWAP_ROM_HIGH at $5B10, so ROM 1 and ROM 3, or ROM\n0 and ROM 2, change places), then goes on at the address in $5B5A (GO_5B5A's copy at $5B34)\nin the ROM now paged in. Nothing in this ROM uses it; ROM 1 loads $5B2A (at $00AD, $1119,\n$1876). Keeps every register.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "232": {"comment":"GO_5B5A's copy ($5B34) as where to go on"},
        "235": {"comment":"GO_5B5A under the registers, HL back"},
        "236": {"comment":"Stacked as SWAP_ROM_HIGH expects them"},
        "238": {"comment":"Only the ROM's high bit flipped ($5B10)"},
        "241": {"synopsis":"At $5B34: jumps to the address in $5B5A, keeping every register.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "242": {"comment":"The address at $5B5A on the stack, HL back"},
        "246": {"comment":"Go there"},
        "247": {"synopsis":"At $5B3A: pages ROM 1 in from scratch, with interrupts off: port $1FFD = $10 (ROM high bit\n0, disk motor off) and port $7FFD = $10 (ROM 1, bank 0, normal screen), both copies set,\nthen on at $26A7 in ROM 1. ROM 1 pushes $5B3A and points ERR_SP at it (at $138E, $1444,\n$2665, $2728), so an error report ends up here.","comment":"Interrupts off while paging"},
        "248": {"comment":"Port $1FFD = $10: ROM high bit 0, motor off"},
        "250": {"comment":"Written"},
        "255": {"comment":"Its copy"},
        "258": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = $10: ROM 1, bank 0, normal screen"},
        "260": {"comment":"Written"},
        "265": {"comment":"Its copy"},
        "268": {"comment":"On at $26A7 in ROM 1, now paged in"},
        "271": {"synopsis":"Clears the eight RAM banks, 7 down to 0: each paged in at $C000 (port $7FFD) and $C000-$FFFF\nset to 0. Then RAM_TEST.","comment":"Eight banks, 7 down to 0"},
        "273": {"synopsis":"One bank: bank B - 1.","comment":"A = B - 1, the bank"},
        "274": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "276": {"comment":"Paged in at $C000"},
        "279": {"comment":"Written"},
        "281": {"comment":"$C000-$FFFF cleared to 0"},
        "287": {"comment":"$3FFF more after the first"},
        "290": {"comment":"The first byte 0"},
        "292": {"comment":"The rest"},
        "294": {"comment":"The counter back"},
        "295": {"comment":"The next bank"},
        "297": {"synopsis":"Tests the byte at $DCBA in each RAM bank, 0 up to 7: each of its eight bits is written alone\nand read back set, then the other seven written and the bit read back clear. A failure stops\nat RAM_FAULT with E counting the bits left and A' the bank. Bank 7 stays paged in\nafterwards. Then the AY's register 14 is set to $FF and the start-up goes on at COLD_START.","comment":"From bank 0 up"},
        "298": {"comment":"The byte tested in every bank"},
        "301": {"comment":"The paging port"},
        "304": {"synopsis":"One bank: bank A paged in, D = 1 (the bit), E = 8 (the count).","comment":"D = 1, the first bit; E = 8 bits"},
        "307": {"comment":"Bank A paged in at $C000"},
        "309": {"comment":"The bank kept in A'"},
        "310": {"synopsis":"One bit.","comment":"The bit alone written"},
        "311": {"comment":"Written"},
        "312": {"comment":"Read back: is the bit set?"},
        "314": {"comment":"No: a fault"},
        "317": {"comment":"Every other bit written"},
        "318": {"comment":"Written"},
        "319": {"comment":"Read back: is the bit clear?"},
        "321": {"comment":"No: a fault"},
        "324": {"comment":"The next bit"},
        "326": {"comment":"All eight bits?"},
        "327": {"comment":"The next bit"},
        "329": {"comment":"The bank back"},
        "330": {"comment":"The next bank"},
        "331": {"comment":"All eight banks?"},
        "333": {"comment":"The next bank"},
        "335": {"comment":"C = $FD for ports $FFFD and $BFFD"},
        "337": {"comment":"D, E = their high bytes $FF and $BF"},
        "341": {"comment":"AY register 14 selected (port $FFFD)"},
        "342": {"comment":"Register 14"},
        "346": {"comment":"Register 14 = $FF (port $BFFD)"},
        "347": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "351": {"comment":"On with the start-up"},
        "353": {"comment":"Not reached from anywhere: border from B'"},
        "354": {"comment":"B' as the colour"},
        "357": {"synopsis":"Forever. Nothing jumps to $0161, the border-setting code before it.","comment":"Forever"},
        "359": {"synopsis":"After the RAM test: A' = 0, then START_SETUP.","comment":"A' = 0: a start from reset"},
        "361": {"comment":"The stack above the screen, in bank 5"},
        "364": {"synopsis":"Sets the machine up (from COLD_START with A' = 0, and from $267C with A' = $52, without the\nRAM clear and test):\n1. The stack at $6000; AY register 7 = $FF; the RAM routines from $00BD copied to\n   $5B00-$5B51; $5B5D = $CF.\n2. As a 48K start: P_RAMT = $FFFF, the UDGs copied below it from ROM 3's letters A-U ($3EAF\n   down, through ROM 3's $1661), UDG, RASP/PIP, RAMTOP, CHARS = $3C00, IM 1, IY = $5C3A;\n   FLAGS bit 4 set (128K mode).\n3. The +3's own variables: $5B66 bits 7 and 3 cleared and bit 2 set, $5B7B = 9, $5B5F =\n   $000B, FLAGS2 bit 6 cleared, $5B61, $5B63 and $5B65 = 0, $FF24 = $EC00 (bank 7), $5B64 =\n   $50, $5B75 and $5B77 = 10, $5B79 and $5B7A = $54.\n4. CHANS from CHANS_128_INIT, the program, variable and edit-line pointers, the colours\n   ($38), $EC13 = 0, border 7, REPDEL $23 and REPPER 5, KSTATE free, STRMS from STRMS_INIT,\n   FLAGS bit 1 cleared, ERR_NR = $FF, DF_SZ = 2.\n5. With A' = $52 it ends at $2682. Otherwise the stack under the UDGs, interrupts on, CLS\n   (ROM 3's CLS_CMD), the test screen when BREAK is held (TEST_ON_BREAK), COPYRIGHT_MSG\n   printed; $5B6A = $5BFF, bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), $EC11 and $EC0F = $38; ROM\n   1's $257D (through $3E80); DF_SZ = 2, TV_FLAG bit 5 set, EDITOR_RESET, bank 0\n   (BANK0_STACK), and the start-up menu (MAIN_MENU).","comment":"AY register 7 selected"},
        "365": {"comment":"Register 7"},
        "369": {"comment":"Register 7 = $FF: tones and noise off"},
        "370": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "374": {"comment":"The RAM routines at $00BD copied to $5B00-$5B51"},
        "377": {"comment":"From $00BD, 82 bytes"},
        "385": {"comment":"$5B5D = $CF"},
        "387": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "390": {"comment":"P_RAMT = $FFFF"},
        "396": {"comment":"ROM 3's letters A-U ($3E08-$3EAF), 168 bytes"},
        "402": {"comment":"HL = the source's end, DE = P_RAMT"},
        "403": {"comment":"ROM 3's LDDR; RET (in MAKE_ROOM): the UDGs below P_RAMT"},
        "406": {"comment":"HL = the byte below them"},
        "407": {"comment":"UDG = $FF58, the first UDG"},
        "408": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "411": {"comment":"HL = $FF57"},
        "412": {"comment":"RASP = $40, PIP = 0"},
        "419": {"comment":"RAMTOP = $FF57, below the UDGs"},
        "422": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 7 cleared"},
        "425": {"comment":"Its bit 7 cleared"},
        "427": {"comment":"$5B7B = 9"},
        "432": {"comment":"CHARS = $3C00"},
        "438": {"comment":"Interrupt mode 1"},
        "440": {"comment":"IY at ERR_NR, as BASIC expects"},
        "444": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 4 set: 128K mode"},
        "448": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 3 cleared, bit 2 set"},
        "451": {"comment":"Bit 3 cleared"},
        "453": {"comment":"Bit 2 set"},
        "455": {"comment":"$5B5F = $000B"},
        "461": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 6 cleared"},
        "466": {"comment":"$5B61, $5B63 and $5B65 = 0"},
        "476": {"comment":"$FF24 = $EC00 (bank 7, left paged in by the test)"},
        "482": {"comment":"$5B64 = $50"},
        "487": {"comment":"$5B75 and $5B77 = 10"},
        "496": {"comment":"$5B79 and $5B7A = $54"},
        "504": {"comment":"CHANS = $5CB6"},
        "507": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "510": {"comment":"The channels from CHANS_128_INIT, 21 bytes"},
        "513": {"comment":"21 bytes"},
        "517": {"comment":"Copied to $5CB6"},
        "520": {"comment":"HL at the channels' $80 end marker"},
        "521": {"comment":"DATADD = it"},
        "524": {"comment":"PROG and VARS just after it"},
        "525": {"comment":"PROG"},
        "528": {"comment":"VARS"},
        "531": {"comment":"The variables' end marker"},
        "533": {"comment":"E_LINE after it"},
        "534": {"comment":"E_LINE"},
        "537": {"comment":"The edit line: ENTER and the $80 end marker"},
        "539": {"comment":"The edit line's end marker after ENTER"},
        "543": {"comment":"WORKSP, STKBOT and STKEND after it"},
        "546": {"comment":"STKBOT"},
        "549": {"comment":"STKEND"},
        "552": {"comment":"ATTR_P, ATTR_T and BORDCR = $38: black on white"},
        "554": {"comment":"ATTR_P"},
        "557": {"comment":"ATTR_T"},
        "560": {"comment":"BORDCR"},
        "563": {"comment":"$EC13 = 0 (bank 7)"},
        "567": {"comment":"White border"},
        "569": {"comment":"Written"},
        "571": {"comment":"REPDEL = $23, REPPER = 5"},
        "577": {"comment":"KSTATE's two key slots free ($FF)"},
        "580": {"comment":"The second slot free"},
        "583": {"comment":"STRMS from STRMS_INIT, 14 bytes"},
        "589": {"comment":"14 bytes"},
        "592": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "594": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 1 cleared: not the printer"},
        "598": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no report"},
        "602": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "606": {"comment":"A = the start's kind, from A'"},
        "607": {"comment":"$52 ('R', from $267C)?"},
        "609": {"comment":"Yes: this start ends at $2682"},
        "612": {"comment":"The stack just under the UDGs (RAMTOP + 1)"},
        "616": {"comment":"SP = RAMTOP + 1"},
        "617": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "618": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_CMD: the whole screen cleared"},
        "621": {"comment":"The test screen when BREAK is held"},
        "624": {"comment":"The copyright message"},
        "627": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "630": {"comment":"The editor's stack at $5BFF, kept in $5B6A"},
        "636": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "639": {"comment":"$EC11 and $EC0F = $38 (bank 7)"},
        "641": {"comment":"$EC11"},
        "644": {"comment":"$EC0F"},
        "647": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "650": {"comment":"ROM 1's $257D, through $3E80 and the word after"},
        "655": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "658": {"comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "662": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5 set"},
        "666": {"comment":"The editor's state cleared"},
        "669": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "672": {"comment":"The start-up menu"},
        "675": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at DE through RST $10, up to and including the character with bit 7 set\n(printed without it).\nExit: DE = the place after the text.","comment":"The character without bit 7"},
        "678": {"comment":"DE kept round the print"},
        "681": {"comment":"The character again"},
        "682": {"comment":"The next one"},
        "683": {"comment":"Bit 7 set: was it the last?"},
        "687": {"synopsis":"Start-up's test screen, shown only when BREAK (CAPS SHIFT and SPACE) is held; otherwise it\nreturns at once.\n1. Border 7, stream 2, TV_FLAG = 0, AT 0,0.\n2. TEST_TEXT (\"1987\", the \"87\" bright) printed in every ink and paper: inks 7 down to 0, for\n   each the papers 7 down to 0; then the pixels of lines 8-23 cleared and the attributes of\n   lines 0-7 copied over lines 8-15 and 16-23, which leaves colour bars.\n3. Interrupts off; then forever: a tone of $0370 half-cycles, and the key sets of\n   TEST_KEY_SETS tried in turn until one is held, $2000 misses before the next tone. A set\n   held jumps to its address: this ROM's $21E4 for Q A Z P L M, $22D5 for E U A, $0000 for B\n   V.","comment":"Is SPACE down (port $7FFE bit 0)?"},
        "692": {"comment":"No: back"},
        "693": {"comment":"Is CAPS SHIFT down (port $FEFE bit 0)?"},
        "698": {"comment":"No: back"},
        "699": {"comment":"White border"},
        "703": {"comment":"Stream 2"},
        "705": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: stream 2, the upper screen"},
        "708": {"comment":"TV_FLAG = 0"},
        "712": {"comment":"AT 0,0"},
        "719": {"comment":"E = 8: eight papers, eight inks, eight characters"},
        "721": {"comment":"B = the paper counter, D = the ink counter"},
        "723": {"synopsis":"One group of eight characters: ATTR_T from the paper (B - 1) and the ink (D - 1).","comment":"The paper (B - 1) into bits 3-5"},
        "731": {"comment":"The ink (D - 1)"},
        "733": {"comment":"ATTR_T = the colours"},
        "736": {"comment":"The eight characters of TEST_TEXT"},
        "740": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"One character"},
        "743": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "746": {"comment":"The next paper"},
        "748": {"comment":"The papers again from 8"},
        "749": {"comment":"The next ink"},
        "752": {"comment":"The pixels of lines 8-23 cleared ($4800-$57FF)"},
        "765": {"comment":"HL = $5800, the attributes of lines 0-7"},
        "766": {"comment":"Copied over lines 8-15 and 16-23: colour bars"},
        "774": {"comment":"No interrupts from here"},
        "775": {"synopsis":"The tone: $0370 half-cycles, the speaker bit flipped after each wait of $0099 rounds; then\nthe key sets.","comment":"A tone of $0370 half-cycles"},
        "778": {"comment":"Border 7, speaker bit 0"},
        "780": {"synopsis":"One half-cycle.","comment":"One half-cycle's wait"},
        "783": {"synopsis":"The wait."},
        "788": {"comment":"The speaker bit (bit 4) flipped"},
        "794": {"comment":"All half-cycles done?"},
        "799": {"comment":"$2000 misses before the tone again"},
        "802": {"comment":"The list of key sets"},
        "806": {"synopsis":"The next key set from TEST_KEY_SETS; after the last ($0000) the list starts again.","comment":"HL = the next set's address"},
        "816": {"comment":"The list's end?"},
        "820": {"comment":"Yes: from the start of the list"},
        "826": {"synopsis":"One row of the set: port BC read, its low five bits must be the set's byte. A set ends with\nport $0000 and the address to go to.","comment":"A keyboard row's port"},
        "831": {"comment":"The set's end?"},
        "835": {"comment":"That row's keys"},
        "839": {"comment":"Exactly these keys down?"},
        "840": {"comment":"Yes: the set's next row"},
        "842": {"comment":"No: one miss more"},
        "845": {"comment":"Misses left: the next set"},
        "847": {"comment":"None: the tone again"},
        "849": {"synopsis":"The whole set is held: on at its address.","comment":"The set's address"},
        "852": {"comment":"Jump there"},
        "854": {"synopsis":"A key set for TEST_ON_BREAK (TEST_KEY_SETS points at the byte before it): port and row value\nfor each row, $0000, then the address. $FBFE $1E (Q), $FDFE $1E (A), $FEFE $1D (Z), $DFFE\n$1E (P), $BFFE $1D (L), $7FFE $1B (M); then $21E4."},
        "876": {"synopsis":"A bit failed the RAM test (E = the bits left, A' = the bank): A = the bit's number, 0-7. In\nbank 0 the border shows that number and the machine stops (RAM_FAULT_STOP); in any other\nbank the border flashes between that colour and its complement (the number xor 7), forever.","comment":"A = the failing bit's number (8 - E)"},
        "879": {"comment":"Kept in A'; A = the bank"},
        "880": {"comment":"Bank 0?"},
        "883": {"comment":"Yes: A = the bit's number"},
        "884": {"comment":"A steady border in that colour"},
        "886": {"synopsis":"Forever.","comment":"Forever"},
        "888": {"synopsis":"Not bank 0: C = the bit's number, B = it xor 7.","comment":"A = the bit's number"},
        "889": {"comment":"C = it, B = it xor 7"},
        "894": {"synopsis":"Border C, a wait of 65536 rounds, border B, a wait of $2AAA rounds; forever.","comment":"Border colour C"},
        "897": {"comment":"A long wait"},
        "900": {"synopsis":"The long wait."},
        "905": {"comment":"Border colour B"},
        "908": {"comment":"A shorter wait"},
        "911": {"synopsis":"The short wait."},
        "916": {"comment":"Again"},
        "918": {"synopsis":"TEST_ON_BREAK's second key set, as TEST_KEYS_1: $FBFE $1B (E), $DFFE $17 (U), $FDFE $1E (A);\nthen $22D5."},
        "931": {"synopsis":"TEST_ON_BREAK's third key set: $7FFE $0F (B), $FEFE $0F (V); then $0000, a restart."},
        "941": {"synopsis":"TEST_ON_BREAK's list of key sets, each address the byte before a set: $0355 (TEST_KEYS_1),\n$0395 (TEST_KEYS_2), $03A2 (TEST_KEYS_3), and $0000 to end it."},
        "949": {"synopsis":"TEST_ON_BREAK's eight characters: BRIGHT 0, \"19\", BRIGHT 1, \"87\"."},
        "957": {"synopsis":"CHANS as start-up copies it to $5CB6 (21 bytes): K (output $09F4, input $10A8), S ($09F4,\n$15C4), X ($0F81, $15C4), P ($3A05, $3A00), then the $80 end marker. The addresses are ROM\n3's: K, S and X's as in the 48K ROM; P's are ROM 3's ROM_SWAP_3D06 and ROM_SWAP_3D03, which go\non in ROM 1."},
        "978": {"synopsis":"STRMS as start-up copies it to $5C10: the offsets of streams -3 to 3 into CHANS: 1 (K), 6\n(S), 11 (R), 1, 1, 6, 16 (P)."},
        "992": {"synopsis":"The start-up message, printed by START_SETUP through PRINT_BIT7_TEXT: $7F (the copyright\nsign in the character set), \"1982, 1986, 1987 Amstrad Plc.\" and ENTER, which has bit 7 set."},
        "1023": {"synopsis":"Rebuilds the editing rows from the program and draws them; the cursor goes to E_PPC's line\nwhen it is among them. An editing row is 35 bytes ($EC16 + 35 x row): 32 characters (0 an\nempty cell), a flags byte (bit 0: the first row of a line), then the line's number, high\nbyte first. The rows above the screen are kept at $F9DB (a count, then the rows); $FC9A is\nthe number of the line they belong to.\n1. $EEF5 bit 0 cleared, bit 1 set (E_PPC's line looked for); when E_PPC is 0, $EC06 = 0.\n2. The rows above are made again: $F9D7 = the line before $FC9A ($141D), both buffers\n   emptied ($12F5, $11A9), then as many rows as were above taken from the program ($11B2)\n   and put back above ($133D).\n3. Rows 0 to $EC15 filled with the next rows ($11B2). In E_PPC's first row (flags bit 0, the\n   number matching) the search succeeds ($EEF5 bit 0); from there the cursor moves $EC06\n   places on through the line's characters, row by row ($0F14), and is stored (CURSOR_STORE,\n   $0AE1) at the row and column reached, no further than a row's last character ($0F36);\n   $EEF5 = 0 then.\n4. E_PPC not found: $FC9A = E_PPC and the rows above emptied, so that its line comes at the\n   top (when E_PPC is 0: $FC9A = 0 and E_PPC = the program's first line, $1425); then the\n   whole again from ROWS_REBUILD_GO.\n5. The rows drawn (ROWS_DRAW).\nExit: Z.","comment":"$EEF5 bit 0 cleared, bit 1 set: E_PPC looked for"},
        "1026": {"comment":"Bit 0 cleared: not found yet"},
        "1028": {"comment":"Bit 1 set: looking"},
        "1030": {"synopsis":"Again from here (RB_AGAIN), with E_PPC changed.","comment":"Is E_PPC 0?"},
        "1035": {"comment":"No: keep $EC06"},
        "1037": {"comment":"Yes: $EC06 = 0"},
        "1040": {"synopsis":"The count of rows above the screen kept; $F9D7 = the line before $FC9A; both buffers\nemptied.","comment":"The count of rows above the screen kept"},
        "1044": {"comment":"$F9D7 = the line before $FC9A"},
        "1047": {"comment":"HL = the line before $FC9A"},
        "1053": {"comment":"Both buffers emptied"},
        "1056": {"comment":"The rows below emptied too"},
        "1059": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "1060": {"synopsis":"One row from the program put back above the screen, until the count is used up.","comment":"Rows left to put back above?"},
        "1061": {"comment":"None: fill the editing rows"},
        "1063": {"comment":"One row from the program"},
        "1064": {"comment":"HL = the next row's text"},
        "1067": {"comment":"Put above the screen"},
        "1068": {"comment":"Put above"},
        "1071": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "1075": {"synopsis":"Rows 0 to $EC15: B = the row, C = $EC15, DE = the row's place; the first two kept on the\nstack.","comment":"Row 0's place"},
        "1077": {"comment":"DE = row 0's place"},
        "1080": {"comment":"B = row 0, C = the last editing row"},
        "1081": {"comment":"C = $EC15, the last row"},
        "1085": {"comment":"Kept for the end"},
        "1087": {"synopsis":"One row: the next from the program ($11B2); while E_PPC is looked for, is this E_PPC's first\nrow?","comment":"The next row from the program"},
        "1090": {"comment":"Still looking for E_PPC's line?"},
        "1095": {"comment":"No: just copy"},
        "1099": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "1102": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "1103": {"comment":"The first row of a line?"},
        "1105": {"comment":"No: not E_PPC's"},
        "1107": {"comment":"DE = its number, high byte first"},
        "1111": {"comment":"Is it E_PPC?"},
        "1112": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "1117": {"comment":"Not the same: not E_PPC's"},
        "1119": {"comment":"Yes: found"},
        "1122": {"comment":"$EEF5 bit 0 set: found"},
        "1124": {"synopsis":"Not E_PPC's first row."},
        "1126": {"synopsis":"The row copied into the editing rows (35 bytes); DE = the next row's place.","comment":"The row copied into the editing rows"},
        "1128": {"comment":"35 bytes"},
        "1135": {"comment":"The next row's place kept"},
        "1137": {"comment":"DE = the copied row"},
        "1138": {"comment":"E_PPC's line found in this row?"},
        "1143": {"comment":"No: the next row"},
        "1145": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "1147": {"synopsis":"The cursor $EC06 places on: while there are places left and the row has a character at or\nafter column B ($0F14), one more column.","comment":"Places left to move?"},
        "1152": {"comment":"None: the search ends"},
        "1154": {"comment":"A character at or after column B?"},
        "1155": {"comment":"Is there text at or after column B?"},
        "1159": {"comment":"No: past the row's end"},
        "1161": {"comment":"One place used, one column on"},
        "1163": {"comment":"$EC06 = places left"},
        "1166": {"comment":"Again"},
        "1168": {"synopsis":"No places left: past the row's last character, B goes back to just after it ($0F36); the\nsearch ends ($EEF5 = 0).","comment":"Past the last character: back to just after it"},
        "1171": {"comment":"None: B back to just after the last"},
        "1174": {"comment":"The search ends"},
        "1177": {"comment":"$EEF5 = 0"},
        "1179": {"synopsis":"The cursor stored at this row, column B, remembered column B (CURSOR_STORE, $0AE1).","comment":"B = the column, C = the row"},
        "1180": {"comment":"The row number again"},
        "1184": {"comment":"The cursor stored there"},
        "1187": {"synopsis":"The next row, up to $EC15.","comment":"The row back"},
        "1189": {"comment":"Past the last editing row?"},
        "1190": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "1192": {"comment":"Up to the last"},
        "1194": {"comment":"Was E_PPC looked for?"},
        "1199": {"comment":"No: draw the rows"},
        "1201": {"comment":"Was it found?"},
        "1203": {"comment":"Found: draw the rows"},
        "1205": {"comment":"Not found: is E_PPC 0?"},
        "1210": {"comment":"Yes: the first line"},
        "1212": {"comment":"No: its line at the top"},
        "1215": {"comment":"The rows above emptied"},
        "1218": {"comment":"Again"},
        "1220": {"synopsis":"E_PPC 0: $FC9A = 0, and E_PPC = the program's first line ($1425).","comment":"E_PPC 0: $FC9A = 0"},
        "1223": {"comment":"E_PPC = the program's first line"},
        "1226": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "1229": {"synopsis":"Again (ROWS_REBUILD_GO).","comment":"The whole again"},
        "1231": {"comment":"From ROWS_REBUILD_GO"},
        "1234": {"synopsis":"Rows 0 to $EC15 drawn (ROWS_DRAW, with Z)."},
        "1236": {"comment":"Z: the cursor not moved after drawing"},
        "1237": {"synopsis":"Draws editing rows B to C on the screen, each through $1703. With NZ on entry the cursor\nwould then be moved $EC06 places on ($0C48 each) and stored ($0AE1); both callers (RB_DRAW\nand $10DB) enter with Z, so that part ($04EB-$04FE) is never run.\nEntry: B = the first row, C = the last, F's Z flag as above.\nExit: Z; HL = the place after the last row drawn.","comment":"The flags kept"},
        "1238": {"comment":"A = the last row, C = the first"},
        "1240": {"comment":"The first row's place"},
        "1243": {"comment":"HL = the row"},
        "1244": {"synopsis":"One row drawn ($1703); the next, up to A.","comment":"Kept"},
        "1245": {"comment":"Drawn"},
        "1249": {"comment":"The next row's place"},
        "1252": {"comment":"The next row's place"},
        "1253": {"comment":"Up to the last"},
        "1255": {"comment":"Up to the last"},
        "1257": {"comment":"Z on entry: done"},
        "1259": {"comment":"The cursor's place"},
        "1262": {"synopsis":"One place on ($0C48), $EC06 times, then the cursor stored.","comment":"One place on"},
        "1265": {"comment":"$EC06 places in all"},
        "1271": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "1274": {"comment":"More to move?"},
        "1276": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1279": {"comment":"Not reached"},
        "1280": {"synopsis":"Clears editing rows 0 to $EC15 on the screen ($1D70 with B = 0, D = $EC15).\nExit: through $1D70.","comment":"From line 0"},
        "1282": {"comment":"To the last editing row"},
        "1285": {"comment":"D = the last row"},
        "1286": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "1289": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the editing rows up by one: row 0 goes to the rows above the screen ($133D; when\nthere is no room there, nothing is done), the next row from the program ($11B2) comes in at\nrow $EC15 (ROWS_UP_FROM with B = 0).\nExit: carry when scrolled; HL kept when not.","comment":"Row 0"},
        "1292": {"comment":"C = row 0"},
        "1293": {"comment":"DE = its place"},
        "1296": {"comment":"Put above the screen: was there room?"},
        "1299": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "1300": {"comment":"No: nothing done"},
        "1301": {"comment":"HL = the next row from the program"},
        "1304": {"synopsis":"Rows B+1 to $EC15 moved up by one into rows B to $EC15 - 1, the screen scrolled the same way\n($1717), and the row at HL copied into row $EC15.\nEntry: B = the row that goes, DE = its place, HL = the row that comes in at the bottom.\nExit: carry. Keeps BC."},
        "1305": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "1306": {"comment":"HL = the row below row B"},
        "1309": {"comment":"HL = the next row's place"},
        "1310": {"comment":"Is B the last row?"},
        "1315": {"comment":"Yes: no rows to move"},
        "1318": {"synopsis":"One row up.","comment":"One row up, 35 bytes"},
        "1319": {"comment":"35 bytes"},
        "1325": {"comment":"Up to the last row"},
        "1326": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "1328": {"comment":"Up to the last"},
        "1331": {"synopsis":"The screen scrolled up ($1717); the new row into the last row.","comment":"HL = the new row"},
        "1332": {"comment":"The screen scrolled up the same way"},
        "1335": {"comment":"The new row into the last row"},
        "1338": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "1340": {"comment":"Carry: scrolled"},
        "1343": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the editing rows down by one: the last row above the screen comes back ($12FE; when\nthere is none, nothing is done) and goes in at row 0 (ROWS_DOWN_FROM with B = 0).\nExit: carry when scrolled.","comment":"Row 0"},
        "1345": {"comment":"The last row above the screen back: was there one?"},
        "1348": {"comment":"No: nothing done"},
        "1349": {"synopsis":"Row $EC15 goes to the rows below the screen ($11F1; when there is no room there, nothing is\ndone), rows B to $EC15 - 1 move down by one, the screen is scrolled the same way ($172B),\nand the row at HL is copied into row B.\nEntry: B = the row, HL = the row that comes in.\nExit: carry when done. Keeps BC."},
        "1350": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "1351": {"comment":"C = the last row"},
        "1354": {"comment":"C = $EC15"},
        "1355": {"comment":"Its place"},
        "1358": {"comment":"It goes below the screen: was there room?"},
        "1361": {"comment":"No: nothing done"},
        "1363": {"comment":"DE = the end of the row before"},
        "1364": {"comment":"HL = the last row's end"},
        "1367": {"comment":"HL = the last row's end"},
        "1370": {"comment":"Is B the last row?"},
        "1372": {"comment":"Yes: no rows to move"},
        "1374": {"synopsis":"One row down (copied from its end).","comment":"One row down, from its end"},
        "1375": {"comment":"35 bytes, backwards"},
        "1381": {"comment":"Down to row B"},
        "1382": {"comment":"The row before"},
        "1384": {"comment":"Down to row B"},
        "1386": {"synopsis":"DE = row B's place; the screen scrolled down ($172B); the new row into row B.","comment":"DE = row B's place"},
        "1387": {"comment":"Row B's start"},
        "1390": {"comment":"The screen scrolled down the same way"},
        "1393": {"comment":"The new row into row B"},
        "1396": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "1398": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "1401": {"synopsis":"No room below: no carry.","comment":"Not done"},
        "1402": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "1404": {"synopsis":"Puts character A in column B of the row at DE, moving columns B to 30 one to the right.\nExit: A = E = the character pushed out of column 31; Z when that was 0 (an empty cell); HL =\nthe row's flags byte. Keeps BC, DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "1405": {"comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "1409": {"comment":"D = the character carried, A = the column"},
        "1411": {"synopsis":"One column: its character swapped with the one carried, up to column 31.","comment":"Swapped with the column's"},
        "1412": {"comment":"The carried one in"},
        "1414": {"comment":"The next column"},
        "1415": {"comment":"The next column"},
        "1416": {"comment":"Up to column 31"},
        "1418": {"comment":"Up to column 31"},
        "1420": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out; is it 0?"},
        "1421": {"comment":"Z when 0"},
        "1425": {"synopsis":"Takes the character in column B out of the row at DE, moving columns B+1 to 31 one to the\nleft; character A comes in at column 31.\nExit: A = E = the character taken out; Z when it was 0 (an empty cell); HL = the row's flags\nbyte. Keeps BC, DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "1426": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "1430": {"comment":"Kept for the exit"},
        "1431": {"comment":"D = the character carried in"},
        "1432": {"comment":"From column 31"},
        "1434": {"comment":"Into the loop at column 31"},
        "1436": {"synopsis":"One column: its character swapped with the one carried; column B ends it.","comment":"Swapped with the column's"},
        "1437": {"comment":"The carried one in"},
        "1439": {"comment":"Column B reached?"},
        "1440": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "1442": {"comment":"One column left"},
        "1443": {"synopsis":"One column to the left.","comment":"The column to the left"},
        "1446": {"synopsis":"Column B's character in A; Z when it was 0.","comment":"A = column B's character; is it 0?"},
        "1447": {"comment":"Z when 0"},
        "1452": {"synopsis":"Back to RAM bank 0 (paging byte 0: ROM 0, bank 0, normal screen, through PAGE_WRITE) and to\nthe stack kept in $5B6A, which in turn keeps this one: the pair of BANK7_STACK. The return\naddress goes with the caller; AF and HL kept (HL through $5B58).\nChanges: AF'.","comment":"A kept in A'"},
        "1453": {"comment":"Paging byte 0: bank 0, ROM 0, normal screen"},
        "1455": {"comment":"Interrupts off while the stack changes"},
        "1456": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "1459": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "1460": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "1463": {"comment":"The other stack swapped in"},
        "1466": {"comment":"$5B6A = this stack"},
        "1470": {"comment":"SP = the other"},
        "1471": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "1472": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "1475": {"comment":"The return address back"},
        "1476": {"comment":"A back"},
        "1478": {"synopsis":"Writes A to port $7FFD and to the paging byte at $5B5C. Keeps BC.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "1479": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "1482": {"comment":"Written"},
        "1484": {"comment":"Its copy at $5B5C"},
        "1489": {"synopsis":"Swaps the stack with the one kept in $5B6A, then pages RAM bank 7 in at $C000 (paging byte\n7, PAGE_WRITE): where the editor's own data lives ($EC00 up). The return address goes with\nthe caller; AF and HL kept (HL through $5B58).\nChanges: AF'.","comment":"A kept in A'"},
        "1490": {"comment":"No interrupts while the stack changes"},
        "1491": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "1492": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "1495": {"comment":"The other stack swapped in"},
        "1498": {"comment":"$5B6A = this stack"},
        "1502": {"comment":"SP = the other"},
        "1503": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "1506": {"comment":"The return address back"},
        "1507": {"comment":"Paging byte 7: bank 7 at $C000"},
        "1509": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "1512": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "1513": {"comment":"A back"},
        "1515": {"synopsis":"The editor's key table for TABLE_DISPATCH ($216B; KEY_DISPATCH with no menu up): a count\n($15), then for each key its code and the address of its routine: $0B $0B64, $0A $0B85, $08\n$0BA7, $09 $0BB3, $AD $0B1F, $AC $0AF5, $AF $0AA4, $AE $0AB1, $A6 $0A53, $A5 $0A7B, $A8\n$0B57, $A7 $0B4A, $AA KEY_DELETE_RIGHT, $0C KEY_DELETE_LEFT, $B3 $10EA, $B4 $108F, $B0\n$1145, $B1 $1111, $0D $0A14 (ENTER), $A9 SCREEN_TOGGLE, $07 MENU_OPEN."},
        "1579": {"synopsis":"The key table with a menu up (KEY_DISPATCH): a count (4), then code and routine for each\nkey: $0B MENU_UP, $0A MENU_DOWN, $07 and $0D MENU_SELECT."},
        "1592": {"synopsis":"Clears the editor's state: UPPER_SETUP, $FC9A = 0, $EC0D = $82, E_PPC = 0, $16BB, $175D.","comment":"Editing in the upper screen"},
        "1595": {"comment":"$FC9A = 0: no rows above"},
        "1598": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1601": {"comment":"$EC0D = $82"},
        "1603": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1606": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0"},
        "1609": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1612": {"comment":"The editing rows set up ($16BB)"},
        "1615": {"comment":"The keys' defaults ($175D)"},
        "1619": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu: $5B6A = $5BFF, bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), stream 2 (ROM 3's\nSTREAM_SELECT); then MAIN_MENU_SET.\nObserved: the start-up menu \"128 +3\" lists Loader, +3 BASIC, Calculator and 48 BASIC, above\n\"1982, 1986, 1987 Amstrad Plc.\" and \"Drives A: and M: available.\".","comment":"The editor's stack at $5BFF"},
        "1622": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1625": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1628": {"comment":"Stream 2"},
        "1630": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: stream 2, the upper screen"},
        "1633": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's actions (MENU_ACTIONS) and text ($0804) into $F6EA and $F6EC; $EC0D bit\n1 set (a menu up), bit 4 cleared, $EC0C = 0; the menu drawn ($189F), then the key loop\n(MAIN_KEY_LOOP). EDITOR_TO_MENU comes here with bank 7 and its stack already in place.","comment":"$F6EA = the menu's actions"},
        "1636": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1639": {"comment":"$F6EC = its text"},
        "1642": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1646": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 1 set (a menu up), bit 4 cleared"},
        "1653": {"comment":"$EC0C = 0: the bar on item 0"},
        "1657": {"comment":"The menu drawn"},
        "1661": {"comment":"The key loop"},
        "1664": {"synopsis":"The +3 BASIC editor and the Calculator: IX = $FD98, $5B6A = $5BFF, bank 7 and its stack,\nstream 2, the key mode ($185F); it waits for a key (FLAGS bit 5), then: $EC0D bit 3 cleared;\nunless editing is in the lower screen ($EC0D bit 6), the bar for the mode $EC0E (0: +3\nBASIC, $1A5F; 4: the Calculator, $1A64; any other: the start-up menu, EDITOR_TO_MENU); then\nEDITOR_ROWS.","comment":"IX = $FD98"},
        "1668": {"comment":"The editor's stack at $5BFF"},
        "1671": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1674": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1677": {"comment":"Stream 2"},
        "1679": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: stream 2, the upper screen"},
        "1682": {"comment":"The key mode set"},
        "1685": {"comment":"Has a key arrived (FLAGS bit 5)?"},
        "1688": {"synopsis":"Until a key arrives (FLAGS bit 5)."},
        "1690": {"comment":"Not yet: wait"},
        "1692": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 3 cleared"},
        "1697": {"comment":"Editing in the lower screen?"},
        "1699": {"comment":"Yes: no bar"},
        "1701": {"comment":"The mode: 4, the Calculator?"},
        "1706": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1708": {"comment":"0, +3 BASIC?"},
        "1710": {"comment":"Neither: the start-up menu"},
        "1713": {"comment":"The +3 BASIC bar"},
        "1716": {"comment":"To the rows"},
        "1718": {"synopsis":"Calculator: its bar ($1A64).","comment":"The Calculator's bar"},
        "1721": {"synopsis":"The rows above and below the screen emptied ($11A9, $12F5); the Calculator goes straight to\nthe key loop. MENU_SET_GO jumps here.","comment":"The rows below the screen emptied"},
        "1724": {"comment":"The rows above emptied"},
        "1727": {"comment":"The Calculator?"},
        "1732": {"comment":"Yes: straight to the key loop"},
        "1734": {"comment":"Is E_PPC set?"},
        "1739": {"comment":"Yes: from it"},
        "1741": {"comment":"Is there a program (PROG = VARS)?"},
        "1744": {"comment":"BC = VARS"},
        "1749": {"comment":"Equal: no program"},
        "1753": {"comment":"No: $EC08 = 0"},
        "1756": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1759": {"synopsis":"HL = $EC08 in place of E_PPC (set to 0 first when there is no program).","comment":"HL = $EC08"},
        "1762": {"synopsis":"E_PPC = the number of the first line at or after HL (bank 0; ROM 3's FIND_LINE and LINE_NO);\nthen, unless $EC0D bit 5 is set, $EC06 = 0, the rows rebuilt (ROWS_REBUILD), the cursor\nshown ($0AC2) and the ENTER key's routine run ($0A14); on to MAIN_KEY_LOOP.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "1765": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_LINE: the first line at or after HL"},
        "1768": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_NO: DE = its number"},
        "1771": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack"},
        "1774": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "1778": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 5 set?"},
        "1783": {"comment":"Yes: straight to the key loop"},
        "1785": {"comment":"$EC06 = 0"},
        "1788": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "1791": {"comment":"The rows rebuilt"},
        "1794": {"comment":"The cursor shown"},
        "1797": {"comment":"As ENTER"},
        "1800": {"synopsis":"The stack reset to $5BFF; then forever: a key (WAIT_KEY, $1876), a click (CLICK_A with PIP),\nand the key handled (KEY_DISPATCH).","comment":"The stack reset to $5BFF"},
        "1803": {"synopsis":"The next key.","comment":"A key"},
        "1806": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "1807": {"comment":"A click of PIP"},
        "1810": {"comment":"The click"},
        "1813": {"comment":"The key back"},
        "1814": {"comment":"Handled"},
        "1817": {"comment":"Again"},
        "1819": {"synopsis":"Handles key A: looked up in KEY_TABLE_B when $EC0D bit 1 is set (a menu is up), else in\nKEY_TABLE_A (TABLE_DISPATCH, $216B); a key found runs its routine (and a click when that\nreturns no carry). A key not found: with $EC0D bit 1 set, MODE = 0; otherwise, with $EC0D\nbit 0 set, a click; below $A3, KEY_INSERT; $A3 and up go back to KEY_LOOP_WAIT, leaving\nKEY_DISPATCH's return address on the stack.","comment":"A menu up ($EC0D bit 1)?"},
        "1824": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "1825": {"comment":"The menu's keys"},
        "1828": {"comment":"Yes: the menu's keys"},
        "1830": {"comment":"No menu: the editor's keys"},
        "1833": {"synopsis":"The key looked up (TABLE_DISPATCH).","comment":"Looked up and run: found?"},
        "1836": {"comment":"Not found"},
        "1838": {"comment":"Found: a click when it returns no carry"},
        "1843": {"synopsis":"Not in the table.","comment":"Not found: a menu up?"},
        "1844": {"comment":"No menu"},
        "1846": {"comment":"Menu up: MODE = 0"},
        "1847": {"comment":"MODE = 0: K mode back"},
        "1851": {"synopsis":"No menu up.","comment":"$EC0D bit 0 set?"},
        "1856": {"comment":"No: no click"},
        "1858": {"comment":"Yes: a click"},
        "1862": {"synopsis":"Below $A3: KEY_INSERT; otherwise ignored.","comment":"Below $A3?"},
        "1864": {"comment":"No: ignored (the return address left stacked)"},
        "1866": {"comment":"A character: put in"},
        "1869": {"synopsis":"Key $A9 and the editor's menu item 2 (MENU_SCREEN): moves editing between the upper screen\nand the two-row lower screen. Not in the Calculator ($EC0E = 4: returns with no carry). The\nrows cleared on the screen (ROWS_CLEAR), $EC0D bit 3 cleared and bit 6 flipped; bit 6 now\nset: SCREEN_TO_LOWER, clear: SCREEN_TO_UPPER.\nExit: carry.","comment":"The Calculator?"},
        "1874": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "1875": {"comment":"The rows cleared from the screen"},
        "1878": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 3 cleared"},
        "1881": {"comment":"Bit 3 cleared"},
        "1883": {"comment":"Bit 6 flipped: the other screen"},
        "1884": {"comment":"Bit 6 flipped"},
        "1887": {"comment":"Is it the lower screen now?"},
        "1889": {"comment":"No: the upper screen"},
        "1891": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1896": {"synopsis":"Now the upper screen.","comment":"No: the upper"},
        "1899": {"synopsis":"Carry.","comment":"Carry"},
        "1901": {"synopsis":"Editing in the lower screen: lines 21-23 cleared ($1A93), $EC0D bit 6 set, two editing rows\n($0F00), the window for lines 22-23 ($1C9A), the cursor's start (CURSOR_SET_LOWER); then\nSCREEN_REFILL.","comment":"Lines 21-23 cleared"},
        "1904": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 6 set: the lower screen"},
        "1907": {"comment":"Bit 6 set"},
        "1909": {"comment":"Two editing rows"},
        "1912": {"comment":"The window for lines 22-23"},
        "1915": {"comment":"The cursor's start"},
        "1920": {"synopsis":"Editing in the upper screen: $EC0D bit 6 cleared, UPPER_SETUP, the \"+3 BASIC\" bar ($1A5F);\nthen SCREEN_REFILL.","comment":"$EC0D bit 6 cleared: the upper screen"},
        "1923": {"comment":"Bit 6 cleared"},
        "1925": {"comment":"Editing in the upper screen"},
        "1928": {"comment":"The +3 BASIC bar"},
        "1931": {"synopsis":"When $FC9A is not 0, the line before it is looked up ($141D; HL is not kept, so $FC9A\nstays); the rows rebuilt (ROWS_REBUILD), and the cursor shown ($0AC2).","comment":"Rows above the screen?"},
        "1936": {"comment":"Yes: the line before $FC9A looked up"},
        "1939": {"comment":"The rows rebuilt"},
        "1942": {"comment":"The cursor shown"},
        "1945": {"synopsis":"A click of RASP / 2 (CLICK_A).","comment":"A = RASP / 2"},
        "1948": {"comment":"Halved"},
        "1950": {"synopsis":"A short tone: DE = A, HL = $0C80, through ROM 3's TONE_OUT. Keeps IX.","comment":"IX kept round TONE_OUT"},
        "1952": {"comment":"DE = A, the cycles"},
        "1954": {"comment":"E = A"},
        "1955": {"comment":"HL = $0C80, the pitch"},
        "1958": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's TONE_OUT; IX back.","comment":"ROM 3's TONE_OUT"},
        "1961": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "1964": {"synopsis":"A tone with DE = $30 and HL = $0300 (a higher pitch than CLICK_A's $0C80), through ROM 3's\nTONE_OUT. Called from $0DBA. Keeps IX.","comment":"IX kept round TONE_OUT"},
        "1966": {"comment":"DE = $30 cycles"},
        "1969": {"comment":"HL = $0300, a higher pitch"},
        "1972": {"comment":"Through TONE_OUT"},
        "1974": {"synopsis":"Key $07 (EDIT) in the editor: the cursor off ($0ABC), $EC0D bit 1 set (a menu up), the bar\non the first item ($EC0C = 0), and the current menu (its text at ($F6EC)) drawn ($189F).\nExit: carry.\nObserved: EDIT in +3 BASIC opens Options: +3 BASIC, Renumber, Screen, Print, Exit.","comment":"The cursor off"},
        "1977": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 1 set: a menu up"},
        "1980": {"comment":"Bit 1 set"},
        "1982": {"comment":"$EC0C = 0: the bar on item 0"},
        "1983": {"comment":"$EC0C = 0"},
        "1985": {"comment":"The current menu's text"},
        "1988": {"comment":"Drawn"},
        "1989": {"comment":"Drawn"},
        "1992": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "1994": {"synopsis":"Keys $0D (ENTER) and $07 (EDIT) with a menu up: $EC0D bit 1 cleared, the screen under the\nmenu put back ($1955), the item $EC0C's routine from the actions at ($F6EA) run\n(TABLE_DISPATCH, $216B), then the cursor shown ($0AC2).","comment":"$EC0D bit 1 cleared: no menu up"},
        "1997": {"comment":"Bit 1 cleared"},
        "2000": {"comment":"A = the bar's item ($EC0C)"},
        "2001": {"comment":"The menu's actions"},
        "2006": {"comment":"The screen under the menu put back"},
        "2009": {"comment":"The item back"},
        "2011": {"comment":"The item's routine run"},
        "2014": {"comment":"The cursor shown"},
        "2017": {"synopsis":"Key $0B (up) with a menu up: the bar one item up (MENU_MOVE with carry).","comment":"Carry: up"},
        "2018": {"comment":"Into MENU_MOVE"},
        "2020": {"synopsis":"Key $0A (down) with a menu up: the bar one item down (MENU_MOVE without carry).","comment":"No carry: down"},
        "2021": {"synopsis":"The bar moved from item $EC0C, up ($19BE) with carry, down ($19CD) without, in the menu\nwhose text is at ($F6EC); $EC0C = the new item.\nExit: carry.","comment":"A = the bar's item"},
        "2025": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "2026": {"comment":"The menu's text"},
        "2029": {"comment":"Up: the bar one item up"},
        "2032": {"comment":"Down: one item down"},
        "2035": {"comment":"HL = $EC0C"},
        "2036": {"comment":"The new item"},
        "2037": {"synopsis":"Item 0 of the editor's and the Calculator's menus (EDIT_MENU_ACTS, CALC_MENU_ACTS): nothing;\nthe menu is just gone.\nExit: carry.","comment":"Carry"},
        "2039": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's actions (MAIN_MENU_SET): a count (4), then for each item its number and\nroutine: 0 MENU_LOADER, 1 MENU_P3_BASIC, 2 MENU_CALCULATOR, 3 GO_48_BASIC. The text follows\nat $0804: a count (5), the title \"128 +3  \" ended by $FF."},
        "2062": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's items, last letter with bit 7 set: Loader, +3 BASIC, Calculator, 48\nBASIC, then $A0. The bars $1A69, $1A5F and $1A64 print the first three ($080E, $0814, $081C)\nas their titles."},
        "2095": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu (EDITOR_MENU_SET): a count (5), then item 0 MENU_STAY, 1 MENU_RENUMBER, 2\nMENU_SCREEN, 3 MENU_PRINT, 4 MENU_EXIT; then ($083F) a count (6) and the title \"Options \"\nended by $FF."},
        "2121": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu items, last letter with bit 7 set: +3 BASIC, Renumber, Screen, Print,\nExit, then $A0."},
        "2153": {"synopsis":"The Calculator's menu (MENU_CALCULATOR): a count (2), item 0 MENU_STAY, item 1 MENU_EXIT;\nthen ($0870) a count (3) and the title \"Options \" ended by $FF."},
        "2170": {"synopsis":"The Calculator's menu items, last letter with bit 7 set: Calculator, Exit, then $A0."},
        "2185": {"synopsis":"MENU_LOADER's text for the lower screen (PRINT_BIT7_TEXT): AT 0,0, INK 0, PAPER 7, BRIGHT 0,\nthen \"Insert tape and press PLAY\", ENTER, \"To cancel - press BREAK twice\", its last letter\nwith bit 7 set."},
        "2250": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu item 2: editing moved to the other screen (SCREEN_TOGGLE), then\nEDITOR_MENU_SET.","comment":"Editing on the other screen"},
        "2253": {"comment":"The editor's menu again"},
        "2255": {"synopsis":"Back to the start-up menu (the editor's menu item 4, the Calculator's item 1): $EC0D bit 6\ncleared, UPPER_SETUP, screen lines 0-23 cleared ($1D70), bank 0 and the machine stack\n(BANK0_STACK), then MAIN_MENU.","comment":"$EC0D bit 6 cleared"},
        "2258": {"comment":"Bit 6 cleared"},
        "2260": {"comment":"Editing in the upper screen"},
        "2263": {"comment":"Lines 0-23 cleared"},
        "2267": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "2270": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2273": {"comment":"The start-up menu"},
        "2276": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's 48 BASIC (MENU_ACTIONS item 3): bank 0 and the machine stack\n(BANK0_STACK), then ROM 1's $14A4 through $3E80, which does the rest.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2279": {"comment":"ROM 1's $14A4, through $3E80 and the word after"},
        "2285": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's item 0, Loader: the \"Loader\" bar ($1A69), LOADER_MSG in the lower screen\n(TV_FLAG bit 0 set meanwhile) unless $5B66 bit 4 is set, TV_FLAG bit 6 set, $EC0E = 7, AT\n0,0 ($1922), bank 0 (BANK0_STACK), then ROM 1's $1304 through $3E80.","comment":"The Loader bar"},
        "2288": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 set: the lower screen"},
        "2291": {"comment":"Bit 0 set"},
        "2293": {"comment":"The loader's message"},
        "2296": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "2297": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 4 set?"},
        "2303": {"comment":"Yes: no message"},
        "2305": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "2308": {"synopsis":"With or without the message: TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared and bit 6 set, $EC0E = 7, AT 0,0, then\nROM 1's $1304.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared, bit 6 set"},
        "2310": {"comment":"Bit 6 set"},
        "2312": {"comment":"$EC0E = 7"},
        "2314": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "2317": {"comment":"AT 0,0"},
        "2320": {"comment":"PRINT_AT_BC"},
        "2323": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2326": {"comment":"ROM 1's $1304, through $3E80 and the word after"},
        "2332": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu item 1: the program renumbered ($1A9A; a click when that returns no\ncarry), E_PPC = 0, $EC08 = 0, then MENU_BAR_BACK.","comment":"The program renumbered"},
        "2335": {"comment":"A click when that returns no carry"},
        "2338": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0"},
        "2341": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "2344": {"comment":"$EC08 = 0"},
        "2347": {"comment":"The bar, then the editor's menu"},
        "2349": {"synopsis":"The editor's menu item 3: bank 0 (BANK0_STACK) and ROM 1's $146D through $3E80 (LLIST run as\na command), then MENU_BAR_BACK.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "2352": {"comment":"ROM 1's $146D (LLIST run), through $3E80"},
        "2357": {"synopsis":"Unless editing is in the lower screen ($EC0D bit 6), the \"+3 BASIC\" bar again (as\nMENU_P3_BASIC); then EDITOR_MENU_SET.","comment":"Editing in the lower screen?"},
        "2362": {"comment":"Yes: no bar"},
        "2364": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's item 1, +3 BASIC: TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared, the \"+3 BASIC\" bar ($1A5F),\nthen EDITOR_MENU_SET.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared"},
        "2367": {"comment":"Bit 0 cleared"},
        "2369": {"comment":"The +3 BASIC bar"},
        "2372": {"synopsis":"$EC0D bits 5 and 4 cleared; mode 0 (+3 BASIC), the editor's menu (EDIT_MENU_ACTS, its text\nat $083F); then MENU_SET_GO.","comment":"$EC0D bits 5 and 4 cleared"},
        "2375": {"comment":"Bit 5 cleared"},
        "2377": {"comment":"Bit 4 cleared"},
        "2379": {"comment":"Mode 0: +3 BASIC"},
        "2381": {"comment":"The editor's menu actions"},
        "2384": {"comment":"Its text"},
        "2387": {"comment":"Set and on"},
        "2389": {"synopsis":"The start-up menu's item 2: $EC0D bits 5 and 4 set, bit 6 cleared; UPPER_SETUP; the\n\"Calculator\" bar ($1A64); $EC0E = 4; E_PPC = 0; the rows rebuilt (ROWS_REBUILD); the cursor\nat row 0, column 0 ($0AC8); mode 4 and the Calculator's menu (CALC_MENU_ACTS, its text at\n$0870), then MENU_SET_GO.","comment":"$EC0D bits 5 and 4 set, bit 6 cleared"},
        "2392": {"comment":"Bit 5 set"},
        "2394": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "2396": {"comment":"Bit 6 cleared"},
        "2398": {"comment":"Editing in the upper screen"},
        "2401": {"comment":"The Calculator's bar"},
        "2404": {"comment":"$EC0E = 4"},
        "2406": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "2409": {"comment":"E_PPC = 0"},
        "2412": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "2415": {"comment":"The rows rebuilt"},
        "2418": {"comment":"Row 0, column 0"},
        "2421": {"comment":"A = 0: the remembered column"},
        "2422": {"comment":"The cursor put there"},
        "2425": {"comment":"Mode 4: the Calculator"},
        "2427": {"comment":"The Calculator's menu actions"},
        "2430": {"comment":"Its text"},
        "2433": {"synopsis":"$EC0E = A (the mode), $F6EA = HL (the menu's actions), $F6EC = DE (its text), then on in\nEDITOR_MAIN at EDITOR_ROWS.","comment":"$EC0E = the mode"},
        "2436": {"comment":"$F6EA = the actions"},
        "2439": {"comment":"$F6EC = the text"},
        "2443": {"comment":"On in EDITOR_MAIN"},
        "2446": {"synopsis":"Editing in the upper screen: 21 editing rows ($0EF2), the window for lines 0-20 ($1C91), and\nthe cursor's start (CURSOR_SET_UPPER).","comment":"21 editing rows in the upper screen"},
        "2449": {"comment":"The window for lines 0-20"},
        "2452": {"comment":"The cursor's start"},
        "2455": {"synopsis":"EDITOR_MAIN with a mode other than 0 or 4: screen lines 0-23 cleared ($1D70), then\nMAIN_MENU_SET (the start-up menu set up and drawn).","comment":"Lines 0-23 cleared"},
        "2459": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "2462": {"comment":"The start-up menu set and drawn"},
        "2465": {"synopsis":"CURSOR_SET_UPPER's block for $2157: a count (6), then $F6EE-$F6F3 = 0, 0, 0, 4, $10, $14\n(row, column and remembered column 0, then three bytes for the upper screen)."},
        "2472": {"synopsis":"CURSOR_SET_LOWER's block: a count (6), then $F6EE-$F6F3 = 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1."},
        "2479": {"synopsis":"$F6EE-$F6F3 from CURS_LOWER_INIT ($2157 copies a counted block).","comment":"The lower screen's block"},
        "2482": {"comment":"To $F6EE-$F6F3"},
        "2485": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "2488": {"synopsis":"$F6EE-$F6F3 from CURS_UPPER_INIT.","comment":"The upper screen's block"},
        "2491": {"comment":"To $F6EE-$F6F3"},
        "2494": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "2497": {"synopsis":"A character key (KEY_CHAR, codes below $A3): with $EC0D bit 0 set it is ignored (the cursor\nshown again, $0AC2). Otherwise $EC0D bit 7 cleared and bit 3 set (the line changed), the\ncursor off ($0ABC), the character put in at the cursor ($0F54), the cursor one place on\n($0C48), $EC0D bit 7 set again; the cursor stored with its column as the remembered one and\nshown ($0AC8), or, when it could not move, shown where it was ($0AC2).","comment":"HL = $EC0D"},
        "2500": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "2502": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 set?"},
        "2504": {"comment":"Yes: the key ignored, the cursor shown"},
        "2507": {"comment":"Bit 7 cleared, bit 3 set: the line changed"},
        "2509": {"comment":"Bit 3 set"},
        "2511": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "2512": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "2513": {"comment":"The cursor off"},
        "2517": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "2518": {"comment":"The character put in at the cursor"},
        "2522": {"comment":"The cursor one place on"},
        "2526": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 7 set again"},
        "2527": {"comment":"Bit 7 set"},
        "2529": {"comment":"Could not move: shown where it was"},
        "2532": {"comment":"Moved: stored, its column remembered"},
        "2536": {"comment":"Not reached"},
        "2539": {"synopsis":"Key $AA: $EC0D bit 3 set, the cursor off ($0ABC), the character under it taken out ($0FE5),\nthen the cursor shown ($0AC8, the column remembered).","comment":"$EC0D bit 3 set: the line changed"},
        "2542": {"comment":"Bit 3 set"},
        "2544": {"comment":"The cursor off"},
        "2547": {"comment":"The character under it taken out"},
        "2550": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "2551": {"comment":"A = the column, remembered"},
        "2552": {"comment":"Shown there"},
        "2555": {"synopsis":"Key $0C (DELETE): $EC0D bit 0 cleared and bit 3 set, the cursor off ($0ABC), one place back\n($0C2B; at the start nothing more, the cursor shown, $0AC2); the character there taken out\n($0FE5), then the cursor shown ($0AC8, the column remembered).","comment":"HL = $EC0D"},
        "2558": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 cleared, bit 3 set"},
        "2562": {"comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2565": {"comment":"One place back: not possible?"},
        "2569": {"comment":"Then only CURSOR_ON"},
        "2572": {"comment":"LINE_DELETE_CHAR: the character there out"},
        "2575": {"comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "2576": {"comment":"The column remembered"},
        "2577": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2580": {"synopsis":"Key $0D (ENTER), also called from $0705: the cursor off. A row that is empty and is a\nwhole line by itself (flags bits 0 and 3) does nothing. Otherwise, when the line was changed\n($EC0D bit 3), it is entered ($0D5E; nothing more when that returns no carry); then the\ncursor goes to the line's end ($0D1C), one place on ($0C48), a blank row is made there\n($0FA1), and the cursor is stored at its column 0 (CURSOR_PUT).\nExit: carry.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2583": {"comment":"The remembered column kept"},
        "2584": {"comment":"DE = the cursor row's place"},
        "2588": {"comment":"Anything on the row?"},
        "2594": {"comment":"Text: the line entered if changed"},
        "2596": {"comment":"Empty: a line of one row (flags bits 0 and 3)?"},
        "2606": {"synopsis":"Changed ($EC0D bit 3)? Then the line entered ($0D5E)."},
        "2611": {"comment":"Unchanged: on to the next line"},
        "2613": {"comment":"EDIT_LINE_ENTER"},
        "2616": {"comment":"A report: the cursor shown only"},
        "2618": {"synopsis":"The cursor to the line's end ($0D1C), one place on, a blank row there ($0FA1), column 0.","comment":"TO_LINE_END"},
        "2621": {"comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT: one place on"},
        "2624": {"comment":"NEW_BLANK_ROW: a blank row there"},
        "2627": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "2629": {"comment":"A = the remembered column back"},
        "2631": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2634": {"synopsis":"An empty one-row line: only the cursor shown.","comment":"A back"},
        "2636": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "2639": {"synopsis":"Not entered: the cursor shown.","comment":"A back"},
        "2640": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "2643": {"synopsis":"Key $A6: E_PPC = the program's first line (bank 0; ROM 3's FIND_LINE from 0 and LINE_NO);\nthe cursor's colour $0F ($1CA8), the rows rebuilt ($03FF), the cursor shown\n(CURSOR_ON). Not in the Calculator (no carry: a click).\nExit: carry.","comment":"The Calculator: no carry, a click"},
        "2649": {"comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2652": {"comment":"From line 0"},
        "2655": {"comment":"Bank 0 and its stack ($05AC): the program"},
        "2658": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_LINE: HL = the first line"},
        "2661": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_NO: DE = its number"},
        "2664": {"comment":"Back to bank 7 and its stack ($05D1)"},
        "2667": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "2671": {"comment":"The cursor's colour $0F"},
        "2673": {"comment":"$1CA8 sets the cursor's colour"},
        "2676": {"comment":"$03FF: the rows rebuilt"},
        "2679": {"comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "2680": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "2683": {"synopsis":"Key $A5: E_PPC = the line before the first one numbered 9999 or more (FIND_LINE's DE, then\nLINE_NO), normally the program's last; the cursor's colour $0F, the rows rebuilt, the cursor\nshown. Not in the Calculator (no carry: a click).\nExit: carry.","comment":"The Calculator: no carry, a click"},
        "2689": {"comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2692": {"comment":"Line 9999"},
        "2695": {"comment":"Bank 0 and its stack ($05AC): the program"},
        "2698": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_LINE: DE = the line before"},
        "2701": {"comment":"HL = the line before it"},
        "2702": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_NO: DE = its number"},
        "2705": {"comment":"Back to bank 7 and its stack ($05D1)"},
        "2708": {"comment":"E_PPC = it"},
        "2712": {"comment":"The cursor's colour $0F"},
        "2714": {"comment":"$1CA8 sets the cursor's colour"},
        "2717": {"comment":"$03FF: the rows rebuilt"},
        "2720": {"comment":"Carry: no click"},
        "2721": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "2724": {"synopsis":"Key $AF: the cursor off, back to the start of the previous word ($0CBA); stored with the\ncolumn remembered (CURSOR_PUT), or, when it did not move, shown again (CURSOR_ON).","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2727": {"comment":"WORD_LEFT"},
        "2730": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2733": {"comment":"The column remembered: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2737": {"synopsis":"Key $AE: the cursor off, on to the start of the next word ($0CD9); stored (CURSOR_PUT), or,\nwhen it did not move, shown again.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2740": {"comment":"WORD_RIGHT"},
        "2743": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2745": {"comment":"The column remembered: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2748": {"synopsis":"Takes the cursor off the screen: its place (CURSOR_GET), the cell's attribute put back\n($174E).\nExit: C = the row, B = the column, A = the remembered column, HL = $F6F1.","comment":"CURSOR_GET"},
        "2751": {"comment":"$174E: the cell's attribute back"},
        "2754": {"synopsis":"Shows the cursor at its place (CURSOR_GET, then $173F: the cell's attribute kept, the\ncursor's colour put in).\nExit: as CURSOR_GET.","comment":"CURSOR_GET"},
        "2757": {"comment":"$173F: the cursor's colour put in the cell"},
        "2760": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to row C, column B, remembered column A (CURSOR_STORE), sets its colour to\n$0F ($1CA8: ink 7 on paper 1), and shows it ($173F). Keeps AF, BC.","comment":"CURSOR_STORE"},
        "2763": {"comment":"AF and BC kept"},
        "2765": {"comment":"Ink 7 on paper 1"},
        "2767": {"comment":"$1CA8 sets the cursor's colour"},
        "2770": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "2772": {"comment":"$173F: the cursor's colour put in the cell"},
        "2775": {"synopsis":"C = the cursor's row ($F6EE), B = its column ($F6EF), A = the remembered column ($F6F0), the\none up and down movement aim for.\nExit: HL = $F6F1.","comment":"HL = the cursor's row, $F6EE"},
        "2778": {"comment":"C = the row"},
        "2780": {"comment":"B = the column"},
        "2782": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2783": {"comment":"HL = $F6F1"},
        "2785": {"synopsis":"The other way: $F6EE = C, $F6EF = B, $F6F0 = A.\nExit: HL = $F6F0.","comment":"HL = the cursor's row, $F6EE"},
        "2788": {"comment":"The row"},
        "2790": {"comment":"The column"},
        "2792": {"comment":"The remembered column"},
        "2794": {"synopsis":"A = the character at column B of window row C (ROW_ADDRESS); 0 is no character.\nExit: DE = the row. Keeps BC, HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "2795": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "2798": {"comment":"HL = B"},
        "2801": {"comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "2802": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "2805": {"synopsis":"Key $AC (the key table at $05EB): the cursor down ten rows. Each step is ROW_DOWN, the\ncursor kept as\nnear the remembered column ($F6F0) as the row's text allows (COL_PLACE_R) and stored at once\n(the cursor at $F6EE, $0AE1). A row with no text sends it back up one row (ROW_UP); the last\nrow stops it.\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($0AC8); no carry (a click) when it could not go the whole\nway, or did not move at all ($0AC2).","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2808": {"comment":"E = the remembered column, D = 10 rows"},
        "2811": {"synopsis":"One row down."},
        "2812": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "2816": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2818": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2819": {"comment":"Each row's place stored"},
        "2822": {"comment":"Column E placed in the row's text"},
        "2826": {"comment":"No text on the row?"},
        "2828": {"comment":"Ten rows yet?"},
        "2831": {"comment":"Ten rows: done"},
        "2832": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2834": {"synopsis":"A row without text: back up one row, the column placed (COL_PLACE_R); no carry."},
        "2835": {"comment":"ROW_UP: back up one"},
        "2839": {"comment":"Column E"},
        "2840": {"comment":"COL_PLACE_R"},
        "2843": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2844": {"comment":"No carry: a click"},
        "2845": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2847": {"synopsis":"Key $AD (the key table at $05EB): the cursor up ten rows, as ED_KEY_TEN_DOWN in the other\ndirection\n(ROW_UP, COL_PLACE_L). A row with no text sends it back down one row, to the start of that\nrow's text.\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($0AC8); no carry (a click) when it could not go the whole\nway.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2850": {"comment":"E = the remembered column, D = 10 rows"},
        "2853": {"synopsis":"One row up."},
        "2854": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "2858": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2860": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2861": {"comment":"Each row's place stored"},
        "2864": {"comment":"Column E placed in the row's text"},
        "2865": {"comment":"COL_PLACE_L"},
        "2868": {"comment":"No text on the row?"},
        "2870": {"comment":"Ten rows yet?"},
        "2873": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2874": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2877": {"synopsis":"A row without text: back down one row, to the start of its text (TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT from\ncolumn 0).","comment":"The flags (no carry) kept"},
        "2878": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN: back down one"},
        "2881": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "2883": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "2887": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2890": {"synopsis":"Key $A7 (the key table at $05EB): the cursor to the end of its line's text (TO_LINE_END);\nthat column\nbecomes the remembered one.\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2893": {"comment":"TO_LINE_END"},
        "2896": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2899": {"comment":"The new column remembered"},
        "2900": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2903": {"synopsis":"Key $A8 (the key table at $05EB): the cursor to the start of its line's text\n(TO_LINE_START); that\ncolumn becomes the remembered one.\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2906": {"comment":"TO_LINE_START"},
        "2909": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2912": {"comment":"The new column remembered"},
        "2913": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2916": {"synopsis":"Key $0B (the key table at $05EB): the cursor up one row (ROW_UP), as near the remembered\ncolumn ($F6F0)\nas the row's text allows (COL_PLACE_L); the remembered column is kept. A row with no text\nsends the cursor back down, to the column placed there (COL_PLACE_R).\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($0AC8); no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2919": {"comment":"E = the remembered column"},
        "2921": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "2925": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2928": {"comment":"Column E placed (COL_PLACE_L)"},
        "2932": {"comment":"A = the remembered column, kept"},
        "2933": {"comment":"Text: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2936": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "2937": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN: back down"},
        "2940": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "2942": {"comment":"COL_PLACE_R"},
        "2946": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2949": {"synopsis":"Key $0A (the key table at $05EB): the cursor down one row (ROW_DOWN), as near the remembered\ncolumn as\nthe row's text allows (COL_PLACE_L); a row with no text sends it back up (ROW_UP,\nCOL_PLACE_R).\nExit: the cursor stored and shown ($0AC8); no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2952": {"comment":"E = the remembered column"},
        "2954": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "2958": {"comment":"Not moved: CURSOR_ON"},
        "2961": {"comment":"Column E placed (COL_PLACE_L)"},
        "2965": {"comment":"A = the remembered column, kept"},
        "2966": {"comment":"Text: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2970": {"comment":"ROW_UP: back up"},
        "2974": {"comment":"Column E placed (COL_PLACE_R)"},
        "2978": {"comment":"A = the remembered column"},
        "2979": {"comment":"No carry: a click"},
        "2980": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2983": {"synopsis":"Key $08 (the key table at $05EB): the cursor one place left (CURSOR_LEFT); the new column\nbecomes the\nremembered one.\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2986": {"comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "2989": {"comment":"Moved: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "2992": {"comment":"CURSOR_ON"},
        "2995": {"synopsis":"Key $09 (the key table at $05EB): the cursor one place right (CURSOR_RIGHT); the new column\nbecomes the\nremembered one. When that fails after going down a row, the cursor goes back up to the end\nof that row's text (TEXT_END_LEFT from column 31).\nExit: no carry (a click) when it did not move.","comment":"CURSOR_OFF"},
        "2998": {"comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "3001": {"comment":"Moved: CURSOR_PUT"},
        "3004": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "3005": {"comment":"ROW_UP: back up"},
        "3008": {"comment":"From column 31: the end of the row's text"},
        "3010": {"comment":"TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "3013": {"comment":"The flags back"},
        "3014": {"comment":"CURSOR_PUT"},
        "3017": {"synopsis":"Places column B of row C in the row's text: TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT, and TEXT_END_LEFT when that\nfails.\nExit: carry when the row has text (B moved onto or next to it); no carry for a row with\nnone. Keeps DE."},
        "3018": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "3021": {"comment":"Failed: TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "3026": {"synopsis":"As COL_PLACE_R, the other way round: TEXT_END_LEFT first, then TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT.\nExit: carry when the row has text. Keeps DE."},
        "3027": {"comment":"TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "3030": {"comment":"Failed: TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "3035": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor's row C up one:\n1. Leaving the first row of an edited line enters it first (LEAVE_FIRST_ROW); a report there\nstops the move.\n2. Row C, when it holds no text, is removed (REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW).\n3. With C greater than ($F6F1), C goes up one; otherwise the window scrolls down a row\n($053F) and C stays; when it cannot scroll, C goes up unless it is row 0.\nExit: carry when the cursor moved (or the window scrolled); no carry otherwise. Keeps B.","comment":"LEAVE_FIRST_ROW: an edited line entered first"},
        "3038": {"comment":"A report while entering the line: no move"},
        "3041": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3044": {"comment":"Row C empty? Removed"},
        "3053": {"comment":"Above row ($F6F1)?"},
        "3060": {"comment":"The row kept"},
        "3061": {"comment":"The window scrolled down a row"},
        "3065": {"comment":"Scrolled: C stays"},
        "3066": {"comment":"Row 0: no move"},
        "3069": {"synopsis":"C one row up; carry."},
        "3071": {"synopsis":"Done."},
        "3072": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor's row C down one: a row C with no text is removed instead\n(REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW), the rows below moving up into it. Otherwise ROW_DOWN_TEXT.\nExit: carry when the cursor moved (or the window scrolled). Keeps B."},
        "3073": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3076": {"comment":"Row C empty? Removed instead"},
        "3082": {"comment":"Text: on down"},
        "3084": {"comment":"REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW"},
        "3087": {"synopsis":"Leaving the last row of an edited line enters it first (LEAVE_LAST_ROW; a report stops the\nmove). With C less than ($F6F2), C goes down one; otherwise the window scrolls up a row\n($0509) and C stays; when it cannot scroll, C goes down unless it is already row ($F6F3).","comment":"LEAVE_LAST_ROW: an edited line entered first"},
        "3090": {"comment":"A report: no move"},
        "3092": {"comment":"Below row ($F6F2)?"},
        "3100": {"comment":"The row and HL kept"},
        "3102": {"comment":"The window scrolled up a row"},
        "3107": {"comment":"Scrolled: C stays"},
        "3108": {"comment":"Row ($F6F3): no move"},
        "3112": {"synopsis":"C one row down; carry."},
        "3114": {"synopsis":"Done."},
        "3115": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor (row C, column B) one place left within the text: to the column before, or\npast the gaps before it (TEXT_END_LEFT); from column 0 (or with nothing to the left) up a\nrow (ROW_UP), to the end of that row's text.\nExit: carry and A = the new column when it moved; no carry, B = 0 and A as on entry\notherwise.\nChanges: DE.","comment":"D = the remembered column"},
        "3116": {"comment":"Column 0?"},
        "3120": {"comment":"E = the column"},
        "3121": {"comment":"Back to the text"},
        "3124": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "3125": {"comment":"Moved"},
        "3126": {"synopsis":"Nothing to the left on this row: up a row, to the end of its text."},
        "3127": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "3131": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "3132": {"comment":"No row above: no carry"},
        "3133": {"comment":"The end of the row above's text"},
        "3138": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "3139": {"comment":"Moved"},
        "3140": {"comment":"Not moved: A back, B = 0"},
        "3144": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor (row C, column B) one place right within the text (TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT). Past\nthe row's end:\n1. With $EC0D bit 7 clear and row C not continued (flags bit 1), the row is marked as\ncontinued (bit 1 set, bit 3 cleared), the cursor goes down a row (ROW_DOWN) and a blank\nrow flagged as the line's last row is inserted there (INSERT_ROW), the first ($FD6B)\ncolumns of a row then cleared ($16F3); carry and A = column.\n2. Otherwise down a row (ROW_DOWN) to the start of its text.\nExit: carry and A = the new column when it moved.\nChanges: DE.","comment":"D = the remembered column"},
        "3145": {"comment":"One column right"},
        "3146": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "3151": {"comment":"E = the new column"},
        "3152": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT: text there?"},
        "3155": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "3157": {"synopsis":"Past the row's end.","comment":"B back to column 31"},
        "3158": {"comment":"The row and HL kept"},
        "3160": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 7 set?"},
        "3167": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3170": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3175": {"comment":"Row C continued already?"},
        "3179": {"comment":"Now continued, no longer the line's last row"},
        "3183": {"comment":"DE = the row after it"},
        "3188": {"comment":"HL and BC back"},
        "3190": {"comment":"Row C's old flags kept"},
        "3191": {"comment":"Down a row"},
        "3194": {"comment":"A = them"},
        "3195": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3198": {"comment":"DE = the row after it"},
        "3203": {"comment":"Flags: not the first row, the last"},
        "3207": {"comment":"A blank row inserted at row C"},
        "3210": {"comment":"The first ($FD6B) columns of the row at DE cleared"},
        "3213": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "3214": {"comment":"Carry: moved"},
        "3216": {"synopsis":"Down a row, to the start of its text; no carry (A = E, B = 0) when it has none.","comment":"HL and BC back"},
        "3219": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "3223": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "3224": {"comment":"No row below: no carry"},
        "3225": {"comment":"The start of the new row's text"},
        "3227": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "3230": {"comment":"A = the new column"},
        "3231": {"comment":"Text: carry"},
        "3232": {"comment":"None: A = E, B = 0, no carry"},
        "3236": {"synopsis":"TEXT_FROM_COL on window row C: carry when column B is in or just after the row's text, or\ntext follows it (B moved to it). Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3238": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3241": {"comment":"TEXT_FROM_COL"},
        "3244": {"comment":"MOVE_END: DE and HL back"},
        "3247": {"synopsis":"TEXT_BACK_FROM on window row C: carry when column B holds a character, or B moved back to\njust after the last character before it. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3249": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3252": {"comment":"TEXT_BACK_FROM"},
        "3255": {"comment":"MOVE_END: DE and HL back"},
        "3258": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to the start of the word before it: left (CURSOR_LEFT) past any spaces,\nthen on left to the space before the word, then right one place (CURSOR_RIGHT).\nExit: carry when it got there; no carry when it ran out of text. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3260": {"synopsis":"Left past spaces.","comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "3263": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "3265": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "3268": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "3272": {"synopsis":"Left to the space before the word.","comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "3275": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "3277": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "3280": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "3284": {"comment":"Right onto the word's first character"},
        "3287": {"synopsis":"No more text: no carry.","comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "3289": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to the start of the next word: right (CURSOR_RIGHT) to the next space, then\npast the spaces to a character.\nExit: carry when it got there; no carry (one place back left) when no word follows on the\nrow. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3291": {"synopsis":"Right to a space.","comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "3294": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "3296": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "3299": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "3303": {"synopsis":"Right past spaces.","comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "3306": {"comment":"Out of text?"},
        "3308": {"comment":"More text on the row?"},
        "3313": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "3316": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "3320": {"comment":"Carry: at the word"},
        "3321": {"comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "3323": {"synopsis":"No word follows: back one place, no carry.","comment":"CURSOR_LEFT: back one place"},
        "3326": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "3327": {"comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "3329": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor up (ROW_UP) to its line's first row (flags bit 0) and there to the start of\nthe text (TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT from column 0).\nExit: carry when it got there. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3331": {"synopsis":"The line's first row?","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3334": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3338": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "3342": {"comment":"ROW_UP"},
        "3345": {"comment":"Moved: again"},
        "3347": {"comment":"Could not: MOVE_END"},
        "3349": {"synopsis":"First row: the start of its text.","comment":"From column 0"},
        "3351": {"comment":"TEXT_AT_OR_RIGHT"},
        "3354": {"comment":"MOVE_END"},
        "3356": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor down (ROW_DOWN) to its line's last row (flags bit 3) and there to just\nafter the text (TEXT_END_LEFT from column 31).\nExit: carry when it got there. Keeps DE, HL."},
        "3358": {"synopsis":"The line's last row?","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3361": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3365": {"comment":"The line's last row?"},
        "3369": {"comment":"ROW_DOWN"},
        "3372": {"comment":"Moved: again"},
        "3374": {"comment":"Could not: MOVE_END"},
        "3376": {"synopsis":"Last row: the end of its text.","comment":"From column 31"},
        "3378": {"comment":"TEXT_END_LEFT"},
        "3381": {"synopsis":"HL and DE restored.","comment":"HL and DE back"},
        "3384": {"synopsis":"Before the cursor leaves row C downwards: when the line was edited ($EC0D bit 3) and row C\nis its last row (flags bit 3), the line is entered (EDIT_LINE_ENTER).\nExit: carry when the move may go on.","comment":"A = the editor's flags"},
        "3387": {"comment":"The line edited?"},
        "3391": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3394": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3398": {"comment":"Row C its line's last?"},
        "3402": {"comment":"EDIT_LINE_ENTER"},
        "3404": {"synopsis":"As LEAVE_LAST_ROW, upwards: when the line was edited ($EC0D bit 3) and row C is its first\nrow (flags bit 0), the line is entered (EDIT_LINE_ENTER).\nExit: carry when the move may go on.","comment":"A = the editor's flags"},
        "3407": {"comment":"The line edited?"},
        "3411": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3414": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3418": {"comment":"Row C its line's first?"},
        "3422": {"synopsis":"Enters the edited line the cursor is on:\n1. Up from row C to the line's first row (flags bit 0): the reader LINE_ROWS_CHAR is set to\nstart there in state 2 (the window's rows); when the line starts above the window, in\nstate 1 at row 0 (the rows kept above). $EC00-$EC02 (state with bit 7 set, column 0, row)\nand a copy in $EC03-$EC05; $EC06 = 0.\n2. $1432 and $1DFF, then, in bank 0 on its stack ($05AC), the routine at $265D in\nROM 1 through $3E80 (which pages ROM 1 in and calls the address in the word after\nthe CALL); back in bank 7 ($05D1) with interrupts on.\n3. No report (ERR_NR = $FF): $EC0D bit 3 cleared, $175D, $03FF unless in Calculator\nmode ($EC0E = 4), a tone ($07AC), the cursor reloaded; carry.\n4. A report: ENTER_FAILED.\nExit: carry when the cursor may move on.","comment":"State 2: the window's rows"},
        "3424": {"synopsis":"The line's first row?","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3427": {"comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3431": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "3435": {"comment":"Up a row"},
        "3436": {"comment":"Still in the window?"},
        "3439": {"comment":"Above the window: state 1, row 0"},
        "3443": {"synopsis":"The reader's state, column 0 and row, twice.","comment":"HL = the reader, $EC00"},
        "3446": {"comment":"DE = its copy, $EC03"},
        "3449": {"comment":"Bit 7: counting to the cursor"},
        "3451": {"comment":"The state"},
        "3455": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "3461": {"comment":"Row C"},
        "3464": {"comment":"No characters counted yet"},
        "3470": {"comment":"$1432: the expansion reset"},
        "3473": {"comment":"$1DFF: the rows into the edit line"},
        "3476": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "3478": {"comment":"Bank 0 and its stack ($05AC)"},
        "3481": {"comment":"ROM 1's $265D, the word after the CALL"},
        "3486": {"comment":"Back to bank 7 and its stack ($05D1)"},
        "3489": {"comment":"Interrupts on again"},
        "3490": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "3492": {"comment":"A report (ERR_NR not $FF)?"},
        "3498": {"comment":"No report: the line no longer edited"},
        "3503": {"comment":"$175D: the key mode reset"},
        "3506": {"comment":"Calculator mode?"},
        "3511": {"comment":"Not the Calculator: the rows rebuilt ($03FF)"},
        "3514": {"comment":"A tone"},
        "3517": {"comment":"CURSOR_GET: the cursor reloaded"},
        "3520": {"comment":"Carry: entered"},
        "3522": {"synopsis":"A report while the line was entered: the reader set back to the line's start ($EC03-$EC05\ncopied to $EC00-$EC02, bit 7 cleared), BC from $1DFB (or $EC06 when it gives no carry), and\nthe cursor moved by the difference: left (CURSOR_LEFT) $EC06 - BC places, or right\n(CURSOR_RIGHT, $EC0D bit 7 cleared) BC - $EC06 places, each stopping when the cursor cannot\nmove. Then $EC0D bit 7 set, the cursor stored, the cursor's colour $17 (instead of $0F)\ngiven to $1CA8; no carry, so the move does not happen.","comment":"The reader back at the line's start, not counting"},
        "3528": {"comment":"The state, bit 7 cleared"},
        "3534": {"comment":"The column"},
        "3538": {"comment":"The row"},
        "3540": {"comment":"BC = the count from $1DFB"},
        "3543": {"comment":"No carry: BC = $EC06, no move"},
        "3549": {"synopsis":"HL = $EC06 - BC; the cursor reloaded.","comment":"HL = $EC06 - BC"},
        "3555": {"comment":"The subtraction's flags kept"},
        "3557": {"comment":"CURSOR_GET"},
        "3562": {"comment":"BC the larger: right"},
        "3564": {"comment":"Equal: no move"},
        "3566": {"synopsis":"One place left."},
        "3567": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "3568": {"comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "3572": {"comment":"Could not: done"},
        "3574": {"comment":"One place fewer"},
        "3575": {"comment":"None left?"},
        "3579": {"comment":"Done"},
        "3581": {"synopsis":"BC above $EC06: HL = BC - $EC06 places right."},
        "3582": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 7 cleared while moving right"},
        "3588": {"comment":"DE = $EC06 - BC"},
        "3589": {"comment":"HL = BC - $EC06"},
        "3595": {"synopsis":"One place right."},
        "3596": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "3597": {"comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT"},
        "3601": {"comment":"Could not: done"},
        "3603": {"comment":"One place fewer"},
        "3604": {"comment":"None left?"},
        "3608": {"synopsis":"The cursor stored, its colour $17; no carry.","comment":"$EC0D bit 7 set"},
        "3613": {"comment":"CURSOR_STORE"},
        "3616": {"comment":"The cursor's colour $17"},
        "3618": {"comment":"$1CA8 sets the cursor's colour"},
        "3621": {"comment":"No carry: the move not made"},
        "3623": {"synopsis":"Gives the next character of the line being entered, read from the editor's rows (from\n$1F35). The reader's state is $EC00 (low four bits; bit 7 set while characters before the\ncursor are counted), column $EC01 and row $EC02. While bit 7 is set, $EC06 counts each call.\nThe state picks the routine through ROWS_CHAR_TABLE ($216B): 1 the rows kept above\nthe window (ROWS_ABOVE_CHAR), 2 the window's rows (ROWS_SCREEN_CHAR), 4 the rows kept below\nit (ROWS_BELOW_CHAR); each passes over 0s (no character) and returns the next character with\nL = the new state; 8, the line's end, is not in the table and gives $0D.\nExit: A = the character; the column, row and state stored back.","comment":"HL = the reader's state"},
        "3626": {"comment":"Counting to the cursor?"},
        "3630": {"comment":"One more character before the cursor"},
        "3637": {"synopsis":"State, column and row; the state's routine.","comment":"HL = the reader"},
        "3640": {"comment":"A = the state"},
        "3642": {"comment":"B = the column"},
        "3644": {"comment":"C = the row"},
        "3645": {"comment":"The row's address kept"},
        "3646": {"comment":"The state's routine"},
        "3648": {"comment":"HL = ROWS_CHAR_TABLE"},
        "3651": {"comment":"$216B: the state's routine"},
        "3654": {"comment":"E = the new state"},
        "3656": {"comment":"No routine (state 8): $0D"},
        "3660": {"synopsis":"Row, column and the new state stored.","comment":"The row"},
        "3662": {"comment":"The column"},
        "3664": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "3665": {"comment":"The state's low four bits replaced"},
        "3670": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "3672": {"synopsis":"LINE_ROWS_CHAR's table for $216B: a count (3), then for each state its number and\nroutine: 2 ROWS_SCREEN_CHAR, 4 ROWS_BELOW_CHAR, 1 ROWS_ABOVE_CHAR."},
        "3682": {"synopsis":"State 1: the next character from row C of the rows kept above the window ($F9DE,\nROW_ADDRESS_HL through $138A); after their last row on to state 2 at row 0, column 0.\nExit: A = the character, L = 1.","comment":"ABOVE_ROW_ADDR: DE = row C above the window"},
        "3685": {"synopsis":"The next column; 0s passed over.","comment":"ROW_NEXT_CHAR: A = the next character"},
        "3688": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "3690": {"comment":"No character here?"},
        "3694": {"comment":"State 1"},
        "3697": {"synopsis":"The next row; past the last, state 2.","comment":"The next row"},
        "3698": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "3700": {"comment":"Past the rows above? (HL = the word at $F9DB)"},
        "3704": {"comment":"C against the byte at ($F9DB), not the count itself"},
        "3707": {"comment":"State 2 at row 0, column 0"},
        "3711": {"synopsis":"State 2: the next character from window row C (ROW_ADDRESS). Reaching the cursor's place\n($F6EE row, $F6EF column) clears $EC00 bit 7, which stops the count in $EC06. A row that is\nits line's last (flags bit 3) ends the line ($0D, state 8); past row ($F6F3) on to state 4\nat row 1.\nExit: A = the character, L = 2.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "3712": {"comment":"The cursor's row?"},
        "3719": {"comment":"The cursor's column?"},
        "3724": {"comment":"Reached: stop counting"},
        "3729": {"synopsis":"HL back."},
        "3730": {"synopsis":"The next column; 0s passed over.","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3733": {"comment":"ROW_NEXT_CHAR: A = the next character"},
        "3736": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "3738": {"comment":"No character here?"},
        "3742": {"comment":"State 2"},
        "3745": {"synopsis":"The row's end: the line's last row?","comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3749": {"comment":"The line's last row?"},
        "3753": {"comment":"State 8: the line's end"},
        "3758": {"synopsis":"The next row; past row ($F6F3), state 4.","comment":"HL = the window's last row, $F6F3"},
        "3761": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "3762": {"comment":"Past row ($F6F3)?"},
        "3764": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "3768": {"comment":"State 4 at row 1, column 0"},
        "3772": {"synopsis":"State 4: the next character from row C of the rows kept below the window ($F6F8,\nROW_ADDRESS_HL through $1296, rows 1 up to the count in $F6F5). The line's last row (flags\nbit 3), or the last row kept, ends the line ($0D, state 8).\nExit: A = the character, L = 4.","comment":"BELOW_ROW_ADDR: DE = row C below the window"},
        "3775": {"synopsis":"The next column; 0s passed over.","comment":"ROW_NEXT_CHAR: A = the next character"},
        "3778": {"comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "3780": {"comment":"No character here?"},
        "3784": {"comment":"State 4"},
        "3787": {"synopsis":"The row's end: the line's last row?","comment":"HL = its flags"},
        "3791": {"comment":"The line's last row?"},
        "3795": {"comment":"The next row, from column 0"},
        "3798": {"comment":"Past the last row kept?"},
        "3804": {"synopsis":"The line's end: A = $0D, L = 8."},
        "3809": {"synopsis":"A = the character at column B of the row at DE, B moved on; carry. No carry when B is past\ncolumn 31.","comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "3812": {"comment":"No carry when past"},
        "3814": {"comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "3818": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "3819": {"comment":"B moved on"},
        "3820": {"comment":"Carry: one read"},
        "3822": {"synopsis":"Copy lists for $2157 (a count, then the bytes): 1, $14 (EDIT_IN_MAIN), and at $0EF0 1, $01\n(EDIT_IN_LOWER), each put in $EC15."},
        "3824": {"synopsis":"1, $01: EDIT_IN_LOWER's $EC15."},
        "3826": {"synopsis":"Editing in the main screen: TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared and $EC15, the window's last row, = 20\n(ROW_COUNT_MAIN through $2157).","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared"},
        "3831": {"comment":"$EC15 = 20"},
        "3840": {"synopsis":"Editing in the lower screen: TV_FLAG bit 0 set, the print position at row 0, column 0\n($1922), and $EC15, the window's last row, = 1 (ROW_COUNT_LOWER through $2157).","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 set"},
        "3848": {"comment":"Row 0, column 0"},
        "3851": {"comment":"$EC15 = 1"},
        "3860": {"synopsis":"Is column B of the row at DE in or next to text? Carry when the character at B is not 0, or\n(B not 0) the one before it is not 0, or one further right up to column 30 is not 0 (B moved\nto it; A = it).\nExit: no carry, B = 31, when the row is empty from there on.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "3865": {"comment":"A character at B?"},
        "3869": {"comment":"Column 0?"},
        "3873": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "3874": {"comment":"The column before"},
        "3876": {"comment":"A character before B?"},
        "3881": {"synopsis":"A character here?"},
        "3886": {"synopsis":"The next column, up to 30.","comment":"The next column"},
        "3889": {"comment":"Up to column 30"},
        "3894": {"synopsis":"Carry when column B of the row at DE holds a character; otherwise B moves left over 0s to\njust after the last character before it (carry), or to 0 when there is none (no carry).\nChanges: HL.","comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "3899": {"comment":"A character at B?"},
        "3903": {"synopsis":"A 0 here: one column left."},
        "3908": {"comment":"Column 0: none, no carry"},
        "3911": {"comment":"One column left"},
        "3915": {"synopsis":"Just after the character; carry."},
        "3918": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of column B in the row at DE, A = the character there.","comment":"HL = column B's place"},
        "3922": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "3924": {"synopsis":"Inserts character A at the cursor (row C, column B), the rest of the line moving right\nacross its rows; nothing when $EC0D bit 0 is set (no carry).\n1. The character goes in at column B ($057C) and the row is redrawn ($1703).\n2. The character pushed out of column 31, when not 0, goes on to the next row: when row C\nwas its line's last (flags bit 3 or 5 set) a blank row is inserted after it (INSERT_ROW,\nflags as row C's without bit 0, the first ($FD6B) columns cleared by $16F3) and taken at\ncolumn 0; otherwise at the start of the next row's text (TEXT_FROM_COL). Row C's flags\nlose bits 3 and 5 and get bit 1 (continued).\n3. Past the window's last row ($EC15) the character goes to $1241. Keeps BC.","comment":"HL = the editor's flags"},
        "3927": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "3928": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 set: nothing"},
        "3931": {"comment":"The cursor kept"},
        "3932": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "3933": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "3937": {"synopsis":"The character in at column B; the row redrawn.","comment":"In at column B; A = the character pushed out of column 31"},
        "3940": {"comment":"The character pushed out kept"},
        "3941": {"comment":"HL = the row, for $1703"},
        "3942": {"comment":"The row redrawn"},
        "3946": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "3948": {"comment":"Nothing pushed out: done"},
        "3950": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "3951": {"comment":"The next row, from column 0"},
        "3954": {"comment":"Past the window's last row?"},
        "3960": {"comment":"Row C's flags: bits 3 and 5 cleared; Z when they were clear"},
        "3966": {"comment":"A = the flags as they were"},
        "3967": {"comment":"Row C continued"},
        "3969": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "3970": {"comment":"DE = the next row"},
        "3974": {"comment":"Not the line's last row before: already continued"},
        "3976": {"comment":"New row's flags: not the first"},
        "3978": {"comment":"INSERT_ROW: a new row there"},
        "3981": {"comment":"Not inserted: done"},
        "3983": {"comment":"Its first columns cleared"},
        "3986": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "3987": {"comment":"Into the new row"},
        "3989": {"synopsis":"The row already continued: into the next row at its text's start.","comment":"TEXT_FROM_COL: B = where its text starts"},
        "3992": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "3993": {"comment":"Into that row"},
        "3995": {"synopsis":"Past the window's last row: $1241.","comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "3996": {"comment":"Into the rows below"},
        "3999": {"synopsis":"BC back."},
        "4001": {"synopsis":"Inserts a blank row at row C flagged as both the first and the last row of a line ($09,\nINSERT_ROW); DE = row C's address first.","comment":"DE = row C"},
        "4004": {"comment":"Flags: first and last row"},
        "4006": {"synopsis":"Inserts BLANK_ROW at window row C ($0545, the rows from C down moving down) and gives it\nflags A.\nExit: carry when inserted. Keeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC and DE kept"},
        "4008": {"comment":"B = the row"},
        "4009": {"comment":"HL = BLANK_ROW"},
        "4012": {"comment":"C = the flags"},
        "4014": {"comment":"The template inserted at row B"},
        "4018": {"comment":"A = the flags"},
        "4019": {"comment":"Not inserted?"},
        "4021": {"comment":"C = the row"},
        "4022": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "4025": {"comment":"The new row's flags"},
        "4030": {"comment":"Carry: inserted"},
        "4031": {"synopsis":"DE and BC back."},
        "4034": {"synopsis":"A blank editor row for INSERT_ROW: 32 columns of 0 (no character), flags $09 (the line's\nfirst and last row) and two 0 bytes."},
        "4069": {"synopsis":"Deletes the character at the cursor (row C, column B), the rest of the line moving left\nacross its rows:\n1. Down the continued rows (flags bit 1) to the line's last row; when the line runs on past\nthe window's last row ($EC15), $129C gives the character to bring in from below,\notherwise 0 is brought in.\n2. From that row back up to row C each row moves one column left ($0591) from the start of\nits text (from column B on row C), taking the character in at column 31; the character\nmoved out at the left is carried to the row above.\n3. A row other than row C left without text is removed (REMOVE_EMPTY_ROW); the others are\nredrawn ($1703).\nExit: carry. Keeps BC.","comment":"The cursor kept"},
        "4070": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "4073": {"comment":"Its row and column kept"},
        "4074": {"synopsis":"Row C continued (flags bit 1)?"},
        "4078": {"comment":"Row C continued?"},
        "4080": {"comment":"A = 0: nothing to bring in"},
        "4084": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "4085": {"comment":"DE = it, 35 bytes on"},
        "4090": {"comment":"Past the window's last row?"},
        "4096": {"comment":"C = the window's last row"},
        "4097": {"comment":"A = the character from below"},
        "4100": {"synopsis":"H = column B, L = row C of the cursor."},
        "4101": {"synopsis":"One row: its start column (B on the cursor's row, the text's start on the others)."},
        "4102": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "4106": {"comment":"B = the character to bring in"},
        "4107": {"comment":"The cursor's row?"},
        "4110": {"comment":"Z and A kept"},
        "4113": {"comment":"From column B"},
        "4116": {"synopsis":"A later row: from the start of its text.","comment":"Z and A kept"},
        "4118": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "4120": {"comment":"B = the start of the row's text"},
        "4125": {"synopsis":"$F6F4 bit 0 set on the cursor's row (Z on entry), cleared for a later row.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "4126": {"comment":"$F6F4 bit 0 set (the cursor's row)"},
        "4131": {"comment":"A later row: bit 0 cleared"},
        "4135": {"synopsis":"The row moved left, A in at column 31.","comment":"Moved left from B, A in at 31; A = the one moved out"},
        "4138": {"comment":"The character taken out kept"},
        "4144": {"comment":"The cursor's row?"},
        "4148": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "4150": {"comment":"Text left on the row?"},
        "4155": {"comment":"None: the row removed"},
        "4158": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "4162": {"synopsis":"The row redrawn.","comment":"HL = the row, for $1703"},
        "4164": {"comment":"The row redrawn"},
        "4167": {"synopsis":"The row above, with the character moved out.","comment":"A = the character taken out"},
        "4168": {"comment":"Up a row"},
        "4169": {"comment":"It goes into the row above at column 31"},
        "4170": {"comment":"H, L = the cursor's column and row"},
        "4171": {"comment":"Z: this was the cursor's row"},
        "4172": {"comment":"A = the character to bring in"},
        "4173": {"comment":"Until the cursor's row is done"},
        "4176": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "4177": {"comment":"The cursor back"},
        "4179": {"synopsis":"Removes window row C (at DE), which holds no text:\n1. When it is not its line's first row (flags bit 0), the row above (for row 0 the last of\nthe rows kept above the window: $FC9A moved by $141D, row ($F9DB) - 1 through $138A)\nloses flags bit 1 and takes row C's flags.\n2. A row taken from below the window (ROW_FROM_BELOW) and row C removed ($0518: the rows\nbelow it move up, the taken row at the bottom).\nExit: carry.","comment":"HL = row C's flags"},
        "4183": {"comment":"A = them"},
        "4184": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "4188": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "4189": {"comment":"The row kept"},
        "4190": {"comment":"Row 0?"},
        "4194": {"comment":"The row kept again"},
        "4195": {"comment":"The rows kept above: their last row"},
        "4198": {"comment":"$141D: the line before it"},
        "4201": {"comment":"$FC9A = it"},
        "4204": {"comment":"C = the rows kept above, less 1: their last"},
        "4209": {"comment":"ABOVE_ROW_ADDR: DE = that row"},
        "4212": {"comment":"The row back"},
        "4215": {"synopsis":"Row C - 1.","comment":"Row C - 1"},
        "4216": {"comment":"DE = row C - 1"},
        "4219": {"synopsis":"The row above: bit 1 cleared, row C's flags added.","comment":"The row back"},
        "4220": {"comment":"A = row C's flags"},
        "4221": {"comment":"HL = the row above's flags"},
        "4225": {"comment":"Not continued; row C's flags taken"},
        "4229": {"synopsis":"Row C removed, a row from below at the bottom.","comment":"B = the row"},
        "4230": {"comment":"DE = row C"},
        "4233": {"comment":"A row from below at HL"},
        "4236": {"comment":"Row C removed, the rows below up"},
        "4239": {"synopsis":"Key $B4 (the key table at $05EB): deletes left of the cursor: the spaces before it, then the\nword\nbefore them, stopping at the space before the word or at the line's start (AT_LINE_START).\nEach step is CURSOR_LEFT and LINE_DELETE_CHAR; the cursor then goes right past that space.\nThen DEL_KEY_END.","comment":"DEL_KEY_START: the cursor off"},
        "4242": {"synopsis":"At the line's start? Otherwise left one, deleted; a space: again.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "4243": {"comment":"At the line's start?"},
        "4248": {"comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "4251": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4252": {"comment":"Could not: DEL_KEY_END"},
        "4254": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "4257": {"comment":"It kept"},
        "4259": {"comment":"Deleted"},
        "4262": {"comment":"HL and A back"},
        "4264": {"comment":"A space? Again"},
        "4268": {"synopsis":"The word: left one; a space ends it, any other character is deleted.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "4269": {"comment":"AT_LINE_START"},
        "4272": {"comment":"The line's start: done"},
        "4274": {"comment":"CURSOR_LEFT"},
        "4277": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4278": {"comment":"Could not: DEL_KEY_END"},
        "4280": {"comment":"CHAR_AT_ROW_COL: A = the character"},
        "4283": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "4287": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "4288": {"comment":"LINE_DELETE_CHAR"},
        "4291": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "4292": {"comment":"Again"},
        "4294": {"synopsis":"The space before the word: back right past it.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "4295": {"comment":"CURSOR_RIGHT: past the space"},
        "4298": {"synopsis":"HL back."},
        "4299": {"synopsis":"The end of a deleting key: $EEF5 bit 2 cleared and the window's rows 0 to ($EC15) redrawn\n($04D5), $EC0D bit 3 set (the line edited), the cursor stored and shown ($0AC8).\nExit: A = the cursor's column, flags as on entry.","comment":"A = the cursor's column"},
        "4300": {"comment":"Kept, with the flags"},
        "4302": {"comment":"Rows redrawn one at a time again"},
        "4307": {"comment":"A = ($EC15), the window's last row"},
        "4310": {"comment":"The cursor's row and column kept"},
        "4311": {"comment":"B = row 0, C = the last row"},
        "4314": {"comment":"Z: $04D5 only draws, the cursor is not moved"},
        "4315": {"comment":"Rows 0 to ($EC15) redrawn"},
        "4319": {"comment":"The line edited"},
        "4325": {"comment":"The cursor stored and shown"},
        "4328": {"comment":"A = the cursor's column, the flags as on entry"},
        "4330": {"synopsis":"Key $B3 (the key table at $05EB): deletes at the cursor (LINE_DELETE_CHAR) up to and\nincluding the next\nspace, then the spaces after it; stops at the line's end (a 0 at the cursor). Then\nDEL_KEY_END with carry.","comment":"DEL_KEY_START: the cursor off, row redraws held back"},
        "4333": {"synopsis":"A character at the cursor? Deleted; on to the first space.","comment":"A = the character at the cursor (CHAR_AT_ROW_COL)"},
        "4338": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "4340": {"comment":"Carry for DEL_KEY_END"},
        "4343": {"comment":"It is deleted (LINE_DELETE_CHAR); A kept for the test"},
        "4350": {"comment":"Not a space: on"},
        "4354": {"synopsis":"Spaces after it deleted.","comment":"A = the character now at the cursor"},
        "4357": {"comment":"Not a space: done"},
        "4362": {"comment":"The space deleted (LINE_DELETE_CHAR)"},
        "4367": {"comment":"On to the next character"},
        "4369": {"synopsis":"Key $B1 (the key table at $05EB): deletes everything before the cursor back to the start of\nits line:\non the line's later rows a place left (CURSOR_LEFT) and deleted at a time\n(LINE_DELETE_CHAR); on its first row the character before the cursor while column B is not 0\nand the character before it is not 0. Then DEL_KEY_END with carry.","comment":"DEL_KEY_START: the cursor off, row redraws held back"},
        "4372": {"synopsis":"The line's first row?","comment":"DE = the cursor's row (ROW_ADDRESS)"},
        "4376": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "4380": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "4384": {"comment":"One place left (CURSOR_LEFT)"},
        "4387": {"comment":"Could not move: done"},
        "4389": {"comment":"The character there deleted (LINE_DELETE_CHAR)"},
        "4393": {"comment":"Again, from the row test"},
        "4395": {"comment":"Not reached: the jump at $1129 goes to $1114"},
        "4396": {"synopsis":"First row: the characters before the cursor, back to the text's start."},
        "4397": {"comment":"Column 0?"},
        "4401": {"comment":"A = the character before the cursor (CHAR_AT_ROW_COL)"},
        "4406": {"comment":"A character before the cursor?"},
        "4410": {"comment":"One column back, and that character deleted"},
        "4414": {"comment":"Again"},
        "4416": {"synopsis":"HL back; carry; DEL_KEY_END."},
        "4417": {"synopsis":"Carry; DEL_KEY_END."},
        "4418": {"comment":"DEL_KEY_END: the window redrawn, the cursor shown"},
        "4421": {"synopsis":"Key $B0 (the key table at $05EB): deletes at the cursor (LINE_DELETE_CHAR) until a 0 is at\nthe cursor:\nthe rest of the line. Then DEL_KEY_END with carry.","comment":"DEL_KEY_START: the cursor off, row redraws held back"},
        "4424": {"synopsis":"A character at the cursor?","comment":"A = the character at the cursor (CHAR_AT_ROW_COL)"},
        "4427": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "4429": {"comment":"Carry for DEL_KEY_END"},
        "4432": {"comment":"It is deleted (LINE_DELETE_CHAR)"},
        "4437": {"comment":"Again"},
        "4439": {"synopsis":"The start of a deleting key: $EC0D bit 0 cleared, the cursor loaded and taken off the screen\n($0ABC), $EEF5 bit 2 set (rows are not redrawn one at a time while it is: $1703), HL =\n$F6F1."},
        "4442": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 cleared"},
        "4444": {"comment":"The cursor loaded, taken off"},
        "4450": {"comment":"No redraws one row at a time"},
        "4456": {"synopsis":"Is the cursor (row C, column B) at the start of its line's text? Z when row C is the line's\nfirst row (flags bit 0) and B is 0 or the character before column B is 0; otherwise NZ, A =\n1.","comment":"DE = row C (ROW_ADDRESS)"},
        "4459": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags byte"},
        "4463": {"comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "4470": {"comment":"Column 0?"},
        "4472": {"comment":"A = the character before column B (CHAR_AT_ROW_COL)"},
        "4479": {"comment":"A character before the cursor?"},
        "4481": {"synopsis":"NZ.","comment":"A = 1 and NZ: not at the start"},
        "4485": {"synopsis":"Z.","comment":"A = 0 and Z: at the start"},
        "4487": {"synopsis":"DE = the address of row C of the editor's window, the rows from $EC16, 35 bytes each: 32\ncolumns of characters (0 is no character), at +$20 the row's flags (bit 0 the line's first\nrow, bit 1 continued on the next row, bit 3 the line's last row), and two bytes at +$21 and\n+$22.\nExit: HL = $0023. Keeps AF, BC.","comment":"HL = the window's first row"},
        "4490": {"synopsis":"DE = HL + 35 * C: row C of the rows from HL ($1296 for $F6F8, $138A for $F9DE).\nExit: HL = $0023. Keeps AF, BC.","comment":"AF kept"},
        "4491": {"comment":"A = the rows to step over"},
        "4492": {"comment":"DE = 35, the size of a row"},
        "4495": {"synopsis":"35 for each row.","comment":"Row 0 reached?"},
        "4498": {"comment":"One row on"},
        "4500": {"comment":"One fewer to go"},
        "4502": {"synopsis":"DE = the row.","comment":"DE = the row, HL = 35"},
        "4505": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of column B of window row C (ROW_ADDRESS). Keeps DE."},
        "4506": {"comment":"DE = row C (ROW_ADDRESS)"},
        "4509": {"comment":"HL = DE + B: the cell at column B"},
        "4515": {"synopsis":"A copy list for $2157 (a count, then the bytes): 5, then $00, $00, $00, $F8, $F6 for\n$F6F5-$F6F9 (BELOW_RESET)."},
        "4521": {"synopsis":"$F6F5-$F6F7 = 0 (no rows kept below the window) and $F6F8-$F6F9 = $F6F8 (BELOW_INIT_DATA\nthrough $2157).","comment":"HL = BELOW_INIT_DATA, the list"},
        "4524": {"comment":"DE = $F6F5, where it goes"},
        "4527": {"comment":"$2157 copies it"},
        "4530": {"synopsis":"Takes the next row from those kept below the window: with $F6F5 (their count) not 0, $EC0D\nbit 0 cleared and the 20 rows from $F6F8 + 35 moved down one row, so the first lands at\n$F6F8; with none kept, $1432, $1425 (on $F9D7, updated when it gives carry) and $13A9\nmake them first. $F6F5 = the count less one.\nExit: HL = $F6F8. Keeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4532": {"comment":"HL = $F6F5, the count, kept for the end"},
        "4536": {"comment":"Rows kept below?"},
        "4541": {"comment":"None: made"},
        "4544": {"comment":"HL = $F9D7, the line number to start from"},
        "4550": {"comment":"No line after it: $F9D7 kept"},
        "4552": {"comment":"$F9D7 = the line found"},
        "4555": {"synopsis":"BC = the place; $13A9 on $F6F5.","comment":"BC = the line's number, for LINE_TO_ROWS"},
        "4557": {"comment":"HL = $F6F5"},
        "4558": {"comment":"LINE_TO_ROWS: the line's rows from $F6F8; A = the rows"},
        "4561": {"comment":"All but the one taken are kept"},
        "4562": {"comment":"To store the count"},
        "4564": {"synopsis":"Rows kept: shifted down one."},
        "4567": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 cleared"},
        "4569": {"comment":"DE = $F6F8, HL = $F6F8 + 35"},
        "4578": {"comment":"20 rows down one"},
        "4583": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "4584": {"comment":"Carry: a row given"},
        "4585": {"synopsis":"The count stored; HL = $F6F8.","comment":"DE = $F6F5"},
        "4586": {"comment":"The count stored"},
        "4587": {"comment":"HL = the row taken: the first, at $F6F8"},
        "4593": {"synopsis":"Puts the editor row at DE (35 bytes: 32 cells, flags at +$20, line number at +$21, high byte\nfirst) in front of the rows kept below the screen ($F6F5 the count, the rows from $F6F8, 35\nbytes each, row 1 the nearest):\n1. When the row's flags have bits 0 and 4 set, $F9D7 = the number of the line before the\nrow's line ($141D; kept when there is none).\n2. When bit 0 is set, the buffer is emptied (count 0) and the row is not kept.\n3. Otherwise, with fewer than 20 rows ($14), the row is copied to $F6F8 and rows 0-19 moved\nto rows 1-20, so it becomes row 1; the count goes up by one.\nExit: HL = $F6F8; carry when the row was kept or the buffer emptied, no carry when the\nbuffer was full.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4595": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags"},
        "4599": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 4 both set?"},
        "4605": {"comment":"HL, DE kept"},
        "4607": {"comment":"DE = the row's line number"},
        "4612": {"comment":"Expansion reset"},
        "4616": {"comment":"The line before it"},
        "4621": {"comment":"Kept as $F9D7"},
        "4624": {"synopsis":"No line before: $F9D7 kept."},
        "4626": {"synopsis":"A line's first row (bit 0) empties the buffer.","comment":"The line's first row?"},
        "4628": {"comment":"HL = $F6F5, the count, kept for the end"},
        "4632": {"comment":"Not a first row: the row put in front"},
        "4634": {"comment":"Count 0"},
        "4637": {"comment":"To store the count"},
        "4639": {"synopsis":"The row put in front, when there is room.","comment":"A = the count"},
        "4640": {"comment":"20 rows already?"},
        "4644": {"comment":"The row copied to $F6F8"},
        "4653": {"comment":"Rows 0-19 moved one row on, from the end"},
        "4656": {"comment":"DE = the end of the rows, HL = 35 bytes before it"},
        "4664": {"comment":"20 rows, from the last byte back"},
        "4669": {"comment":"One more"},
        "4671": {"comment":"To store the count"},
        "4673": {"synopsis":"Carries character A, pushed off the end of the screen's last row (HL = that row's flags\nbyte), into the rows below the screen ($F6F5):\n1. B = column 0, C = row 1 (BELOW_ROW_ADDR). When the screen row's bit 3 was set, it is\ncleared and the row after it is found as in step 3.\n2. The character is put in at the row's first used column ($0F14 moves B over empty cells;\n$057C inserts it, pushing the row's cells on). When nothing is pushed off the row's end,\nthe count becomes C and the row's bit 3 is set: done.\n3. The cell pushed off goes on to the next row (C + 1; at row 21, with a character in the\nprevious row's last cell, $EC0D bit 0 is set). The previous row gets bit 1 set and bit 3\ncleared; when its bit 1 was already set the next row is used as it is (step 2), otherwise\nrow C is made a new last row: cleared, flags 8, indented by $FD6B cells ($16F3).\nKeeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC, DE and the character kept"},
        "4676": {"comment":"Column 0, row 1"},
        "4680": {"comment":"DE = row 1 below the screen (BELOW_ROW_ADDR)"},
        "4685": {"comment":"The screen row was a line's last?"},
        "4691": {"synopsis":"B moved over the row's empty cells ($0F14).","comment":"B = the row's first column of text (TEXT_FROM_COL)"},
        "4694": {"comment":"A = the character carried"},
        "4695": {"synopsis":"A inserted at column B of row DE ($057C).","comment":"It goes in at column B ($057C); A = the one pushed out"},
        "4698": {"comment":"Nothing pushed off?"},
        "4700": {"comment":"The character pushed out kept"},
        "4701": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "4704": {"comment":"Past row 20?"},
        "4707": {"comment":"Within 20: on to the next row"},
        "4709": {"comment":"The last cell of the row before used?"},
        "4714": {"comment":"That cell empty: on to the next row"},
        "4717": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 set"},
        "4723": {"synopsis":"The row before marked as continued (bit 1 set, bit 3 cleared); DE = row C.","comment":"Was the row before already continued?"},
        "4729": {"comment":"DE = row C below the screen (BELOW_ROW_ADDR)"},
        "4732": {"comment":"Yes: its next row exists"},
        "4734": {"comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4736": {"comment":"A new row: cleared, flags 8 (bit 3)"},
        "4743": {"comment":"Indented"},
        "4746": {"comment":"A = the character pushed out"},
        "4747": {"comment":"It goes into the new row"},
        "4749": {"synopsis":"Nothing more pushed off: the count = C, bit 3 on row C's flags.","comment":"A = the rows used"},
        "4750": {"comment":"The count of rows kept below"},
        "4753": {"comment":"Row C is now the line's last"},
        "4758": {"synopsis":"DE = row C of the rows below the screen: $F6F8 + 35 x C ($118A).\nExit: HL = $0023. Keeps AF.","comment":"HL = the first row below the screen"},
        "4761": {"comment":"ROW_ADDRESS_HL does the rest"},
        "4764": {"synopsis":"Pulls the rows below the screen one character back, from the last row ($F6F5) up to row 1:\nin each row the character at its first used column is taken out and the one from the row\nbelow put in at column 31 ($0591). A row left with no text is dropped: the row before (the\nscreen's last row, line $EC15, for row 1) loses bit 1 and takes the dropped row's flags, and\nthe count goes down by one. $EC0D bit 0 is cleared first.\nExit: carry, A = the character taken from row 1 (0 when none); with no rows kept, A = 0 and\nno carry.\nKeeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4766": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 0 cleared"},
        "4771": {"comment":"C = the count"},
        "4775": {"comment":"No rows kept below?"},
        "4776": {"comment":"A = 0, the character for the last row"},
        "4780": {"synopsis":"Row C: DE = its address; its first used column found ($0F14).","comment":"DE = row C below the screen (BELOW_ROW_ADDR)"},
        "4783": {"comment":"The incoming character kept"},
        "4784": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "4786": {"comment":"No text in the row?"},
        "4791": {"comment":"A = the character for column 31"},
        "4792": {"comment":"A in at column 31, the cell at B taken out"},
        "4795": {"comment":"The character taken out kept, for the row above"},
        "4797": {"comment":"Any text left in the row?"},
        "4803": {"comment":"Text left: on to the row above"},
        "4805": {"synopsis":"An empty row: A = its flags, for the row before.","comment":"HL = the row's flags byte, past column 31"},
        "4807": {"comment":"The flags and BC kept"},
        "4809": {"comment":"Row 1?"},
        "4814": {"comment":"The row before: the screen's last row"},
        "4818": {"comment":"DE = the screen's last row (ROW_ADDRESS)"},
        "4823": {"synopsis":"The row before: row C - 1 of the buffer.","comment":"Row C - 1 of the rows below"},
        "4824": {"comment":"DE = that row (BELOW_ROW_ADDR)"},
        "4827": {"synopsis":"The row before: bit 1 cleared, the dropped row's flags added; the count one less.","comment":"BC and the dropped row's flags back"},
        "4829": {"comment":"HL = the row before's flags byte"},
        "4833": {"comment":"Not continued on the next row now"},
        "4835": {"comment":"The dropped row's flags added to it"},
        "4837": {"comment":"One row fewer kept below"},
        "4841": {"synopsis":"The row above, until row 1 is done.","comment":"A = the character taken out, for the row above"},
        "4842": {"comment":"The row above"},
        "4845": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "4846": {"synopsis":"Done."},
        "4849": {"synopsis":"ABOVE_INIT's bytes for $2157: a count (3), then $00 for $F9DB and $F9DE for $F9DC."},
        "4853": {"synopsis":"Empties the stack of rows above the screen: $F9DB (the count) = 0 and $F9DC (the pointer\npast the top row) = $F9DE, copied from ABOVE_INIT_DATA through $2157.","comment":"HL = ABOVE_INIT_DATA, the list"},
        "4856": {"comment":"DE = $F9DB, where it goes"},
        "4859": {"comment":"$2157 copies it"},
        "4862": {"synopsis":"Takes the row nearest the screen off the stack of rows above it ($F9DB the count, $F9DC the\npointer past the top row, rows 35 bytes each from $F9DE):\n1. With rows on the stack, the pointer moves back 35 bytes and the count goes down by one:\nHL = that row.\n2. With none, the line before $FC9A ($141D, after $1432) is expanded into rows\nfrom $F9E1 (LINE_TO_ROWS) and $FC9A becomes its number. All its rows but the last stay on\nthe stack (count = rows - 1, pointer = the last row's address); HL = the last row.\nExit: carry and HL = the row; no carry when the stack was empty and there is no line before\n$FC9A.\nKeeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4864": {"comment":"HL = $F9DB, the count, kept for the end"},
        "4868": {"comment":"Rows on the stack?"},
        "4872": {"comment":"HL kept again"},
        "4873": {"comment":"$1432: the expansion reset"},
        "4876": {"comment":"The line before $FC9A"},
        "4884": {"comment":"Found: it is $FC9A now"},
        "4887": {"synopsis":"BC = the line found (or 0).","comment":"BC = the line's number, for LINE_TO_ROWS"},
        "4889": {"comment":"HL = $F9DB"},
        "4890": {"comment":"HL = $F9DE"},
        "4893": {"comment":"No line before: the pointer = $F9DE, the count kept"},
        "4895": {"comment":"Its rows from $F9E1"},
        "4898": {"comment":"All but the last kept"},
        "4899": {"comment":"HL = the line's last row: the one taken"},
        "4902": {"synopsis":"A row off the stack: the pointer back by 35 bytes.","comment":"HL = the pointer past the top row"},
        "4905": {"comment":"Back 35 bytes: HL = the row taken"},
        "4910": {"comment":"Carry: the count is stored"},
        "4911": {"comment":"One row fewer"},
        "4912": {"synopsis":"With carry: the count = A and the pointer = DE.\nExit: HL = DE.","comment":"DE = the new pointer"},
        "4913": {"comment":"HL = $F9DB"},
        "4914": {"comment":"No carry: the count left as it is"},
        "4916": {"comment":"The count"},
        "4917": {"synopsis":"The pointer = DE.","comment":"The pointer, at $F9DC"},
        "4921": {"comment":"HL = the row"},
        "4925": {"synopsis":"Puts the editor row at DE on the stack of rows above the screen ($F9DB):\n1. When the row's flags have bits 0 and 4 set, $FC9A = the row's line number.\n2. When bit 3 is set (the line's last row), the stack is emptied (count 0, pointer $F9DE)\nand $FC9A moves to the line after it ($1425, after $1432; 0 when none): the\nrow is not kept.\n3. Otherwise, with fewer than 20 rows ($14), the row is copied to the pointer, which moves\non 35 bytes, and the count goes up by one.\nExit: carry when the row was kept or the stack emptied; no carry when it was full.\nKeeps BC, DE.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "4927": {"comment":"HL = the row's flags"},
        "4931": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 4 both set?"},
        "4937": {"comment":"DE, HL kept"},
        "4943": {"comment":"$FC9A = the row's line number"},
        "4949": {"synopsis":"A line's last row (bit 3) empties the stack.","comment":"The line's last row?"},
        "4951": {"comment":"HL = $F9DB, kept for the end"},
        "4955": {"comment":"Not a last row: the row pushed"},
        "4957": {"comment":"HL kept again"},
        "4958": {"comment":"$1432: the expansion reset"},
        "4961": {"comment":"The line after $FC9A, or 0"},
        "4967": {"comment":"$FC9A = it"},
        "4970": {"comment":"HL = $F9DE"},
        "4974": {"comment":"Count 0, pointer $F9DE"},
        "4977": {"comment":"To store them"},
        "4979": {"synopsis":"The row copied on top, when there is room.","comment":"A = the count"},
        "4980": {"comment":"20 rows already?"},
        "4982": {"comment":"Full: the row not kept"},
        "4984": {"comment":"One more"},
        "4985": {"comment":"HL = the pointer: where the row goes"},
        "4991": {"comment":"The row copied on top"},
        "4994": {"comment":"DE = the new pointer"},
        "4995": {"comment":"Carry: the count and the pointer stored"},
        "4998": {"synopsis":"Full: the row is not kept."},
        "5002": {"synopsis":"DE = row C of the stack above the screen: $F9DE + 35 x C ($118A).\nExit: HL = $0023. Keeps AF.","comment":"HL = the stack's first row"},
        "5005": {"comment":"ROW_ADDRESS_HL does the rest"},
        "5008": {"synopsis":"LINE_TO_ROWS's table for $216B: a count (8), then a code and a routine for each:\n$0D $16CB, $01 $16D9, and $12, $13, $14, $15, $10, $11 $142D."},
        "5033": {"synopsis":"Writes the text of a program line into editor rows from HL + 3, the expansion being set up\nfor it ($152F or $15B5):\n1. The first row: its flags (+$20) = 1, its line number (+$21, high byte first) = BC; B =\ncolumn 0, C = 1 row.\n2. Each character from $1616 (none in Calculator mode, $EC0E = 4) is looked up in\nEXPAND_CODES: the colour codes $10-$15 lose their argument; $0D ends the line\n($16CB).\n3. Any other character goes in at column B ($16C4). In a full row (column 32) $1404\nends it with flags XOR $12 and starts the next, indented by $FD6B cells ($16F3);\nwith 20 rows written the line is ended there instead, with $0D.\n4. When the text runs out, the line is ended with $0D, or with $01 ($16D9) when\nnothing at all was written.\nExit: HL = the first row, A = C = the number of rows, carry, DE = the last row.","comment":"DE = the first row"},
        "5038": {"comment":"The first row kept, for the exit"},
        "5039": {"comment":"Flags 1; the line number"},
        "5049": {"comment":"Row 1, column 0"},
        "5053": {"synopsis":"The next character, unless in Calculator mode.","comment":"BC, DE kept"},
        "5055": {"comment":"Calculator mode?"},
        "5060": {"comment":"No: A = the line's next character ($1616)"},
        "5065": {"comment":"Got one?"},
        "5067": {"comment":"None: $0D, or $01 for an empty first row"},
        "5074": {"comment":"Still column 0?"},
        "5080": {"comment":"No: $0D"},
        "5082": {"synopsis":"The character looked up in EXPAND_CODES.","comment":"HL = EXPAND_CODES"},
        "5085": {"comment":"Its routine run, if A is a code ($216B)"},
        "5088": {"comment":"Line ended?"},
        "5090": {"comment":"Argument skipped?"},
        "5092": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "5093": {"comment":"Room in the row?"},
        "5096": {"comment":"Yes: it goes in"},
        "5098": {"comment":"A new row, flags XOR $12"},
        "5100": {"comment":"$1404: this row ended, the next started"},
        "5103": {"comment":"Got a row: indented"},
        "5105": {"comment":"No room: the line ends"},
        "5110": {"synopsis":"The new row indented.","comment":"$16F3: the line's later rows start indented"},
        "5113": {"synopsis":"The character in at column B.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "5114": {"comment":"$16C4: in at column B, B + 1"},
        "5117": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "5119": {"synopsis":"HL = the first row, A = the rows.","comment":"HL = the first row"},
        "5120": {"comment":"A = the rows written"},
        "5122": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "5124": {"synopsis":"Ends row DE (ROW_CLEAR_REST) with its flags XOR A and starts the next: C + 1, DE + 35, its\nflags 0.\nExit: carry; no carry (and nothing changed after the flags) when C was 20 or more.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "5125": {"comment":"ROW_CLEAR_REST: the row's rest cleared, HL = its flags"},
        "5128": {"comment":"The flags XOR A"},
        "5131": {"comment":"20 rows already?"},
        "5134": {"comment":"Yes: no carry, no new row"},
        "5135": {"comment":"One row more"},
        "5136": {"comment":"DE = the next row, 35 bytes on"},
        "5141": {"comment":"Its flags byte 0"},
        "5147": {"comment":"Carry: a new row"},
        "5149": {"synopsis":"PREV_LINE_START for the line before line HL.\nExit: carry and HL = its number, the expansion set up; no carry and HL = 0 when there is\nnone.","comment":"PREV_LINE_START"},
        "5152": {"comment":"Found: carry, HL = its number"},
        "5153": {"comment":"None: HL = 0"},
        "5157": {"synopsis":"NEXT_LINE_START for the line after line HL (the first line for HL = 0).\nExit: carry and HL = its number, the expansion set up; no carry and HL = 0 when there is\nnone.","comment":"NEXT_LINE_START"},
        "5160": {"comment":"Found: carry, HL = its number"},
        "5161": {"comment":"None: HL = 0"},
        "5165": {"synopsis":"EXPAND_CODES' routine for the colour codes $10-$15 (the word table at $1390): the argument\nafter the code read (EXPAND_NEXT) and dropped.\nExit: no carry, so LINE_TO_ROWS goes on; with nothing left, EXPAND_INIT and carry.","comment":"The argument (EXPAND_NEXT)"},
        "5168": {"comment":"Got one: no carry, LINE_TO_ROWS goes on"},
        "5170": {"synopsis":"Resets the expansion of a line ($FC9F, the place in the program, and $FCA1, the place in a\ntext, both 0) and copies the 232 bytes $1447-$152E (KEYWORD_TEXT to WORD_FIND_END) to $FCAE\nin\nbank 7, where EXPAND_NEXT and the tokenizer call them: KEYWORD_TEXT runs at $FCAE,\nWORD_TO_BUFFER at $FD09, KEYWORD_FIND at $FD43, WORD_FIND at $FD5C.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"No place in the program"},
        "5176": {"comment":"No text pending"},
        "5179": {"comment":"KEYWORD_TEXT and the rest, 232 bytes, to $FCAE"},
        "5191": {"synopsis":"Run at $FCAE: puts the text of keyword $A5 + A in the buffer at $FCA3 (WORD_TO_BUFFER).\nInterrupts off, ROM 3 and bank 7 paged in (port $7FFD = $17, port $1FFD = $5B67 with bit 2\nset); the search starts from the entry of ROM 3's KEYWORD_TABLE for $A5, $B5, $C5, $D5, $E5\nor\n$F5 ($0096, $00CF, $0100, $013E, $018B, $01D4) below A, then passes over the rest of A's\nstrings (each ends with bit 7 set).\nEntry: A = the keyword's code - $A5.","comment":"Interrupts off; A kept"},
        "5193": {"comment":"Bank 7, the ROM's low bit set"},
        "5200": {"comment":"The ROM's high bit set too: ROM 3"},
        "5210": {"comment":"A = the keyword's place after $A5"},
        "5211": {"comment":"Keyword $F5 or above?"},
        "5215": {"comment":"$E5-$F4?"},
        "5219": {"comment":"$D5-$E4?"},
        "5223": {"comment":"$C5-$D4?"},
        "5227": {"comment":"$B5-$C4?"},
        "5231": {"comment":"$A5-$B4: from RND's entry in ROM 3's KEYWORD_TABLE"},
        "5236": {"synopsis":"Keywords $B5-$C4.","comment":"A = the keyword's place after $B5"},
        "5238": {"comment":"HL = ROM 3's entry for keyword $B5"},
        "5243": {"synopsis":"Keywords $C5-$D4.","comment":"A = the keyword's place after $C5"},
        "5245": {"comment":"HL = ROM 3's entry for keyword $C5"},
        "5250": {"synopsis":"Keywords $D5-$E4.","comment":"A = the keyword's place after $D5"},
        "5252": {"comment":"HL = ROM 3's entry for keyword $D5"},
        "5257": {"synopsis":"Keywords $E5-$F4.","comment":"A = the keyword's place after $E5"},
        "5259": {"comment":"HL = ROM 3's entry for keyword $E5"},
        "5264": {"synopsis":"Keywords $F5-$FF.","comment":"A = the keyword's place after $F5"},
        "5266": {"comment":"HL = ROM 3's entry for keyword $F5"},
        "5269": {"synopsis":"B = the strings to pass over.","comment":"B = the strings to pass over"},
        "5270": {"comment":"None to pass over?"},
        "5271": {"synopsis":"Any more to pass over?"},
        "5273": {"synopsis":"Up to the end of this string (bit 7).","comment":"A = the next byte of the string"},
        "5275": {"comment":"Bit 7: the string's last?"},
        "5279": {"comment":"One string fewer"},
        "5280": {"comment":"Any more?"},
        "5282": {"synopsis":"Run at $FD09 (and the end of KEYWORD_TEXT at $FCAE): copies the string at HL (ended by bit\n7)\nto $FCA3 for EXPAND_NEXT, $FCA1 = $FCA3. A space goes first unless $FC9E is not 0 ($FC9E is\ncleared); the last character loses bit 7 and $A0 (a space with bit 7) follows it. Then the\npaging from $5B5C and $5B67 is put back and interrupts are allowed again.\nExit: HL past the string.","comment":"DE = the buffer at $FCA3, and $FCA1 = it"},
        "5289": {"comment":"No space wanted ($FC9E not 0)?"},
        "5293": {"comment":"$FC9E = 0, the flags kept for the test"},
        "5298": {"comment":"Not 0: no space"},
        "5300": {"comment":"The leading space"},
        "5304": {"synopsis":"One character, up to the one with bit 7.","comment":"A = B = the next character"},
        "5307": {"comment":"To the buffer"},
        "5309": {"comment":"Bit 7: the last?"},
        "5313": {"comment":"The last without bit 7"},
        "5316": {"comment":"Over the last again"},
        "5319": {"comment":"Then $A0, a space with bit 7, ends the text"},
        "5322": {"comment":"The paging as it was: port $7FFD from $5B5C"},
        "5330": {"comment":"Port $1FFD from $5B67"},
        "5338": {"comment":"Interrupts allowed again"},
        "5340": {"synopsis":"Run at $FD43: looks the word at $FDA0 up in ROM 3's KEYWORD_TABLE from RND's entry ($0096;\nB = $A5, the code of its first keyword), with ROM 3 and bank 7 paged in and interrupts off;\nWORD_FIND does the rest.","comment":"Interrupts off; A kept"},
        "5342": {"comment":"Bank 7, the ROM's low bit set"},
        "5349": {"comment":"The ROM's high bit set too: ROM 3"},
        "5360": {"comment":"HL = RND's entry in ROM 3's KEYWORD_TABLE"},
        "5363": {"comment":"B = $A5, the code of the first keyword"},
        "5365": {"synopsis":"Run at $FD5C (and the end of KEYWORD_FIND): compares the word at $FDA0 (its last character\nwith bit 7 set) with each string at HL, B counting up from the code of the first, until B\npasses $FF. Lower-case letters in the word match capitals. Then the paging from $5B5C and\n$5B67 is put back and interrupts are allowed again.\nEntry: HL = the first string, B = its code.\nExit: carry and A = the code of the string that matched; no carry when none did.","comment":"DE = the word at $FDA0, for each string"},
        "5368": {"synopsis":"The word's next character, a letter as a capital.","comment":"A = the word's next character"},
        "5371": {"comment":"A lower-case letter?"},
        "5373": {"comment":"A again, bit 7 included"},
        "5374": {"comment":"Not lower case: as it is"},
        "5376": {"comment":"Made a capital"},
        "5378": {"synopsis":"The same as the string's?","comment":"The same as the string's?"},
        "5379": {"comment":"No: the next string"},
        "5381": {"comment":"Both on one character"},
        "5383": {"comment":"The last character?"},
        "5387": {"comment":"Carry: found"},
        "5388": {"comment":"Then A = the code, paging back"},
        "5390": {"synopsis":"No match: the next string's code; past $FF, none found.","comment":"The next string's code"},
        "5391": {"comment":"Past $FF: none found"},
        "5393": {"synopsis":"Past the end of this string.","comment":"Bit 7: the string's last?"},
        "5399": {"comment":"The word compared with the next string"},
        "5401": {"synopsis":"None found: no carry.","comment":"No carry"},
        "5402": {"synopsis":"A = B; the paging as it was.","comment":"D = the code found"},
        "5404": {"comment":"The paging as it was: port $7FFD from $5B5C"},
        "5412": {"comment":"Port $1FFD from $5B67"},
        "5420": {"comment":"A = the code"},
        "5421": {"comment":"Interrupts allowed again"},
        "5423": {"synopsis":"Sets up the expansion of the first program line numbered above HL (HL = 0: the first line;\n$FC9E = A) for EXPAND_NEXT: LINE_FIND in bank 0, then LINE_START_SET.\nExit: carry, HL = the line's number, DE = the address of its text; no carry when there is\nnone. Bank 7 paged in again.","comment":"EXPAND_CLEAR: nothing pending"},
        "5426": {"comment":"$FC9E = A"},
        "5430": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0, to read the program"},
        "5433": {"comment":"LINE_FIND: the first line HL or above"},
        "5436": {"comment":"Past the end?"},
        "5438": {"comment":"A line numbered above HL?"},
        "5440": {"comment":"HL = 0: this line"},
        "5444": {"comment":"Equal: the next line"},
        "5447": {"comment":"A line there (LINE_IN_PROG)?"},
        "5450": {"comment":"Past the end: none"},
        "5452": {"synopsis":"For the line at HL: its number as four characters at $FCA3 (LINE_NUM_DIGIT; leading zeros\nas 0 bytes, the last with bit 7 set), $FCA1 = $FCA3 and $FC9F = the address of its text.\nExit: carry, HL = the number, DE = the text.","comment":"DE = its number"},
        "5455": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 again"},
        "5458": {"comment":"DE, HL, IX kept"},
        "5462": {"comment":"IX = $FCA3, also $FCA1"},
        "5470": {"comment":"HL = the line's number"},
        "5471": {"comment":"No digit yet"},
        "5473": {"comment":"Thousands (DE = -1000)"},
        "5479": {"comment":"Hundreds (DE = -100)"},
        "5485": {"comment":"Tens (DE = -10)"},
        "5491": {"comment":"Units (DE = -1)"},
        "5497": {"comment":"Bit 7 on the last digit"},
        "5507": {"comment":"IX, HL, DE back"},
        "5511": {"comment":"$FC9F = the line's text"},
        "5517": {"comment":"HL = the number, DE = the text"},
        "5518": {"comment":"Carry: set up"},
        "5520": {"synopsis":"Bank 7 again; the flags as they are.","comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 again"},
        "5524": {"synopsis":"One decimal digit of HL into (IX), DE being minus its place's value (-1000, -100, -10, -1):\na 0 before any other digit (B = 0) is stored as the byte 0; B = 1 once a digit is not 0.\nExit: HL = the remainder, IX + 1.","comment":"A counts the place's value"},
        "5525": {"synopsis":"DE added while it fits; A counts.","comment":"The place's value taken off"},
        "5526": {"comment":"One more"},
        "5527": {"comment":"Not below 0 yet?"},
        "5529": {"comment":"The last one put back"},
        "5531": {"comment":"A = the digit's value"},
        "5532": {"comment":"The digit"},
        "5537": {"comment":"A 0?"},
        "5541": {"comment":"Any digit before it?"},
        "5545": {"comment":"A leading 0: the byte 0"},
        "5552": {"synopsis":"B = 1: zeros from now on are digits.","comment":"Zeros are digits from now on"},
        "5554": {"synopsis":"The next place.","comment":"The next place"},
        "5557": {"synopsis":"As NEXT_LINE_START, for the last program line numbered below HL. No carry when there is\nnone,\nand also when no line is numbered HL or above.","comment":"EXPAND_CLEAR: nothing pending"},
        "5560": {"comment":"$FC9E = A"},
        "5564": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0, to read the program"},
        "5567": {"comment":"LINE_FIND: DE = the line before the one found"},
        "5570": {"comment":"No line HL or above?"},
        "5572": {"comment":"HL = the line before it"},
        "5573": {"comment":"A line before it?"},
        "5576": {"comment":"Yes: its number and text set up"},
        "5579": {"comment":"None: no carry"},
        "5582": {"synopsis":"HL = the address of the line after the line at HL (its length added to its start + 4), DE =\nthe line at HL.","comment":"This line kept"},
        "5583": {"comment":"DE = the line's length"},
        "5588": {"comment":"Past the length bytes"},
        "5589": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "5590": {"comment":"DE = this line"},
        "5592": {"synopsis":"Is HL on a line? Carry when the byte there has bits 6 and 7 clear (a line number's high\nbyte, not the end of the program).","comment":"Bits 6 and 7 clear?"},
        "5595": {"comment":"Yes: carry, a line"},
        "5597": {"comment":"No: the program's end"},
        "5599": {"synopsis":"Compares the line number at HL (high byte first) with BC.\nExit: carry and Z when equal, carry and NZ when the line's is higher, no carry when it is\nlower. Keeps HL.","comment":"High bytes the same?"},
        "5601": {"comment":"No: carry when the line's is higher"},
        "5602": {"comment":"Low bytes the same?"},
        "5606": {"comment":"No: carry when the line's is higher"},
        "5607": {"comment":"Equal: carry and Z"},
        "5609": {"synopsis":"$FCA1 and $FC9F = 0: nothing to expand. Keeps HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "5610": {"comment":"Nothing pending, nothing of a line left"},
        "5621": {"synopsis":"Finds the first program line (from PROG) numbered HL or above; the program must be paged in.\nExit: carry, HL = that line, DE = the line before it (0 for none), Z when its number is HL;\nno\ncarry when there is none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC = the number sought"},
        "5623": {"comment":"DE = 0: no line before"},
        "5626": {"comment":"HL = PROG, the first line"},
        "5629": {"comment":"No lines at all?"},
        "5633": {"comment":"The first already HL or above?"},
        "5637": {"comment":"Seeking line 0?"},
        "5641": {"synopsis":"The next line, until the end or one numbered HL or above.","comment":"The next line (LINE_NEXT_ADDR), DE = this one"},
        "5644": {"comment":"The program's end?"},
        "5648": {"comment":"Numbered HL or above?"},
        "5651": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5654": {"synopsis":"The next character of the program line being expanded (set up by NEXT_LINE_START or\nPREV_LINE_START):\n1. While a text is pending at $FCA1 (the line number, a keyword's text), its next character,\nwithout bit 7; the one with bit 7 ends the text. $FC9E = $FF after the space ($A0) that\nends a keyword, else 0.\n2. Otherwise the next byte of the line at $FC9F (bank 0): the five-byte form of a number\nafter $0E is passed over. A keyword ($A5 up) puts its text at $FCA3 (KEYWORD_TEXT at\n$FCAE); $A3 and $A4 put \"SPECTRUM\" and \"PLAY\" there (WORD_TO_BUFFER at $FD09); and the\ntext's first character is taken. Any other byte is returned as it is, with $FC9E = 0;\n$0D, the line's end, also ends the expansion (both pointers 0).\nExit: carry and A = the character; no carry when nothing is left.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A text pending?"},
        "5661": {"comment":"A = the text's next character"},
        "5663": {"comment":"The space that ends a keyword?"},
        "5665": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "5670": {"comment":"$FF after the space that ends a keyword"},
        "5672": {"synopsis":"$FC9E = 0, or $FF after a keyword's last space.","comment":"$FC9E = 0 or $FF"},
        "5675": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "5676": {"comment":"The text's last character?"},
        "5680": {"comment":"The last: nothing pending after it"},
        "5683": {"synopsis":"$FCA1 = the next character, or 0 after the last.","comment":"$FCA1 = the next character or 0"},
        "5686": {"comment":"Without bit 7"},
        "5688": {"comment":"Carry: a character"},
        "5691": {"synopsis":"Nothing pending: the next byte of the line, if any.","comment":"Anything left in the line?"},
        "5696": {"comment":"Nothing: no carry"},
        "5699": {"comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0"},
        "5702": {"synopsis":"A = the byte; a number's hidden form passed over.","comment":"A = the line's next byte"},
        "5703": {"comment":"A number's marker?"},
        "5707": {"comment":"Past the marker and the number's 5 bytes"},
        "5713": {"comment":"Then the next byte"},
        "5715": {"synopsis":"Bank 7; $FC9F on.","comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 again"},
        "5718": {"comment":"$FC9F = the next byte"},
        "5722": {"comment":"A 48K keyword?"},
        "5724": {"comment":"No"},
        "5726": {"comment":"A = the keyword's place after $A5"},
        "5728": {"comment":"KEYWORD_TEXT at $FCAE: its text to $FCA3"},
        "5731": {"comment":"Then its first character"},
        "5734": {"synopsis":"$A3 (SPECTRUM) and $A4 (PLAY): their text from OWN_WORDS.","comment":"$A3 or $A4?"},
        "5736": {"comment":"Below $A3: a character"},
        "5738": {"comment":"$A4: PLAY"},
        "5740": {"comment":"HL = \"SPECTRUM\" in OWN_WORDS"},
        "5745": {"synopsis":"$A4: \"PLAY\".","comment":"HL = \"PLAY\" in OWN_WORDS"},
        "5748": {"synopsis":"The text to $FCA3, then its first character.","comment":"WORD_TO_BUFFER at $FD09: the text to $FCA3"},
        "5751": {"comment":"Then its first character"},
        "5754": {"synopsis":"Any other character: $FC9E = 0; $0D ends the expansion.","comment":"$FC9E = 0, A kept"},
        "5761": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "5763": {"comment":"No: the character"},
        "5765": {"comment":"Yes: nothing pending, the line done"},
        "5774": {"synopsis":"Carry: A is a character.","comment":"Carry: A is a character"},
        "5776": {"synopsis":"No carry: nothing left.","comment":"No carry: nothing left"},
        "5779": {"synopsis":"Seven words, each with bit 7 set on its last character, for WORD_FIND (from $2124, B = $F9\nfor the first): \"SPECTRUM\", \"PLAY\", \"GOTO\", \"GOSUB\", \"DEFFN\", \"OPEN#\", \"CLOSE#\". EXPAND_NEXT\nalso prints the first two as the texts of $A3 and $A4."},
        "5816": {"synopsis":"ROW_SETUP's bytes for COPY_COUNTED: a count (2), then 1 for $FD96 and 5 for $FD97."},
        "5819": {"synopsis":"$FD96 = 1 and $FD97 = 5 (the cells a line's later rows are indented by, ROW_INDENT), copied\nfrom ROW_SETUP_DATA by COPY_COUNTED ($2157).","comment":"HL = ROW_SETUP_DATA"},
        "5822": {"comment":"DE = $FD96"},
        "5825": {"comment":"Copied (COPY_COUNTED)"},
        "5828": {"synopsis":"Puts A in column B of row DE; B + 1.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"HL = the cell at column B"},
        "5832": {"comment":"A in it"},
        "5833": {"comment":"The next column"},
        "5835": {"synopsis":"EXPAND_CODES' routine for $0D (the word table at $1390): the rest of row DE cleared\n(ROW_CLEAR_REST), its flags' bits 3 and 4 set, $FD96 bit 0 set.\nExit: carry, which ends LINE_TO_ROWS.","comment":"ROW_CLEAR_REST: the row's rest cleared, HL = its flags"},
        "5838": {"comment":"Bits 3 and 4 set"},
        "5842": {"comment":"$FD96 bit 0 set"},
        "5847": {"comment":"Carry: the line has ended"},
        "5849": {"synopsis":"EXPAND_CODES' routine for $01 (a line with no text; the word table at $1390): as\nROW_END_LINE, setting only bit 3 of the flags.","comment":"ROW_CLEAR_REST: the row's rest cleared, HL = its flags"},
        "5852": {"comment":"Bit 3: the line's last row"},
        "5854": {"comment":"$FD96 bit 0 set"},
        "5859": {"comment":"Carry: the line has ended"},
        "5861": {"synopsis":"Clears row DE's cells from column B to 31 (to 0).\nExit: B = 32, HL = the row's flags byte.","comment":"HL = the cell at column B"},
        "5865": {"comment":"A = 32, the column past the last"},
        "5867": {"synopsis":"Up to column 32.","comment":"Past column 31?"},
        "5869": {"comment":"The cell cleared"},
        "5871": {"comment":"The next"},
        "5875": {"synopsis":"Clears row DE's first ($FD97) cells.\nExit: B = ($FD97), the column after them.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"A = the indent, from $FD97"},
        "5878": {"comment":"From column 0"},
        "5880": {"synopsis":"One cell.","comment":"HL = the cell"},
        "5884": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "5886": {"comment":"The next"},
        "5887": {"comment":"More?"},
        "5891": {"synopsis":"Prints the row at HL on window line C (PRINT_ROW with B = C), unless $EEF5 bit 2 is set.\nKeeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "5895": {"comment":"Output held back ($EEF5 bit 2)?"},
        "5903": {"comment":"B = the line"},
        "5904": {"comment":"PRINT_ROW: the row printed"},
        "5907": {"synopsis":"BC, DE, HL back.","comment":"BC, DE, HL back"},
        "5911": {"synopsis":"Unless $EEF5 bit 2 is set: SCROLL_UP with E = C, which moves window lines B + 1 to C one\nline\nup and prints the row at HL on line C. Keeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "5915": {"comment":"Output held back ($EEF5 bit 2)?"},
        "5923": {"comment":"E = the last line"},
        "5924": {"comment":"SCROLL_UP: the lines moved up, the row printed"},
        "5927": {"synopsis":"BC, DE, HL back.","comment":"BC, DE, HL back"},
        "5931": {"synopsis":"Unless $EEF5 bit 2 is set: SCROLL_DOWN with E = C, which moves window lines B to C - 1 one\nline down and prints the row at HL on line B. Keeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE, HL kept"},
        "5935": {"comment":"Output held back ($EEF5 bit 2)?"},
        "5943": {"comment":"E = the last line"},
        "5944": {"comment":"SCROLL_DOWN: the lines moved down, the row printed"},
        "5947": {"synopsis":"BC, DE, HL back.","comment":"BC, DE, HL back"},
        "5951": {"synopsis":"Marks the cell at column B, line C: WIN_CURSOR_ON (B and C swapped for it) keeps the cell's\nattribute in (IX+7) and gives it (IX+6)'s colours with its FLASH and BRIGHT bits inverted.\nKeeps all registers.","comment":"All registers kept"},
        "5955": {"comment":"B = the line, C = the column"},
        "5958": {"comment":"WIN_CURSOR_ON"},
        "5961": {"comment":"All registers back"},
        "5966": {"synopsis":"Puts back the attribute CELL_CURSOR_ON kept for the cell at column B, line C\n(WIN_CURSOR_OFF). Keeps all registers.","comment":"All registers kept"},
        "5970": {"comment":"B = the line, C = the column"},
        "5973": {"comment":"WIN_CURSOR_OFF"},
        "5976": {"comment":"All registers back"},
        "5981": {"synopsis":"MODE ($5C41) = 0, REPPER = 2, then KEY_MODE.","comment":"MODE = 0"},
        "5986": {"comment":"REPPER = 2"},
        "5991": {"comment":"KEY_MODE"},
        "5995": {"synopsis":"244 bytes no code in this ROM reads (KEY_DEFAULTS returns just before them; KEY_MODE\nfollows). The low 7 bits of each byte XOR $30 are ASCII; bit 7 is set on many bytes in no\npattern that matters to the text. Decoded, lines ended by $0D credit the ROM's authors,\nthank\nothers, and say it was written on Amstrad PCWs with M80 and L80 under CP/M+."},
        "6239": {"synopsis":"FLAGS bits 2 and 3 set; $5B66 bit 0 set when $EC0D bit 4 is set, else cleared.","comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "6242": {"comment":"Bits 2 and 3 set"},
        "6246": {"comment":"$EC0D bit 4 set?"},
        "6251": {"comment":"HL = $5B66"},
        "6254": {"comment":"Yes: bit 0 set"},
        "6256": {"comment":"No: bit 0 cleared"},
        "6259": {"synopsis":"$5B66 bit 0 set.","comment":"Bit 0 set"},
        "6262": {"synopsis":"Waits for a new key (FLAGS bit 5), takes it from LAST_K (MODE bit 0 cleared): codes $20 and\nup, and $06-$0F after ROM 3's KI_CAPS_LOCK accepts them (KEY_CONTROL); $00-$05 and $10-$1F\nare ignored.\nExit: A = the key. Keeps HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "6263": {"synopsis":"HL = FLAGS, for the next key.","comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "6266": {"synopsis":"Until FLAGS bit 5 says a key came.","comment":"A new key?"},
        "6270": {"comment":"It is taken"},
        "6272": {"comment":"A = LAST_K"},
        "6275": {"comment":"MODE bit 0 cleared"},
        "6280": {"comment":"$20 and up: a key"},
        "6284": {"comment":"$10-$1F: ignored"},
        "6288": {"comment":"Below $06: ignored"},
        "6292": {"comment":"KEY_CONTROL: ROM 3's KI_CAPS_LOCK on it"},
        "6295": {"comment":"Not taken: wait again"},
        "6297": {"synopsis":"HL back; A = the key.","comment":"HL back; A = the key"},
        "6299": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's KI_CAPS_LOCK on the key in A.","comment":"ROM 3's KI_CAPS_LOCK: CAPS LOCK or a mode key handled"},
        "6303": {"synopsis":"Draws the menu whose text is at HL (a count, a title ended by $FF, items ended by bit 7):\n1. The area under it saved (MENU_AREA_SAVE); printing to the main screen.\n2. MENU_HEADER_TEXT and the title (PRINT_FF_TEXT), the stripes (DRAW_STRIPES) and\nMENU_AFTER_TITLE.\n3. The items from AT 8,7, one a line (MENU_ITEM).\n4. A border plotted down the left, along the bottom and up the right (PLOT_LINE).\n5. The bar on item 0 (MENU_BAR).","comment":"The menu's text kept"},
        "6304": {"comment":"MENU_AREA_SAVE: what the menu covers saved"},
        "6307": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared: printing to the main screen"},
        "6312": {"comment":"HL = the menu's text"},
        "6313": {"comment":"E = the count"},
        "6315": {"comment":"The header's place and colours (MENU_HEADER_TEXT)"},
        "6322": {"comment":"The title (PRINT_FF_TEXT)"},
        "6326": {"comment":"HL kept; DRAW_STRIPES: the title's stripes"},
        "6330": {"comment":"PAPER 0, a space, PAPER 7, INK 0 after the stripes"},
        "6336": {"comment":"HL = the items"},
        "6337": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "6338": {"comment":"AT line 8, column 7"},
        "6344": {"synopsis":"One item at the print position: a space, then up to 12 characters.","comment":"The line kept"},
        "6345": {"comment":"B = 12 characters at most"},
        "6347": {"comment":"A space first"},
        "6350": {"synopsis":"The next character; the one with bit 7 is the last.","comment":"The next character"},
        "6352": {"comment":"Bit 7: the item's last?"},
        "6356": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "6359": {"synopsis":"The last character without bit 7.","comment":"Without bit 7, printed"},
        "6362": {"synopsis":"Spaces to the width.","comment":"A space, B times: the line is 14 cells wide"},
        "6367": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "6369": {"comment":"AT the next line"},
        "6372": {"comment":"Items left?"},
        "6375": {"comment":"H = 111, L = 56: the border's corner"},
        "6378": {"comment":"E = the count"},
        "6379": {"comment":"Times 8: the height in pixels"},
        "6385": {"comment":"D = the height - 1"},
        "6387": {"comment":"E = 111, the width"},
        "6389": {"comment":"The left side: y - 1 each, D pixels down"},
        "6396": {"comment":"The bottom: x + 1 each, E pixels across"},
        "6403": {"comment":"The right side: y + 1 each, D + 1 pixels up"},
        "6411": {"comment":"The bar on item 0"},
        "6416": {"synopsis":"Plots A pixels from H (y), L (x), stepping by BC (B to H, C to L) each time: ROM 3's\nPLOT_SUB entered at $22E9, past its COORDS store. Keeps all registers but HL, AF.","comment":"AF, HL, DE, BC kept"},
        "6420": {"comment":"B = y (H), C = x (L)"},
        "6422": {"comment":"ROM 3's PLOT_SUB past its COORDS store: pixel C, B"},
        "6425": {"comment":"Back"},
        "6429": {"comment":"H, L one step on"},
        "6430": {"comment":"More?"},
        "6434": {"synopsis":"AT B, C through RST $10.","comment":"AT"},
        "6437": {"comment":"Line B"},
        "6439": {"comment":"Column C"},
        "6442": {"synopsis":"Prints the characters at HL through RST $10, up to the $FF that ends them. A '+' followed by\n'3' is printed as \"+2A\", the '3' and the character after it dropped, unless $5B66 bit 4 is\nset.\nExit: HL past the $FF.","comment":"The next character"},
        "6444": {"comment":"$FF: the end?"},
        "6447": {"comment":"A '+'?"},
        "6451": {"synopsis":"A printed; the next.","comment":"Printed"},
        "6452": {"comment":"The next"},
        "6454": {"synopsis":"A '+': is a '3' next?","comment":"A '3' after the '+'?"},
        "6457": {"comment":"A = '+' (the flags kept)"},
        "6459": {"comment":"No: the '+' printed as it is"},
        "6461": {"comment":"$5B66 bit 4 set?"},
        "6468": {"comment":"Yes: the '+' printed, then the '3'"},
        "6470": {"comment":"No: past the '3' and the character after it"},
        "6472": {"comment":"'+'"},
        "6475": {"comment":"'2'"},
        "6478": {"comment":"Then 'A', printed at PRINT_FF_CHAR"},
        "6482": {"synopsis":"Saves TV_FLAG, COORDS onwards (20 bytes) and the screen and attributes where the menu goes\nto\n$EEF6 on; MENU_AREA_BACK puts them back.","comment":"Carry: saving"},
        "6483": {"comment":"To MENU_AREA_COPY"},
        "6485": {"synopsis":"MENU_AREA_SAVE the other way: back from $EEF6 (from $07D6).","comment":"No carry: putting back"},
        "6486": {"synopsis":"The copy, from the menu's area to $EEF6 with carry, the other way without: DE is kept as the\nplace in $EEF6.","comment":"DE = the store at $EEF6, HL = TV_FLAG"},
        "6492": {"comment":"Saving: from TV_FLAG to the store"},
        "6494": {"comment":"Putting back: the other way"},
        "6495": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG.","comment":"TV_FLAG copied"},
        "6497": {"comment":"DE = the store's place again"},
        "6500": {"synopsis":"HL = COORDS ($5C7D).","comment":"HL = COORDS"},
        "6503": {"comment":"Putting back: swapped"},
        "6506": {"synopsis":"20 bytes from COORDS.","comment":"20 bytes copied"},
        "6511": {"comment":"DE = the store's place again"},
        "6514": {"synopsis":"The screen: 12 lines from line 7, columns 7-20; the direction kept in F'.","comment":"The direction kept in F'"},
        "6515": {"comment":"Line 7, column 7"},
        "6518": {"comment":"POSN_TO_ROM3: line and column in ROM 3's form"},
        "6521": {"comment":"Plus the window's top line"},
        "6526": {"comment":"12 lines"},
        "6528": {"synopsis":"One line: its display address (ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR) + 7.","comment":"Line, count and place kept"},
        "6531": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR: HL = the line's display address"},
        "6534": {"comment":"Plus 7: column 7"},
        "6538": {"comment":"DE = the store's place"},
        "6539": {"comment":"MENU_LINE_COPY: the line's 8 pixel rows and attributes"},
        "6542": {"comment":"Count and line back"},
        "6544": {"comment":"The next line down"},
        "6545": {"comment":"More?"},
        "6549": {"synopsis":"Eight pixel rows of 14 bytes, then the line's 14 attributes (ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR),\nbetween\nHL and DE as F' carry says.","comment":"B = 8 pixel rows, C = 14 bytes in each"},
        "6552": {"synopsis":"One pixel row.","comment":"The row count kept, BC = 14"},
        "6555": {"comment":"The row's start kept"},
        "6556": {"comment":"The direction from F'"},
        "6557": {"comment":"Saving: from the screen"},
        "6559": {"comment":"Putting back: to the screen"},
        "6560": {"synopsis":"14 bytes.","comment":"14 bytes"},
        "6562": {"comment":"The pair as it was"},
        "6565": {"synopsis":"The next pixel row down.","comment":"The direction back in F'"},
        "6566": {"comment":"HL = the next pixel row (H + 1)"},
        "6568": {"comment":"Rows left?"},
        "6571": {"comment":"BC = 14 and the store's place kept"},
        "6573": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR: the line's attributes"},
        "6576": {"comment":"HL = the attributes' address"},
        "6577": {"comment":"DE = the store's place, BC = 14"},
        "6579": {"comment":"The direction from F'"},
        "6580": {"comment":"Saving: from the attributes"},
        "6582": {"comment":"Putting back: to them"},
        "6583": {"synopsis":"14 attributes.","comment":"14 attributes"},
        "6585": {"comment":"The pair as it was"},
        "6588": {"synopsis":"The direction back in F'.","comment":"The direction back in F'"},
        "6590": {"synopsis":"Moves the menu's bar from item A to the one above it, from item 0 to the last ((HL) - 2, HL\nbeing the menu's text, whose first byte is DRAW_MENU's count).\nExit: A = the new item, carry.","comment":"The bar off item A"},
        "6593": {"comment":"The item above"},
        "6594": {"comment":"Not above item 0?"},
        "6597": {"comment":"Above it: the last item, (HL) - 2"},
        "6600": {"synopsis":"The bar on item A.","comment":"The bar on item A"},
        "6603": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "6605": {"synopsis":"Moves the menu's bar from item A to the one below it, from the last ((HL) - 2) to item 0.\nExit: A = the new item. Keeps DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "6606": {"comment":"The bar off item A"},
        "6609": {"comment":"The item below"},
        "6610": {"comment":"D = it"},
        "6611": {"comment":"A = the last item, (HL) - 2"},
        "6614": {"comment":"Past it?"},
        "6615": {"comment":"A = the item below"},
        "6616": {"comment":"Not past the last: kept"},
        "6619": {"comment":"Past it: item 0"},
        "6620": {"synopsis":"The bar on item A.","comment":"The bar on item A"},
        "6623": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "6625": {"synopsis":"Flips the menu's bar on or off at item A: the 14 attribute cells of row $5907 + 32 x A\nbecome $68 when they are $78, otherwise $78. Keeps all registers.","comment":"AF, HL, DE kept"},
        "6628": {"comment":"HL = item 0's bar: line 8, column 7"},
        "6631": {"comment":"DE = 32, an attribute line"},
        "6634": {"comment":"Item 0?"},
        "6637": {"synopsis":"One attribute line per item.","comment":"Down a line"},
        "6638": {"comment":"For each item"},
        "6641": {"synopsis":"$68 (cyan paper) where it is $78 (white paper), else $78.","comment":"White paper ($78)?"},
        "6646": {"comment":"Yes: cyan paper ($68)"},
        "6648": {"synopsis":"14 cells.","comment":"14 cells"},
        "6650": {"synopsis":"One cell.","comment":"The cell"},
        "6652": {"comment":"More?"},
        "6655": {"comment":"DE, HL, AF back"},
        "6659": {"synopsis":"DRAW_MENU's and TITLE_BAR's header, ended by $FF (PRINT_FF_TEXT): AT 7,7; OVER 0; INVERSE 0;\nINK 7; PAPER 0; BRIGHT 1."},
        "6673": {"synopsis":"Printed after a menu's stripes, ended by $FF: PAPER 0, a space, PAPER 7, INK 0."},
        "6681": {"synopsis":"DRAW_STRIPES' two character pictures, 8 bytes each, copied to $5B7C: a triangle filling the\nlower right of the cell (01 03 07 ... FF) and its complement (FE FC ... 00)."},
        "6697": {"synopsis":"The stripes, ended by $FF, printed with codes $20 and $21 as STRIPE_GLYPHS' pictures:\nINK 2, ' ', PAPER 6, '!', INK 4, ' ', PAPER 5, '!', INK 0, ' '."},
        "6713": {"synopsis":"Draws the coloured stripes after a title: STRIPE_GLYPHS copied to $5B7C and STRIPE_TEXT\nprinted with CHARS = $5A7C, so that codes $20 and $21 are those pictures; CHARS back.\nKeeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC, DE and HL kept"},
        "6716": {"comment":"The two diagonal pictures (STRIPE_GLYPHS) to $5B7C"},
        "6727": {"comment":"CHARS kept"},
        "6731": {"comment":"CHARS = $5A7C: codes $20 and $21 are the pictures at $5B7C"},
        "6737": {"comment":"The stripes (STRIPE_TEXT, PRINT_FF_TEXT)"},
        "6743": {"comment":"CHARS back"},
        "6747": {"comment":"HL, DE and BC back"},
        "6751": {"synopsis":"The bottom title bar with \"+3 BASIC\" ($0814): on at TITLE_BAR.","comment":"HL = \"+3 BASIC\" at $0814"},
        "6756": {"synopsis":"The bottom title bar with \"Calculator\" ($081C).","comment":"HL = \"Calculator\" at $081C"},
        "6761": {"synopsis":"The bottom title bar with \"Loader\" ($080E).","comment":"HL = \"Loader\" at $080E"},
        "6764": {"synopsis":"Draws the title bar on line 21 with the text at HL (ended by bit 7): lines 21 to 23 cleared\n(CLEAR_LOW_3), line 21's attributes $40, MENU_HEADER_TEXT's colours, the text at AT 21,0\n(PRINT_BIT7_TEXT, $02A3), then the stripes at AT 21,26 (DRAW_STRIPES).","comment":"The text kept"},
        "6765": {"comment":"CLEAR_LOW_3: lines 21 to 23 cleared"},
        "6768": {"comment":"Line 21's attributes"},
        "6771": {"comment":"32 cells of $40: BRIGHT 1, PAPER 0, INK 0"},
        "6775": {"synopsis":"One attribute.","comment":"One cell"},
        "6777": {"comment":"All 32?"},
        "6779": {"comment":"MENU_HEADER_TEXT's colours"},
        "6785": {"comment":"AT 21,0"},
        "6791": {"comment":"DE = the title"},
        "6792": {"comment":"Printed up to its bit-7 end (PRINT_BIT7_TEXT)"},
        "6795": {"comment":"AT 21,26 and the stripes"},
        "6800": {"comment":"DRAW_STRIPES, which returns to the caller"},
        "6803": {"synopsis":"Clears lines 21 to 23 (CLEAR_LINES with B = 21, D = 23).","comment":"B = 21, the first line"},
        "6805": {"comment":"D = 23, the last"},
        "6807": {"comment":"Cleared (CLEAR_LINES)"},
        "6810": {"synopsis":"Renumbers the program, from the number in $5B75 in steps of the one in $5B77 (start-up sets\nboth to 10 at $01EA), with bank 0 and the machine stack:\n1. The lines counted (COUNT_LINES); none, or start + step x count (one step past the last\nline's new number; the product's overflow is not tested) 10000 or more: RENUM_FAIL.\n2. Every line's text is searched for LINE, LIST, LLIST, GO TO, GO SUB, RESTORE and RUN\nfollowed by a plain number (RENUM_REF); each such number is replaced by the new number of\nthe line it names.\n3. Every line gets its new number, start + step x its place.\n4. Bank 7 and its stack; $5B73 = 0.\nExit: carry when done; no carry (RENUM_FAIL) when there are no lines, the numbers would go\npast 9999, or there is no room for a longer number.\nObserved: lines 1 and 2 became 10 and 20; $5B75 and $5B77 held 10 and 10.","comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "6813": {"comment":"COUNT_LINES: DE = the number of lines"},
        "6816": {"comment":"No lines at all?"},
        "6821": {"comment":"HL = the step, from $5B77"},
        "6824": {"comment":"HL = step x count; its overflow not tested"},
        "6827": {"comment":"DE = step x count"},
        "6828": {"comment":"Plus the start, from $5B75"},
        "6832": {"comment":"10000 or more?"},
        "6841": {"comment":"From the first line"},
        "6844": {"synopsis":"One line: $5B73 = the address of its length, $5B96 = the next line's (ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM).","comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM: DE = the next line"},
        "6847": {"comment":"HL = the address of the line's length"},
        "6849": {"comment":"Kept in $5B73"},
        "6852": {"comment":"HL = the line's first character"},
        "6854": {"comment":"$5B96 = the next line"},
        "6858": {"synopsis":"The line's next character, past a hidden number (ROM 3's SKIP_NUMBER); up to its ENTER each\nis checked by RENUM_REF.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "6859": {"comment":"Past a hidden number (ROM 3's SKIP_NUMBER)"},
        "6862": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "6866": {"comment":"RENUM_REF: a keyword with a line number to change?"},
        "6869": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "6871": {"synopsis":"The line done: on to the next, up to VARS.","comment":"DE = the next line"},
        "6875": {"comment":"Reached VARS?"},
        "6881": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "6884": {"comment":"COUNT_LINES again: DE = the count"},
        "6887": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "6889": {"comment":"DE = 0, the line's place"},
        "6892": {"comment":"HL = PROG, the first line"},
        "6895": {"synopsis":"One line's new number: step x DE + start, written high byte first over the old; then past\nthe line by its length.","comment":"Count, place and line kept"},
        "6898": {"comment":"HL = the step"},
        "6901": {"comment":"ROM 3's HL_HL_X_DE: HL = step x place"},
        "6904": {"comment":"Plus the start: the new number"},
        "6909": {"comment":"DE = the new number"},
        "6910": {"comment":"HL = the line"},
        "6911": {"comment":"Written over the old, high byte first"},
        "6915": {"comment":"BC = the line's length"},
        "6918": {"comment":"HL past the length, then past the line"},
        "6920": {"comment":"DE = the next place"},
        "6922": {"comment":"BC = the lines left"},
        "6923": {"comment":"The last line?"},
        "6928": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 and its stack"},
        "6931": {"comment":"$5B73 = 0"},
        "6935": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "6937": {"synopsis":"RENUM_REF's keywords, searched with CPIR: LINE, LIST, LLIST, GO TO, GO SUB, RESTORE, RUN\n($CA $F0 $E1 $EC $ED $E5 $F7)."},
        "6944": {"synopsis":"Checks the character A at HL for a line number to change: when it is one of RENUM_TOKENS and\na number follows (spaces, digits, '.', 'E' after a digit) whose hidden form is followed by\n':' or ENTER, the number's text and hidden value are replaced by the new number of the line\nit names (the first line from that number on): RENUM_REF_NUMBER. $5B94 = the place after the\nkeyword, $5B8C = the old text's length.\nExit: HL = the place to go on from; $5B96 and the line's length moved by the change.","comment":"HL = the place after the character"},
        "6945": {"comment":"$5B94 = it"},
        "6948": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "6949": {"comment":"RENUM_TOKENS' 7 codes searched for A"},
        "6955": {"comment":"One of RENUM_TOKENS?"},
        "6957": {"comment":"HL = the place after the character"},
        "6958": {"comment":"Not one: back"},
        "6959": {"comment":"BC counts the number's characters"},
        "6961": {"synopsis":"The next character of the number.","comment":"A = the next character"},
        "6962": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "6966": {"comment":"ROM 3's DIGIT_TEST: a digit?"},
        "6969": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6971": {"comment":"A '.'?"},
        "6975": {"comment":"The hidden number's marker?"},
        "6979": {"comment":"'e' or 'E'?"},
        "6985": {"comment":"After a digit (BC not 0)?"},
        "6989": {"synopsis":"Not a plain number: left as it is; on from $5B94.","comment":"HL = the place after the keyword"},
        "6993": {"synopsis":"Counted; the next.","comment":"Counted"},
        "6994": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "6997": {"synopsis":"The hidden number reached: $5B8C = the text's length; only a number followed (past spaces)\nby ':' or ENTER is changed.","comment":"$5B8C = the text's length"},
        "7001": {"comment":"The marker's place kept"},
        "7002": {"comment":"ROM 3's SKIP_NUMBER: HL past the hidden number"},
        "7005": {"comment":"SKIP_SPACES"},
        "7008": {"comment":"A = the character after it"},
        "7009": {"comment":"HL = the marker"},
        "7010": {"comment":"A ':' after it?"},
        "7014": {"comment":"ENTER after it? Neither: left as it is"},
        "7017": {"synopsis":"The number's value (ROM 3's PUSH_NUMBER, FP_TO_BC) looked up as a line (ROM 3's FIND_LINE).\nNo such line and nothing after the program (the byte there $80):\n9999. Otherwise HL is the\nline found.","comment":"HL = the hidden number"},
        "7018": {"comment":"ROM 3's PUSH_NUMBER: its value stacked"},
        "7021": {"comment":"ROM 3's FP_TO_BC: BC = the value"},
        "7024": {"comment":"HL = the line number"},
        "7026": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_LINE: HL = the first line from it on"},
        "7029": {"comment":"That line itself?"},
        "7031": {"comment":"No: the byte there, a line's or the variables'"},
        "7032": {"comment":"$80: past the last line?"},
        "7036": {"comment":"No line from it on: 9999"},
        "7041": {"synopsis":"The line found: its new number, step x its place (COUNT_LINES_TO) + start.","comment":"$5B92 = the line found"},
        "7044": {"comment":"COUNT_LINES_TO: DE = the lines before it"},
        "7047": {"comment":"HL = the step"},
        "7050": {"comment":"ROM 3's HL_HL_X_DE: HL = step x place"},
        "7053": {"comment":"Plus the start: its new number"},
        "7058": {"synopsis":"The new number HL as text at $5B8E (NUMBER_TEXT, leading zeros dropped); $5B8C = its length\nless the old text's. Longer: room made after the keyword when STKEND + the difference + $82\nstays below SP (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM), else RENUM_NO_ROOM.","comment":"DE = the text's place, $5B8E"},
        "7061": {"comment":"The new number kept, for the hidden form"},
        "7062": {"comment":"NUMBER_TEXT: HL = the first digit kept, B = digits after it"},
        "7065": {"comment":"DE = the new text's length"},
        "7069": {"comment":"The length and the first digit kept"},
        "7071": {"comment":"HL = the new length"},
        "7074": {"comment":"BC = the old length"},
        "7078": {"comment":"HL = the new length less the old"},
        "7081": {"comment":"$5B8C = the difference"},
        "7084": {"comment":"The same length?"},
        "7086": {"comment":"Shorter?"},
        "7088": {"comment":"Longer: BC = the bytes to make room for"},
        "7090": {"comment":"HL = the place after the keyword"},
        "7093": {"comment":"The place and the length kept"},
        "7095": {"comment":"STKEND + the difference past 65535?"},
        "7101": {"comment":"DE = STKEND + the difference"},
        "7102": {"comment":"Plus $82 bytes to spare"},
        "7108": {"comment":"Still below SP?"},
        "7113": {"comment":"DE = the length, HL = the place"},
        "7115": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM: room after the keyword"},
        "7118": {"comment":"On to the copy"},
        "7120": {"synopsis":"No room: the two words dropped; on to RENUM_FAIL.","comment":"The length and the place dropped"},
        "7122": {"synopsis":"Bank 7 and its stack (BANK7_STACK), no carry, and a return: the swap back to bank 7's stack\nreturns to RENUMBER's caller from any depth.","comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 and its stack"},
        "7125": {"comment":"No carry: not done"},
        "7127": {"synopsis":"Shorter: BC = the old length less the new; that many bytes after the keyword removed (ROM\n3's\nRECLAIM).","comment":"BC less the new length, one by one"},
        "7131": {"comment":"HL = the place after the keyword"},
        "7134": {"comment":"ROM 3's RECLAIM: BC bytes removed there"},
        "7137": {"synopsis":"The new digits copied after the keyword, then the number marker $0E and the new value's five\nbytes (ROM 3's STACK_BC); the line's length at ($5B73) and the next line's address ($5B96)\nmoved by the change.\nExit: HL = the place after the number.","comment":"DE = the place after the keyword"},
        "7141": {"comment":"HL = the new text, BC = its length"},
        "7143": {"comment":"The digits copied in"},
        "7145": {"comment":"HL = the byte after them"},
        "7146": {"comment":"The number's marker"},
        "7148": {"comment":"BC = the new number"},
        "7149": {"comment":"The five bytes' place kept"},
        "7151": {"comment":"ROM 3's STACK_BC: the new value, HL = its 5 bytes"},
        "7154": {"comment":"DE = their place"},
        "7155": {"comment":"The five bytes copied over the old ones"},
        "7160": {"comment":"The place after them kept"},
        "7162": {"comment":"HL = the address of the line's length"},
        "7166": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "7169": {"comment":"Plus the difference"},
        "7173": {"comment":"DE = the new length"},
        "7174": {"comment":"HL = its address"},
        "7175": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "7178": {"comment":"The next line's address"},
        "7181": {"comment":"Moved by the difference"},
        "7189": {"comment":"HL = the place after the number"},
        "7191": {"synopsis":"DE = the number of program lines: COUNT_LINES_TO with $5B92 = VARS.","comment":"HL = VARS"},
        "7194": {"comment":"$5B92 = it, the place to count to"},
        "7197": {"synopsis":"DE = the number of program lines before the address in $5B92, stepping from PROG with ROM\n3's\nNEXT_ITEM (0 when it is PROG).\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "7200": {"comment":"DE = the place to count to"},
        "7204": {"comment":"The first line?"},
        "7209": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "7212": {"comment":"BC = 0 lines"},
        "7215": {"synopsis":"The next line: is it the one?","comment":"The count kept"},
        "7216": {"comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM: DE = the next line"},
        "7219": {"comment":"The place reached?"},
        "7227": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "7228": {"comment":"One more line"},
        "7232": {"synopsis":"Found: DE = the count.","comment":"DE = the count"},
        "7233": {"comment":"Plus the line just stepped over"},
        "7235": {"synopsis":"It is the first: DE = 0.","comment":"None before it"},
        "7239": {"synopsis":"HL moved on, then SKIP_SPACES.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "7240": {"synopsis":"A = the byte at HL, HL moved past spaces.","comment":"A = the byte"},
        "7241": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "7246": {"synopsis":"Writes HL (0-9999) as four digits at DE (NUMBER_DIGIT for the thousands, hundreds and tens),\nthen turns up to three leading '0's into spaces.\nExit: HL = the first digit kept, B = the digits after it; DE past the text.","comment":"The text's start kept"},
        "7247": {"comment":"-1000"},
        "7250": {"comment":"The thousands (NUMBER_DIGIT)"},
        "7253": {"comment":"-100"},
        "7256": {"comment":"The hundreds"},
        "7259": {"comment":"-10"},
        "7261": {"comment":"The tens"},
        "7264": {"comment":"The units"},
        "7265": {"comment":"As a character"},
        "7267": {"comment":"Written"},
        "7269": {"comment":"B = up to three leading '0's"},
        "7271": {"comment":"HL = the first digit"},
        "7272": {"synopsis":"A leading '0'?","comment":"A = the digit"},
        "7273": {"comment":"A '0'?"},
        "7275": {"comment":"Not a '0': HL = the first digit kept"},
        "7276": {"comment":"Made a space"},
        "7279": {"comment":"Up to three"},
        "7282": {"synopsis":"One digit: how many times BC (a negative power of ten) goes into HL, as a character at DE;\nHL\nkeeps the rest.","comment":"A counts"},
        "7283": {"synopsis":"One more.","comment":"The power of ten taken off"},
        "7284": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "7285": {"comment":"Not below zero yet?"},
        "7287": {"comment":"The last one undone"},
        "7289": {"comment":"A = the digit"},
        "7290": {"comment":"As a character"},
        "7292": {"comment":"Written at DE"},
        "7295": {"synopsis":"The editor's window for the main screen, copied to $FD98 (IX) by WINDOW_SET: a count (8),\nthen the bytes 0, 0 (IX + 1, its top line), 20 (IX + 2, its last line counted from the top),\n0, 0, 0, $0F (IX + 6, the cursor's colour), 0."},
        "7304": {"synopsis":"The window for the lower screen: a count (8), then 0, 22 (its top line), 1 (its last line\ncounted from the top: lines 22-23), 0, 0, 0, $0F, 0."},
        "7313": {"synopsis":"IX = $FD98, the window there from WINDOW_MAIN_DATA (main screen, lines 0-20).","comment":"IX = the window's bytes at $FD98"},
        "7317": {"comment":"HL = WINDOW_MAIN_DATA"},
        "7322": {"synopsis":"The window at $FD98 from WINDOW_LOW_DATA (lines 22-23).","comment":"HL = WINDOW_LOW_DATA (IX as it was)"},
        "7325": {"synopsis":"The 8 bytes at HL to $FD98 (COPY_COUNTED, $2157).","comment":"DE = the window at $FD98"},
        "7328": {"comment":"The 8 bytes copied (COPY_COUNTED)"},
        "7331": {"synopsis":"Prints A, then D (RST $10 each); carry. Nothing in this ROM calls it.","comment":"A printed"},
        "7332": {"comment":"Then D"},
        "7334": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7336": {"synopsis":"The cursor's colour, IX + 6 = A's PAPER and INK bits ($3F); carry.","comment":"PAPER and INK only"},
        "7338": {"comment":"The cursor's colour"},
        "7341": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7343": {"synopsis":"Shows the cursor at line B of the window (IX + 1 added), column C: the attribute there kept\nin IX + 7, then replaced by IX + 6's colour with the old FLASH and BRIGHT bits inverted.\nCarry.\nChanges: A, B, DE, HL.","comment":"B = the screen line: B + the window's top"},
        "7348": {"comment":"ATTR_ADDRESS: HL = the cell's attribute address"},
        "7351": {"comment":"The old attribute kept in IX + 7"},
        "7355": {"comment":"FLASH, BRIGHT inverted"},
        "7358": {"comment":"Plus the cursor's colour"},
        "7361": {"comment":"Shown"},
        "7362": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7364": {"synopsis":"Takes the cursor off line B of the window, column C: the attribute kept in IX + 7 put back.","comment":"B = the screen line: B + the window's top"},
        "7369": {"comment":"ATTR_ADDRESS: HL = the cell's attribute address"},
        "7372": {"comment":"The attribute kept in IX + 7 put back"},
        "7377": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window's lines B to E up by one (pixels and attributes, each line from the one\nbelow), then prints the 32 characters at HL on line E (PRINT_ROW).","comment":"The text kept"},
        "7378": {"comment":"H = 0: up"},
        "7380": {"comment":"A = the lines to move, E less B"},
        "7384": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window's lines B to E down by one (B the upper; each line from the one above,\nstarting at E), then prints the 32 characters at HL on line B (PRINT_ROW).","comment":"The text kept"},
        "7385": {"comment":"B = the lower line E, E = the upper B"},
        "7388": {"comment":"A = the lines to move"},
        "7389": {"comment":"H = $FF: down"},
        "7391": {"synopsis":"C = the lines to move; none when B = E.","comment":"C = the count"},
        "7392": {"comment":"Only one line?"},
        "7396": {"comment":"The line to print kept in E"},
        "7397": {"comment":"LINE_TO_ROM3: B in ROM 3's form"},
        "7400": {"synopsis":"One line: its display address (ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR), and the source's, one below (up)\nor one above (down).","comment":"Line and count kept"},
        "7401": {"comment":"C = the direction"},
        "7402": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR: the line's display address"},
        "7405": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "7406": {"comment":"Up?"},
        "7410": {"comment":"Down: the line above (ROM 3 counts lines upwards)"},
        "7413": {"synopsis":"Up: the line below.","comment":"Up: the line below"},
        "7414": {"synopsis":"Its 8 pixel rows copied, 32 bytes each, then its 32 attributes.","comment":"The target kept"},
        "7415": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR: HL = the source's"},
        "7418": {"comment":"DE = the target"},
        "7419": {"comment":"A = the direction"},
        "7420": {"comment":"32 bytes a row, 8 rows"},
        "7424": {"synopsis":"One pixel row.","comment":"Count and addresses kept"},
        "7427": {"comment":"BC = 32"},
        "7429": {"comment":"One row copied"},
        "7431": {"comment":"Addresses and count back"},
        "7434": {"comment":"Both one pixel row down"},
        "7436": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "7438": {"comment":"The direction and the target kept"},
        "7440": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR: the source's attributes"},
        "7443": {"comment":"DE = them"},
        "7444": {"comment":"The target's row taken, the source's attributes kept"},
        "7445": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR: the target's attributes"},
        "7448": {"comment":"DE = them"},
        "7449": {"comment":"HL = the source's attributes, the target's kept"},
        "7450": {"comment":"DE = the target's attributes"},
        "7451": {"comment":"32 attributes copied"},
        "7456": {"comment":"A = the direction"},
        "7457": {"comment":"B = the line, C = the count"},
        "7458": {"comment":"Up?"},
        "7461": {"comment":"Down: the line above"},
        "7464": {"synopsis":"Up: the next line is the one below.","comment":"Up: the line below"},
        "7465": {"synopsis":"The next, while C counts.","comment":"One fewer: more to move?"},
        "7466": {"comment":"H = the direction again"},
        "7469": {"comment":"DE = the lines given"},
        "7470": {"comment":"B = E: the freed line"},
        "7471": {"synopsis":"The freed line printed.","comment":"HL = the text"},
        "7472": {"synopsis":"Prints the 32 characters at HL on line B, from column 0 (PRINT_AT_BC), with the editor's\ncolours (SWAP_COLOURS around it); in the lower screen (TV_FLAG bit 0 set) when $EC0D bit 6\nis\nset. A 0 prints a space; codes from $90 (UDGs) are printed with bank 0 paged in.\nExit: carry; TV_FLAG as it was.","comment":"SWAP_COLOURS: the editor's colours in"},
        "7475": {"comment":"DE = the text"},
        "7476": {"comment":"TV_FLAG kept"},
        "7480": {"comment":"The lower screen ($EC0D bit 6)?"},
        "7485": {"comment":"Bit 0 off: the main screen"},
        "7489": {"comment":"Bit 0 on: the lower screen"},
        "7491": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG set; AT B,0.","comment":"TV_FLAG set"},
        "7494": {"comment":"AT B,0 (PRINT_AT_BC)"},
        "7499": {"comment":"HL = the text"},
        "7500": {"comment":"32 characters"},
        "7502": {"synopsis":"One character: 0 is a space.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "7503": {"comment":"A 0?"},
        "7506": {"comment":"A space instead"},
        "7508": {"synopsis":"From $90 up?","comment":"A UDG or a token?"},
        "7512": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A: printed"},
        "7515": {"synopsis":"The next.","comment":"The next character"},
        "7516": {"comment":"All 32?"},
        "7518": {"comment":"TV_FLAG back"},
        "7522": {"comment":"SWAP_COLOURS: the program's colours back"},
        "7525": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7527": {"synopsis":"From $90: printed with bank 0 and the machine stack, then back to bank 7.","comment":"BANK0_STACK: bank 0 and the machine stack"},
        "7530": {"comment":"Printed (RST $10), with bank 0's UDGs in place"},
        "7531": {"comment":"BANK7_STACK: bank 7 and its stack"},
        "7534": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "7536": {"synopsis":"Clears the window's lines B to D (IX + 1 added): their pixels to 0 and their attributes to\nthe editor's ATTR_P (SWAP_COLOURS around it), through ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR and\nLINE_ATTR_ADDR. Carry.","comment":"SWAP_COLOURS: the editor's colours in"},
        "7539": {"comment":"C = the number of lines"},
        "7543": {"comment":"LINE_TO_ROM3: B in ROM 3's form"},
        "7546": {"synopsis":"One line.","comment":"Line and count kept"},
        "7547": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_SCREEN_ADDR: HL = the display address"},
        "7550": {"comment":"8 pixel rows"},
        "7552": {"synopsis":"One of its 8 pixel rows.","comment":"The row's start kept"},
        "7553": {"comment":"32 bytes of 0"},
        "7556": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Cleared"},
        "7558": {"comment":"All 32?"},
        "7560": {"comment":"HL = the row's start"},
        "7561": {"comment":"The next pixel row"},
        "7562": {"comment":"All 8?"},
        "7565": {"comment":"B = 32, kept"},
        "7568": {"comment":"ROM 3's LINE_ATTR_ADDR: the line's attributes"},
        "7571": {"comment":"HL = them"},
        "7572": {"comment":"B = 32"},
        "7573": {"comment":"A = ATTR_P"},
        "7576": {"synopsis":"One attribute.","comment":"One attribute"},
        "7578": {"comment":"All 32?"},
        "7580": {"comment":"B = the line, C = the count"},
        "7581": {"comment":"One line lower (ROM 3 counts lines upwards)"},
        "7582": {"comment":"One fewer: more?"},
        "7585": {"comment":"SWAP_COLOURS: the program's colours back"},
        "7588": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7590": {"synopsis":"Line B, column C of the window in ROM 3's print-position form: C = 33 - C, then\nLINE_TO_ROM3.","comment":"C = 33 - C, the column as ROM 3 counts it"},
        "7594": {"synopsis":"B = 24 - B - (IX + 1): line B of the window as ROM 3 counts lines.\nChanges: A, B.","comment":"A = 24 - B"},
        "7597": {"comment":"Less the window's top line"},
        "7600": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "7602": {"synopsis":"HL = $5800 + 32 x B + C, the attribute address of line B, column C. Keeps BC.\nChanges: A, DE, HL.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "7603": {"comment":"DE = B x 256"},
        "7606": {"comment":"Three shifts right: DE = B x 32"},
        "7618": {"comment":"The attribute area"},
        "7621": {"comment":"BC = the column"},
        "7622": {"comment":"Plus the column and 32 x the line"},
        "7624": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "7626": {"synopsis":"Swaps ATTR_P, MASK_P, ATTR_T and MASK_T ($5C8D-$5C90) with the copies at $EC0F-$EC12, and\nP_FLAG with $EC13: the editor's colours in, or the program's back. Keeps AF, DE and HL.\nChanges: DE', HL'.","comment":"AF, HL and DE kept"},
        "7629": {"comment":"HL = ATTR_P and MASK_P"},
        "7632": {"comment":"DE = ATTR_T and MASK_T"},
        "7636": {"comment":"The alternate set for the copies"},
        "7637": {"comment":"HL, DE = the copies at $EC0F"},
        "7644": {"comment":"To the system variables"},
        "7651": {"comment":"The old values"},
        "7652": {"comment":"Kept at $EC0F"},
        "7659": {"comment":"HL = $EC13, P_FLAG's copy"},
        "7662": {"comment":"A = P_FLAG"},
        "7665": {"comment":"D = the copy"},
        "7666": {"comment":"P_FLAG kept"},
        "7667": {"comment":"The copy to P_FLAG"},
        "7671": {"comment":"DE, HL and AF back"},
        "7675": {"synopsis":"The tokenizer at $1E01 in mode 1 ($FDB6 = 1), from $0DD4: the line is walked, not written.","comment":"Mode 1: the line walked, not written"},
        "7677": {"comment":"To TOKENIZE at $1E01"},
        "7679": {"synopsis":"The tokenizer at $1E01 in mode 0 ($FDB6 = 0), from $0D91: the line is written.","comment":"Mode 0: the line written"},
        "7681": {"synopsis":"Turns the line the editor holds, read character by character ($0E27 through TOK_GET_CHAR),\ninto a BASIC line at E_LINE, keywords typed letter by letter becoming their tokens:\n1. $FDB6 = the mode; $FDB1 (characters read) and $FDB3 (written) = 0; $FDB7 = SP, for the\nreturns from deeper down; $FC9F and $FCA1 = 0 ($15E9); $FDB0 = 0; the word buffer $FDA0\nempty ($FDA9 its end).\n2. The edit line emptied (ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS, bank 0); $FDAD = 0, the state; $FDAE =\nE_LINE, the place written; $FDAB = 0.\n3. Each character's class (TOK_GET_CHAR): letters gather in the buffer; at the first\ncharacter that cannot be in a word the buffer is looked up (KEYWORD_LOOKUP) and written\nas a token or as its letters. A space in a word is kept once ($FDAB marks it), so that GO\nTO and DEF FN are found; when the two words are not one keyword the first is written as\ntext and the rest looked up again.\n4. The state: 0 between words, 1 in a word, 2 in quotes ('\"' toggles it), 4 after REM: in 2\nand 4 the characters are written as they are.\n5. Writing goes through TOK_OUT (< >, <= >= and <> joined), TOK_PUT (states) and TOK_SPACING\n(spaces around keywords dropped).\nEntry: A = the mode, from $1DFB (1: the line walked, not written, up to X_PTR) or $1DFF\n(0: the line written).\nExit: mode 0: no carry at the line's ENTER; mode 1: carry, BC = the characters read up to\nX_PTR (the smaller of read and written) or to ENTER.","comment":"$FDB6 = the mode"},
        "7684": {"comment":"$FDB1 and $FDB3 = 0: none read, none written"},
        "7693": {"comment":"$FDB7 = SP"},
        "7697": {"comment":"$FCA1 and $FC9F = 0 ($15E9)"},
        "7700": {"comment":"$FDB0 = 0: no keyword last, no space held"},
        "7705": {"comment":"The word buffer empty"},
        "7711": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack ($05AC)"},
        "7714": {"comment":"The edit line emptied (ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS)"},
        "7717": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack ($05D1)"},
        "7720": {"comment":"$FDAD = 0: between words"},
        "7725": {"comment":"$FDAE: the place to write, at E_LINE"},
        "7731": {"comment":"$FDAB = 0: no space in the word"},
        "7737": {"synopsis":"The next character: $FDB1 counted, B = it, C = its class (TOK_GET_CHAR).","comment":"One more read ($FDB1)"},
        "7744": {"comment":"B = the character, A = its class (TOK_GET_CHAR)"},
        "7747": {"comment":"C = the class"},
        "7748": {"comment":"Between words?"},
        "7753": {"comment":"No: TOK_IN_STATE"},
        "7755": {"synopsis":"State 0: a letter starts a word; anything else is written (TOK_CHAR_OUT).","comment":"Can it start a word?"},
        "7758": {"comment":"No: written as it is"},
        "7760": {"synopsis":"Into the word buffer (TOK_BUF_ADD): state 1.","comment":"Into the word buffer (TOK_BUF_ADD)"},
        "7763": {"comment":"Full?"},
        "7765": {"comment":"State 1: in a word"},
        "7770": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "7772": {"synopsis":"The buffer is full: with a space in it, TOK_SPLIT.","comment":"A space in the word?"},
        "7777": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPLIT"},
        "7780": {"synopsis":"The buffer written as text (TOK_FLUSH); state 0.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "7781": {"comment":"The word written as text (TOK_FLUSH)"},
        "7785": {"comment":"State 0"},
        "7790": {"synopsis":"The rest of the word passed as text, up to a character that ends a word (class bit 0), which\nis taken again in state 0.","comment":"Can it end a word?"},
        "7793": {"comment":"Yes: back to state 0"},
        "7795": {"comment":"No: it is written (TOK_OUT)"},
        "7799": {"comment":"The line's end: done"},
        "7800": {"comment":"One more read"},
        "7807": {"comment":"B = the next, A = its class"},
        "7810": {"comment":"C = the class"},
        "7811": {"comment":"Until one ends the word"},
        "7813": {"synopsis":"B written (TOK_OUT); at ENTER in mode 0, TOKENIZE ends with no carry.","comment":"Written (TOK_OUT)"},
        "7817": {"comment":"The line's end: done"},
        "7818": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "7820": {"synopsis":"State 1 (a word): a letter, '#' or '$' goes into the buffer; other states: written as it is.","comment":"In a word?"},
        "7822": {"comment":"No: written as it is"},
        "7824": {"comment":"The word ended?"},
        "7827": {"comment":"No: into the buffer"},
        "7829": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "7830": {"synopsis":"The word ended: looked up (KEYWORD_LOOKUP); a keyword: TOK_KEYWORD.","comment":"A keyword? (KEYWORD_LOOKUP)"},
        "7833": {"comment":"B, C = the character again"},
        "7834": {"comment":"A keyword: TOK_KEYWORD"},
        "7836": {"comment":"A space in the buffer?"},
        "7841": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPLIT"},
        "7843": {"comment":"A space ended it?"},
        "7846": {"comment":"No: the word written as text"},
        "7848": {"comment":"The space into the buffer (TOK_BUF_ADD)"},
        "7851": {"comment":"Full?"},
        "7853": {"comment":"$FDAB = the space's place"},
        "7860": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "7862": {"synopsis":"The buffer is two words and not a keyword: the first written as text, and what follows from\nthe space moved to the buffer's start, then looked up again (at the second time the space\nitself is written and dropped).","comment":"The character kept"},
        "7863": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's start"},
        "7866": {"comment":"DE = the space's place"},
        "7870": {"comment":"The space first?"},
        "7878": {"comment":"Yes: DE one on, so the space itself is written"},
        "7879": {"synopsis":"DE = the last character to write.","comment":"DE = the last character before the space"},
        "7880": {"comment":"From the first"},
        "7882": {"synopsis":"The next.","comment":"The next character"},
        "7883": {"synopsis":"One character written (TOK_OUT).","comment":"A = the character, bit 7 off"},
        "7886": {"comment":"Both places kept"},
        "7888": {"comment":"Written (TOK_OUT)"},
        "7891": {"comment":"Both places back"},
        "7893": {"comment":"Up to DE?"},
        "7901": {"comment":"The rest moved down"},
        "7905": {"comment":"HL = the buffer's start"},
        "7908": {"comment":"$FDAB = it: the space now first"},
