        "7916": {"comment":"The space was first?"},
        "7918": {"comment":"No: the rest moved down"},
        "7924": {"comment":"DE = the character after the space"},
        "7925": {"comment":"$FDAB = 0: no space in the word"},
        "7933": {"comment":"Only the space in the buffer?"},
        "7941": {"comment":"Yes: the character back, the buffer emptied"},
        "7942": {"comment":"State 0, the buffer empty"},
        "7944": {"synopsis":"One byte down, up to the one with bit 7 set; $FDA9 = the new end; looked up again.","comment":"One byte down"},
        "7948": {"comment":"The last one (bit 7)?"},
        "7952": {"comment":"$FDA9 = the new end"},
        "7955": {"comment":"Looked up again"},
        "7957": {"synopsis":"A keyword: its token written (TOK_OUT); $FDAB = 0; the state 0 unless it is 4 (after REM);\nthe buffer emptied; the character that ended the word taken again at TOK_BETWEEN.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "7958": {"comment":"The token written (TOK_OUT)"},
        "7961": {"comment":"B, C = the character again"},
        "7962": {"comment":"$FDAB = 0: no space in the word"},
        "7968": {"comment":"After REM (state 4)?"},
        "7973": {"comment":"Yes: the state kept"},
        "7975": {"synopsis":"State 0."},
        "7980": {"synopsis":"The buffer empty.","comment":"$FDA9 = the start: the buffer empty"},
        "7986": {"comment":"The ending character taken again"},
        "7989": {"synopsis":"The next character of the line ($0E27) in B, and its class in A: 6 a letter (bits 1 and 2),\n2 '#' or '$' (bit 1), 3 a space (bits 0 and 1), 1 anything else (bit 0). Bit 2: starts a\nword; bit 1: can be in one; bit 0: ends one.","comment":"A = the next character ($0E27)"},
        "7992": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "7993": {"comment":"Below '?'"},
        "7995": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_CLASS_LOW"},
        "7997": {"comment":"Made lower case"},
        "7999": {"comment":"A letter? (LOWER_TEST)"},
        "8002": {"comment":"A letter: 6"},
        "8004": {"synopsis":"1: anything else."},
        "8006": {"comment":"1: anything else"},
        "8007": {"synopsis":"Below '?': a space, '#' or '$'?","comment":"A space?"},
        "8009": {"comment":"A space: 3"},
        "8011": {"comment":"A '#'?"},
        "8013": {"comment":"A '#': 2"},
        "8015": {"comment":"Below '#': anything else"},
        "8017": {"comment":"A '$'?"},
        "8019": {"comment":"Not a $: 1"},
        "8021": {"synopsis":"2: '#' or '$'."},
        "8024": {"synopsis":"3: a space."},
        "8027": {"synopsis":"6: a letter."},
        "8030": {"synopsis":"Carry when A is a lower-case letter ('a'-'z').","comment":"Past 'z'?"},
        "8032": {"comment":"Past 'z': no carry"},
        "8033": {"comment":"From 'a' on: carry"},
        "8037": {"synopsis":"Writes the word buffer as text (TOK_SPACING for each character, up to the one with bit 7\nset) and empties it: $FDA9 = $FDA0, $FDAB = 0.","comment":"The buffer's start"},
        "8040": {"comment":"$FDA9 = it: empty"},
        "8043": {"comment":"$FDAB = 0: no space in it"},
        "8050": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"A = the character, bit 7 off"},
        "8053": {"comment":"Its place kept"},
        "8054": {"comment":"Written (TOK_SPACING)"},
        "8058": {"comment":"The last one (bit 7)?"},
        "8061": {"comment":"The last: done"},
        "8062": {"comment":"The next"},
        "8063": {"comment":"The next"},
        "8065": {"synopsis":"Adds character B to the word buffer ($FDA0-$FDA8), the last character marked with bit 7.\nExit: carry; no carry when it is full (its end at $FDA9).","comment":"HL = the buffer's end"},
        "8068": {"comment":"Full (the end at $FDA9)?"},
        "8071": {"comment":"Full?"},
        "8073": {"comment":"No: room for it"},
        "8077": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "8080": {"synopsis":"Not the first: the last one's bit 7 cleared.","comment":"The first character?"},
        "8085": {"comment":"Not the first: link it"},
        "8089": {"comment":"The first: stored at once"},
        "8091": {"synopsis":"Bit 7 off the one before.","comment":"The one before"},
        "8093": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "8097": {"synopsis":"B stored with bit 7 set; $FDA9 moved on.","comment":"B with bit 7: now the last"},
        "8101": {"comment":"$FDA9 = the new end"},
        "8105": {"comment":"Carry: added"},
        "8106": {"comment":"Carry: added"},
        "8107": {"synopsis":"Full: no carry.","comment":"No carry: full"},
        "8110": {"synopsis":"Writes A, joining a '<' or '>' with the character after it: either is held in $FDB5; then <\n> gives <> ($C9), < = gives <= ($C7), > = gives >= ($C8); otherwise the held one is written\nfirst. The rest goes to TOK_PUT.\nExit: carry; no carry at the line's end in mode 0.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "8111": {"comment":"One held in $FDB5?"},
        "8115": {"comment":"One held: TOK_OUT_PAIR"},
        "8117": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "8118": {"comment":"A '>'?"},
        "8120": {"comment":"Held"},
        "8122": {"comment":"A '<'?"},
        "8124": {"comment":"Held"},
        "8126": {"synopsis":"On to TOK_PUT.","comment":"Written (TOK_PUT)"},
        "8130": {"synopsis":"'<' or '>' held; carry.","comment":"Held"},
        "8133": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "8135": {"synopsis":"One is held: $FDB5 = 0; was it '<'?","comment":"The held one a '<'?"},
        "8137": {"comment":"Nothing held now"},
        "8142": {"comment":"A '>' was held: TOK_OUT_GT"},
        "8144": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "8145": {"comment":"A '>' after it?"},
        "8147": {"comment":"No: TOK_OUT_LT_EQ"},
        "8149": {"comment":"The <> token, $C9"},
        "8151": {"comment":"Written"},
        "8153": {"synopsis":"'<' then '='?","comment":"A '=' after it?"},
        "8155": {"comment":"No: '<' first"},
        "8157": {"comment":"The <= token, $C7"},
        "8159": {"comment":"Written"},
        "8161": {"synopsis":"'<' then something else: '<' written first.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "8162": {"comment":"The '<' written (TOK_PUT)"},
        "8164": {"comment":"The '<' written (TOK_PUT)"},
        "8167": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "8168": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "8170": {"synopsis":"'>' held: then '='?","comment":"A = the character"},
        "8171": {"comment":"A '=' after it?"},
        "8173": {"comment":"No: '>' first"},
        "8175": {"comment":"The >= token, $C8"},
        "8177": {"comment":"Written"},
        "8179": {"synopsis":"'>' then something else: '>' written first.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "8180": {"comment":"The '>' written (TOK_PUT)"},
        "8182": {"comment":"The '>' written (TOK_PUT)"},
        "8185": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "8186": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "8188": {"synopsis":"Writes A (TOK_SPACING), keeping the state: REM ($EA) makes it 4; '\"' toggles state 2 (bit 1,\nbit 0 cleared). ENTER ends the line: TOK_PUT_ENTER.","comment":"ENTER? Not written: the edit line has one"},
        "8190": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_PUT_ENTER"},
        "8192": {"comment":"REM?"},
        "8194": {"comment":"B = the character"},
        "8195": {"comment":"No: a quote?"},
        "8197": {"comment":"State 4: after REM"},
        "8202": {"comment":"Written"},
        "8204": {"synopsis":"A quote?","comment":"A '\"'?"},
        "8206": {"comment":"No: written as it is"},
        "8208": {"comment":"The state's bit 0 off, bit 1 toggled"},
        "8218": {"synopsis":"Written; carry.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "8219": {"comment":"Written (TOK_SPACING)"},
        "8222": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "8223": {"comment":"Carry: on"},
        "8224": {"synopsis":"ENTER: in mode 0 no carry (the line done); in mode 1 BC = $FDB1, SP = $FDB7 and a return\nfrom TOKENIZE with carry.","comment":"Mode 0?"},
        "8229": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "8231": {"comment":"BC = the characters read"},
        "8235": {"comment":"SP as TOKENIZE found it"},
        "8239": {"comment":"Carry, back to TOKENIZE's caller"},
        "8240": {"comment":"Back to TOKENIZE's caller"},
        "8241": {"synopsis":"No carry.","comment":"No carry"},
        "8243": {"comment":"Back to the caller"},
        "8244": {"synopsis":"Writes A (TOK_WRITE), dropping the spaces around keywords, with the flags in $FDB0 (bit 0: a\nkeyword was the last written; bit 1: a space held back): a space after a keyword is dropped;\nof a run of spaces the last is held; a keyword ($A3 and up) drops a held space; any other\ncharacter writes the held one first.","comment":"E = the character"},
        "8245": {"comment":"D = the flags"},
        "8250": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "8252": {"comment":"No: TOK_SPACING_CHR"},
        "8254": {"comment":"After a keyword?"},
        "8257": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPACE_AFTER"},
        "8259": {"comment":"One held already?"},
        "8262": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPACE_HELD"},
        "8264": {"comment":"Held: bit 1 set, nothing written"},
        "8271": {"synopsis":"A space held already: this one written.","comment":"This one written (TOK_WRITE)"},
        "8275": {"comment":"A = the flags"},
        "8278": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8279": {"synopsis":"After a keyword: dropped.","comment":"Bit 0 off: the space dropped"},
        "8286": {"synopsis":"Not a space: a keyword ($A3 up)?","comment":"A keyword?"},
        "8288": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPACING_KEY"},
        "8290": {"comment":"A space held?"},
        "8293": {"comment":"Yes: TOK_SPACE_FIRST"},
        "8295": {"comment":"No: bit 0 off"},
        "8301": {"comment":"The character written (TOK_WRITE)"},
        "8306": {"synopsis":"The held space written first, then the character; both flags cleared.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "8307": {"comment":"The held space written (TOK_WRITE)"},
        "8312": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "8313": {"comment":"Both bits off"},
        "8321": {"comment":"Then the character"},
        "8326": {"synopsis":"A keyword: a held space dropped, bit 0 set; written.","comment":"Bit 1 off (the held space dropped), bit 0 on"},
        "8334": {"comment":"The token written (TOK_WRITE)"},
        "8339": {"synopsis":"Writes A at the place in $FDAE and moves it on ($FDB3 counted). Mode 0: one byte of room\nopened there (ROOM_TEST_BC, ROM 3's MOVE_POINTERS, the bytes above moved up) and A stored.\nMode 1: nothing written, the place moved past the byte there (and past a hidden number after\n$0E); when the place is X_PTR, BC = the smaller of $FDB1 and $FDB3, SP = $FDB7 and a return\nfrom TOKENIZE with carry.","comment":"One more written ($FDB3)"},
        "8346": {"comment":"HL = the place"},
        "8349": {"comment":"B = the character"},
        "8350": {"comment":"Mode 0?"},
        "8355": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "8356": {"comment":"Mode 0: TOK_WRITE_ZERO"},
        "8358": {"comment":"At X_PTR?"},
        "8364": {"comment":"No: TOK_FIND_ON"},
        "8368": {"comment":"No: TOK_FIND_ON"},
        "8370": {"comment":"BC = the characters read"},
        "8374": {"comment":"Fewer written than read?"},
        "8380": {"comment":"No: BC = the characters read"},
        "8382": {"comment":"Then BC = the characters written"},
        "8386": {"synopsis":"SP back: out of TOKENIZE, carry.","comment":"SP as TOKENIZE found it"},
        "8390": {"comment":"Carry, back to TOKENIZE's caller"},
        "8391": {"comment":"Back to TOKENIZE's caller"},
        "8392": {"synopsis":"Mode 1: carry.","comment":"Carry: mode 1"},
        "8395": {"synopsis":"Mode 0: no carry.","comment":"No carry: mode 0"},
        "8397": {"synopsis":"Bank 0 and the machine stack.","comment":"Bank 0 and the machine stack ($05AC; carry kept)"},
        "8400": {"comment":"Mode 0?"},
        "8402": {"comment":"A = the byte at the place"},
        "8403": {"comment":"DE = the place"},
        "8404": {"comment":"A hidden number?"},
        "8406": {"comment":"No: past the byte"},
        "8408": {"comment":"DE past its five bytes"},
        "8413": {"comment":"Then past the byte"},
        "8415": {"synopsis":"Mode 0: room for one byte at HL, then A stored there.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "8416": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "8419": {"comment":"HL and DE kept"},
        "8421": {"comment":"Room for it? (ROOM_TEST_BC; report 4 if not)"},
        "8424": {"comment":"DE and HL back"},
        "8426": {"comment":"Pointers moved (ROM 3's MOVE_POINTERS)"},
        "8429": {"comment":"The bytes up to STKEND moved up"},
        "8432": {"comment":"DE = the new STKEND, HL = the old"},
        "8435": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "8436": {"comment":"Stored at the place"},
        "8437": {"synopsis":"$FDAE = the next place; bank 7.","comment":"DE = the next place"},
        "8438": {"comment":"Bank 7 and its stack ($05D1)"},
        "8441": {"comment":"$FDAE = it"},
        "8445": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8446": {"synopsis":"Whether BC bytes fit between STKEND and the stack, with $82 bytes to spare; returns with\ncarry when they do. Otherwise ERR_NR = 3 and REPORT_4_ROOM (report 4, \"Out of memory\").","comment":"HL = STKEND + BC"},
        "8450": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "8452": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "8453": {"comment":"Plus $82 to spare"},
        "8457": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "8459": {"comment":"Below SP?"},
        "8461": {"comment":"Yes: carry, they fit"},
        "8462": {"synopsis":"No room: ERR_NR = 3 (report 4), then ROM 1's $2739 through $3E80, which calls the ROM 1\nroutine whose address is the word after the CALL.","comment":"ERR_NR = 3: report 4"},
        "8467": {"comment":"To ROM 1's $2739 (the word after the CALL)"},
        "8472": {"synopsis":"Looks the word in the buffer at $FDA0 up as a keyword, letters in either case:\n1. $1432 copies the RAM routines to $FCAE again ($E8 bytes from $1447), clearing $FC9F and\n$FCA1.\n2. ROM 3's keywords: the RAM routine at $FD43 (the copy of $14DC) pages ROM 3 in and looks\nthrough its list at $0096, codes from $A5.\n3. Then this ROM's list at $1693 (the RAM routine at $FD5C, the copy of $14F5, B = $F9):\nSPECTRUM, PLAY, GOTO, GOSUB, DEFFN, OPEN#, CLOSE# (the spellings as stored there), which\ngive $A3, $A4, $EC (GO TO), $ED (GO SUB), $CE (DEF FN), $D3 (OPEN #), $D4 (CLOSE #).\nExit: carry and A = the token when found; no carry otherwise.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The RAM routines copied to $FCAE again ($1432)"},
        "8475": {"comment":"ROM 3's keywords (the RAM routine at $FD43)"},
        "8478": {"comment":"Found: carry, A = the token"},
        "8479": {"comment":"The 128K's own list, codes from $F9"},
        "8481": {"comment":"DE = the word"},
        "8484": {"comment":"HL = the 128K's list"},
        "8487": {"comment":"Looked up (the RAM routine at $FD5C)"},
        "8490": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "8491": {"comment":"$FF: CLOSE # ($D4)?"},
        "8493": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FF"},
        "8495": {"comment":"The CLOSE # token"},
        "8497": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8499": {"synopsis":"$FE: OPEN # ($D3)?"},
        "8501": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FE"},
        "8503": {"comment":"The OPEN # token"},
        "8505": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8507": {"synopsis":"$FD: DEF FN ($CE)?"},
        "8509": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FD"},
        "8511": {"comment":"The DEF FN token"},
        "8513": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8515": {"synopsis":"$FC: GO SUB ($ED)?"},
        "8517": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FC"},
        "8519": {"comment":"The GO SUB token"},
        "8521": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8523": {"synopsis":"$FB: GO TO ($EC)?"},
        "8525": {"comment":"No: KW_NOT_FB"},
        "8527": {"comment":"The GO TO token"},
        "8529": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8531": {"synopsis":"$F9 or $FA: less $56 (SPECTRUM $A3, PLAY $A4).","comment":"$A3 SPECTRUM or $A4 PLAY"},
        "8533": {"synopsis":"Carry: found."},
        "8534": {"comment":"Back with the token"},
        "8535": {"synopsis":"Copies the bytes at HL, a count first, to DE.\nExit: HL and DE past them; B = 0.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "8537": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Copied"},
        "8539": {"comment":"Both on"},
        "8541": {"comment":"All?"},
        "8543": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8544": {"synopsis":"Carry and A = its value when A is a digit '0'-'9'; no carry otherwise. Nothing in this ROM\ncalls it.","comment":"Below '0'?"},
        "8547": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "8548": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "8550": {"comment":"Yes: no carry"},
        "8551": {"comment":"A = its value"},
        "8553": {"comment":"Carry: a digit"},
        "8555": {"synopsis":"Looks key A up in the table at HL (a count, then code and address per key) and runs the\nroutine found.\nExit: no carry and NZ when not found; Z when found, carry as the routine\nreturned it.","comment":"BC and DE kept"},
        "8557": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "8559": {"synopsis":"The next entry: its code compared with A.","comment":"This key?"},
        "8560": {"comment":"DE = the entry's address"},
        "8564": {"comment":"Yes: TABLE_FOUND"},
        "8566": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8567": {"comment":"The next"},
        "8569": {"comment":"Not found: no carry"},
        "8571": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "8574": {"synopsis":"Found: the routine run (TABLE_CALL), Z, its carry kept.","comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "8575": {"comment":"DE and BC back"},
        "8577": {"comment":"Run (TABLE_CALL)"},
        "8580": {"comment":"It returned carry?"},
        "8582": {"comment":"Z and no carry"},
        "8584": {"synopsis":"The routine returned carry: Z and carry.","comment":"Z"},
        "8585": {"comment":"And carry"},
        "8587": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL."},
        "8588": {"synopsis":"The routine ROM 2 reaches through this ROM's $3FF0 (its ASK_RETRY's hook): prints a message\nin the lower screen and waits for a key:\n1. With Z, DE is the list of keys to take ($FF at its end); with NZ any key (DE = 0).\n2. Stream -3 ($FD, the lower screen) selected (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT).\n3. The message wrapped to 32 columns: in a stretch of 32 characters without its end, the\nlast space becomes ENTER (the message is changed where it is).\n4. AT 0,0 and the message printed.\n5. Keys read ($1876) until one in the list comes.\n6. ROM 3's CLS_LOWER, and stream -2 ($FE, the upper screen) selected.\nEntry: HL = the message ($FF at its end); DE = the keys, when Z is set.\nExit: A = the key; 0 when there was no list. HL = the list.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Z: DE is the list of keys"},
        "8590": {"comment":"NZ: no list, any key"},
        "8593": {"synopsis":"The list kept, then the message.","comment":"The list kept"},
        "8594": {"comment":"The message kept"},
        "8595": {"comment":"Stream -3: the lower screen"},
        "8597": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "8600": {"comment":"HL = the message"},
        "8602": {"synopsis":"A stretch of up to 32 characters from HL.","comment":"B = 32: one screen line"},
        "8604": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"A space?"},
        "8607": {"comment":"No: DE kept"},
        "8609": {"comment":"DE = the last space so far"},
        "8611": {"synopsis":"The message's end?","comment":"The message's end?"},
        "8613": {"comment":"Yes: the message fits"},
        "8615": {"comment":"The next, up to 32"},
        "8616": {"comment":"Up to 32"},
        "8618": {"comment":"No end in 32: the last space becomes ENTER"},
        "8622": {"comment":"The next stretch from there"},
        "8624": {"synopsis":"AT 0,0, then the message.","comment":"AT 0,0"},
        "8626": {"comment":"AT"},
        "8629": {"comment":"Row 0"},
        "8632": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "8633": {"comment":"HL = the message"},
        "8634": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"Its end?"},
        "8637": {"comment":"Yes: a key"},
        "8639": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8641": {"comment":"The next"},
        "8643": {"synopsis":"A key ($1876); with a list, one in it.","comment":"A key ($1876)"},
        "8646": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "8647": {"comment":"HL = the list"},
        "8648": {"comment":"No list? Any key, A = 0"},
        "8651": {"comment":"No list: done"},
        "8653": {"synopsis":"The next key in the list.","comment":"The list's key the one pressed?"},
        "8655": {"comment":"Found: done"},
        "8657": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8658": {"comment":"The list's end? Then another key"},
        "8660": {"comment":"Not the end: the next"},
        "8662": {"comment":"Another key"},
        "8664": {"synopsis":"The key taken: the lower screen cleared, the upper screen's stream again.","comment":"The key kept"},
        "8665": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_LOWER"},
        "8668": {"comment":"Stream -2: the upper screen"},
        "8670": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "8673": {"comment":"A = the key, HL = the list"},
        "8676": {"synopsis":"The start of a program that tests the machine's hardware; no call or jump in this ROM's\ncode reaches it. Each check shifts one bit into IX at bit 0 (TEST_RESULT_BIT), 1 for a pass:\n1. Interrupts off, IX = $FFFF, border white, SP = $7FFF; $2904 first.\n2. The screen cleared, INK 7 and PAPER 0, the text at $326E, 40 frames waited.\n3. Border green and the RAM test: banks 0-7 filled with D = $00; each byte checked and\nmade its complement, banks 0 up; each checked and given D again, from $FFFF of bank 7\ndown; the same again with D = $FF. A byte that differs: RAM_FAIL.\n4. Then BANK_ID_TEST.","comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "8677": {"comment":"IX: the results, one bit per check"},
        "8681": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "8683": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "8685": {"comment":"The stack below $8000"},
        "8688": {"comment":"First $2904"},
        "8691": {"comment":"Interrupts off, border white"},
        "8696": {"comment":"Screen cleared, plain colours (TEST_CLS)"},
        "8699": {"comment":"INK 7, PAPER 0"},
        "8705": {"comment":"The text at $326E"},
        "8711": {"comment":"40 frames (WAIT_40_FRAMES)"},
        "8714": {"comment":"Border green: the RAM test"},
        "8716": {"comment":"Border green"},
        "8718": {"comment":"Two passes; D = $00, the pattern"},
        "8721": {"synopsis":"One pass with pattern D: every bank filled with it.","comment":"Bank 0 first"},
        "8723": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "8726": {"synopsis":"Bank A filled with D, $C000-$FFFF.","comment":"Bank A paged in at $C000"},
        "8728": {"comment":"The bank number aside"},
        "8729": {"comment":"From $C000"},
        "8732": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"The pattern"},
        "8733": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "8736": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "8738": {"comment":"The next bank, up to 7"},
        "8742": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "8744": {"comment":"Bank 0 again"},
        "8746": {"synopsis":"Bank A checked upwards: each byte must be D, then is made its complement.","comment":"Paged in"},
        "8748": {"comment":"The number aside"},
        "8749": {"comment":"From $C000"},
        "8752": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Still the pattern? If not, RAM_FAIL"},
        "8754": {"comment":"No: RAM_FAIL"},
        "8756": {"comment":"Its complement written"},
        "8758": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "8761": {"comment":"Up to $FFFF"},
        "8763": {"comment":"The next bank, up to 7"},
        "8767": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "8769": {"comment":"From bank 7 down"},
        "8770": {"synopsis":"Bank A checked from the top down: each byte must be D's complement, then is D again.","comment":"The number aside; HL from $FFFF down"},
        "8774": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Down one; below $C000?"},
        "8778": {"comment":"Yes: the next bank"},
        "8780": {"comment":"Still the complement? If not, RAM_FAIL"},
        "8783": {"comment":"No: RAM_FAIL"},
        "8785": {"comment":"The pattern again"},
        "8786": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "8788": {"synopsis":"The next bank down.","comment":"Bank 0 done?"},
        "8791": {"comment":"Yes: the pass ends"},
        "8793": {"comment":"The bank below"},
        "8794": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "8796": {"comment":"And checked"},
        "8798": {"synopsis":"The pass's end: a second one with D = $FF, then BANK_ID_TEST.","comment":"Both passes done? On to BANK_ID_TEST"},
        "8799": {"comment":"Both: BANK_ID_TEST"},
        "8802": {"comment":"The second pass with $FF"},
        "8804": {"comment":"Again"},
        "8807": {"synopsis":"A RAM byte did not hold its value: the start-up run again (TEST_REINIT), bank 0, INK 7 and\nPAPER 0, the screen cleared and \"RAM fail: address hhhh, page n\" printed, HL being the\naddress and A' the bank, in hex; then the machine stops (interrupts off and HALT).\nBANK_ID_FAIL comes here too, with HL = 0.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "8808": {"comment":"Bank and address kept"},
        "8810": {"comment":"The start-up again (TEST_REINIT)"},
        "8813": {"comment":"Bank 0, paging byte 0"},
        "8820": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "8822": {"comment":"INK 7, PAPER 0"},
        "8828": {"comment":"Screen cleared (TEST_CLS)"},
        "8831": {"comment":"'RAM fail: address '"},
        "8837": {"comment":"The address"},
        "8838": {"comment":"Its high byte in hex (TEST_HEX_A)"},
        "8839": {"comment":"Its high byte"},
        "8842": {"comment":"Its low byte"},
        "8846": {"comment":"The main registers aside"},
        "8847": {"comment":"', page '"},
        "8853": {"comment":"The bank, 0-7"},
        "8856": {"comment":"In hex"},
        "8860": {"comment":"Stopped for good"},
        "8861": {"comment":"For good"},
        "8862": {"synopsis":"Prints A as two hex digits (HEX_DIGITS, TEST_PRINT_A), the alternate DE and HL used for\nthe lookup.\nChanges: AF, B, the alternate DE and HL.","comment":"HL and A kept"},
        "8865": {"comment":"The high digit"},
        "8873": {"comment":"Two digits"},
        "8875": {"synopsis":"One digit.","comment":"DE = the digit (alternate set)"},
        "8879": {"comment":"Its character from HEX_DIGITS"},
        "8884": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8887": {"comment":"Then the low digit"},
        "8891": {"comment":"Both?"},
        "8893": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "8894": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8895": {"synopsis":"RAM_FAIL's text: AT 10,0, \"RAM fail: address \", $FF at its end."},
        "8917": {"synopsis":"No call or jump in this ROM's code reaches it. Border black, the picture cleared, then for\never each attribute from $5800 to $5AFF made of three samples of the EAR input (port $FE\nbit 6) shifted into C.","comment":"Border black"},
        "8919": {"comment":"Border black"},
        "8921": {"comment":"The picture cleared, $4000-$57FF"},
        "8934": {"synopsis":"Again from $5800.","comment":"From the first attribute"},
        "8937": {"synopsis":"One attribute.","comment":"Three samples, C = 0"},
        "8940": {"synopsis":"One sample.","comment":"The EAR bit"},
        "8944": {"comment":"Into C, shifted on"},
        "8948": {"comment":"Timing"},
        "8952": {"comment":"Three?"},
        "8954": {"comment":"The attribute"},
        "8956": {"comment":"Past $5AFF?"},
        "8959": {"comment":"No: the next attribute"},
        "8961": {"comment":"For ever"},
        "8963": {"synopsis":"RAM_FAIL's \", page \", $FF at its end."},
        "8971": {"synopsis":"The 16 hex digits, \"0123456789ABCDEF\", for TEST_HEX_A."},
        "8987": {"synopsis":"PAGING_RESULT's text: AT 10,0, \"RAM test passed\", $FF at its end."},
        "9006": {"synopsis":"Checks that the eight banks are eight: each gets its number at $CAFE, banks 0 up; then from\n7 down each must still hold its own (BANK_ID_FAIL if not). Then each bank's number goes to\n$E000, PAGE_ROM_TEST is copied to $D000 in banks 7 and 3 (COPY_PAGE_TEST) and run there\nwith bank 3 paged in.","comment":"Bank 0 first; HL = $CAFE"},
        "9011": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "9014": {"synopsis":"Its number written.","comment":"Bank A paged in"},
        "9016": {"comment":"Its number at $CAFE"},
        "9017": {"comment":"The next, up to 7"},
        "9020": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "9022": {"synopsis":"Bank A - 1 checked, from 7 down.","comment":"The bank below paged in"},
        "9023": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9025": {"comment":"Its number still there?"},
        "9026": {"comment":"No: BANK_ID_FAIL"},
        "9029": {"comment":"Bank 0 done?"},
        "9030": {"comment":"No: the next one down"},
        "9032": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "9036": {"comment":"Bank 0 first"},
        "9038": {"synopsis":"Its number at $E000.","comment":"Bank A paged in"},
        "9040": {"comment":"Its number at $E000"},
        "9043": {"comment":"The next, up to 7"},
        "9046": {"comment":"All eight?"},
        "9048": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "9049": {"comment":"The ROM test copied into it"},
        "9052": {"comment":"And into bank 3"},
        "9057": {"comment":"Run there, bank 3 paged in"},
        "9060": {"synopsis":"Pages bank A in at $C000 and copies PAGE_ROM_TEST ($B9 bytes from $2375) to $D000 in it.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Bank A paged in"},
        "9063": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9065": {"comment":"PAGE_ROM_TEST to $D000, $B9 bytes"},
        "9076": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9077": {"synopsis":"Runs at $D000, copied there in banks 3 and 7 by COPY_PAGE_TEST (its calls of $D08E and\n$D09B are RESULT_BIT_RAM and ROM_SUM; SPECIAL_BANKS is read at $D0A9):\n1. The four all-RAM configurations of port $1FFD (1, 3, 5, 7): the bytes at $2000, $6000,\n$A000 and $E000, where BANK_ID_TEST put each bank's number, must give SPECIAL_BANKS;\nD = 1 when all do, 0 when one does not, kept in the alternate set.\n2. The ROMs summed (ROM_SUM): ROM 0 and ROM 1 together give one result bit; then with\n$1FFD = 4, two more sums give another.\n3. Normal paging back, ROM 0, the copies at $5B5C and $5B67 = 0, and on at PAGING_RESULT.","comment":"Configuration 0, all-RAM paging on"},
        "9079": {"comment":"DE = SPECIAL_BANKS (its copy at $D0A9)"},
        "9082": {"comment":"HL = $2000, in the first quarter"},
        "9085": {"synopsis":"One configuration of port $1FFD.","comment":"The configuration set (port $1FFD)"},
        "9088": {"comment":"All-RAM configuration A"},
        "9090": {"comment":"Kept aside"},
        "9091": {"comment":"BC = $4000: a quarter"},
        "9094": {"synopsis":"One quarter: its byte must be the bank number expected.","comment":"The bank expected here"},
        "9096": {"comment":"The number BANK_ID_TEST wrote?"},
        "9097": {"comment":"No: SPECIAL_FAIL"},
        "9099": {"comment":"The next quarter, up to $E000"},
        "9100": {"comment":"Until past $FFFF"},
        "9102": {"comment":"The next configuration: 3, 5, 7"},
        "9105": {"comment":"All four?"},
        "9107": {"comment":"No: the next configuration"},
        "9109": {"comment":"D = 1: all right"},
        "9111": {"comment":"On to the ROMs"},
        "9113": {"synopsis":"A wrong bank: D = 0.","comment":"D = 0: a wrong bank"},
        "9116": {"synopsis":"The ROM checksums.","comment":"D into the alternate set"},
        "9117": {"comment":"Bank 3 and ROM 0 ($7FFD = 3, $1FFD = 0)"},
        "9122": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9127": {"comment":"Normal paging, ROM 0"},
        "9129": {"comment":"ROM 0 sums to 0? (ROM_SUM)"},
        "9132": {"comment":"No: ROM_LOW_BAD"},
        "9134": {"comment":"ROM 1: $7FFD = $13"},
        "9139": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9141": {"comment":"Sums to 0?"},
        "9144": {"comment":"No: ROM_LOW_BAD"},
        "9146": {"comment":"Both: a 1 result bit"},
        "9147": {"comment":"Carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9150": {"synopsis":"The second pair of sums, $1FFD bit 2 set.","comment":"$1FFD = 4"},
        "9155": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9157": {"comment":"$7FFD = 3: ROM 2"},
        "9162": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9164": {"comment":"Sums to 0?"},
        "9167": {"comment":"No: ROM_HIGH_BAD"},
        "9169": {"comment":"$7FFD = $0B: still ROM 2 (bit 4 clear)"},
        "9174": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9176": {"comment":"Sums to 0?"},
        "9179": {"comment":"No: ROM_HIGH_BAD"},
        "9181": {"comment":"Both: a 1 result bit"},
        "9182": {"comment":"Carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9185": {"synopsis":"Normal paging again, ROM 0; the copies of both ports 0; on in ROM 0.","comment":"$7FFD = 3"},
        "9192": {"comment":"$1FFD = 0: ROM 0"},
        "9198": {"comment":"The copies at $5B5C and $5B67 = 0"},
        "9204": {"comment":"On in ROM 0"},
        "9207": {"synopsis":"ROM 0 or 1 did not sum to 0: a 0 bit; on to the second pair.","comment":"A 0 result bit"},
        "9208": {"comment":"No carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9211": {"comment":"The second pair"},
        "9213": {"synopsis":"The second pair failed: a 0 bit.","comment":"A 0 result bit"},
        "9214": {"comment":"No carry in (RESULT_BIT_RAM)"},
        "9217": {"comment":"Normal paging again"},
        "9219": {"synopsis":"PAGE_ROM_TEST's copy of TEST_RESULT_BIT (at $D08E): the carry shifted into IX at bit 0.\nKeeps DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "9220": {"comment":"DE = IX"},
        "9223": {"comment":"Carry in at bit 0, the rest up one"},
        "9227": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "9231": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9232": {"synopsis":"Runs at $D09B: adds up the 16K at $0000-$3FFF, the ROM paged in, in A (modulo 256).\nExit: Z when the sum is 0.\nChanges: A, D, HL.","comment":"A = 0, HL = 0"},
        "9235": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Added"},
        "9237": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9238": {"comment":"Up to $3FFF?"},
        "9242": {"comment":"No: the next byte"},
        "9244": {"comment":"Z when 0"},
        "9246": {"synopsis":"The banks PAGE_ROM_TEST expects at $0000, $4000, $8000 and $C000 in the four all-RAM\nconfigurations: 0 1 2 3, 4 5 6 7, 4 5 6 3, 4 7 6 3 (read at $D0A9)."},
        "9262": {"synopsis":"Shifts the carry into IX at bit 0, the rest up one: each check's result, carry for a pass.\nKeeps DE.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "9263": {"comment":"DE = IX"},
        "9266": {"comment":"Carry in at bit 0, the rest up one"},
        "9270": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "9275": {"synopsis":"Back in ROM 0 after PAGE_ROM_TEST: bank 0, SP = $7FFF, the configurations' result (D = 1) as\na\nbit; the start-up run again, \"RAM test passed\" shown for 40 frames; then TEST_SEQUENCE.","comment":"Bank 0, ROM 0"},
        "9280": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "9282": {"comment":"The stack again"},
        "9285": {"comment":"D = the configurations' result"},
        "9286": {"comment":"Carry when D is 1"},
        "9288": {"comment":"The result bit"},
        "9291": {"comment":"The start-up again (TEST_REINIT)"},
        "9294": {"comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "9297": {"comment":"'RAM test passed'"},
        "9303": {"comment":"40 frames"},
        "9306": {"comment":"The other tests"},
        "9308": {"synopsis":"A bank did not hold its number: the start-up run again (TEST_REINIT), then RAM_FAIL with\nHL = 0.","comment":"The start-up again (TEST_REINIT)"},
        "9311": {"comment":"AF swapped, as RAM_FAIL swaps it back"},
        "9312": {"comment":"Address 0"},
        "9315": {"comment":"Reported (RAM_FAIL)"},
        "9318": {"synopsis":"The other tests in turn: $2CA6, $28C3, $296A, KEYBOARD_TEST, $2C2C, $2C7B, $29DD, $2B31,\n$2A58, PRINTER_TEST, $3565 and $35B0, then on at $2B9E.","comment":"Each test in turn"},
        "9321": {"comment":"$28C3"},
        "9324": {"comment":"$296A"},
        "9327": {"comment":"The keys (KEYBOARD_TEST)"},
        "9330": {"comment":"$2C2C"},
        "9333": {"comment":"$2C7B"},
        "9336": {"comment":"$29DD"},
        "9339": {"comment":"$2B31"},
        "9342": {"comment":"$2A58"},
        "9345": {"comment":"The printer (PRINTER_TEST)"},
        "9348": {"comment":"$3565"},
        "9351": {"comment":"$35B0"},
        "9354": {"comment":"Then $2B9E"},
        "9357": {"synopsis":"Tests the printer port:\n1. BUSY: with the printer turned off line (a key waited for), bit 0 of port $0FFD must be\n1; turned on line, 0. One result bit.\n2. Data: bit 4 set in $5B67 (the strobe's resting level); characters $20-$7F and $A0-$FF\nsent twice (PRN_COUNTED, an ENTER after each 72), Q stopping it; then ENTER (a pass) or\nSPACE asked for: another bit.","comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "9360": {"comment":"'Printer BUSY signal test'"},
        "9366": {"comment":"'Turn the printer '"},
        "9372": {"comment":"'OFFLINE'"},
        "9378": {"comment":"'Press any key to continue'"},
        "9384": {"comment":"A key (WAIT_NEW_KEY)"},
        "9387": {"comment":"Port $0FFD: BUSY in bit 0"},
        "9392": {"comment":"Busy while off line? If not, a fail"},
        "9394": {"comment":"Not busy: BUSY_FAIL"},
        "9396": {"comment":"'ONLINE ' over it"},
        "9402": {"comment":"A key"},
        "9405": {"comment":"Port $0FFD again"},
        "9410": {"comment":"Not busy now?"},
        "9412": {"comment":"Busy: BUSY_FAIL"},
        "9414": {"comment":"Carry: a pass"},
        "9417": {"synopsis":"BUSY wrong: no carry.","comment":"No carry: a fail"},
        "9419": {"synopsis":"The BUSY result into IX; then the data test.","comment":"The result bit"},
        "9422": {"comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "9425": {"comment":"Strobe bit 4 set in the $1FFD copy"},
        "9430": {"comment":"'Printer data test'"},
        "9436": {"comment":"The instructions, two lines"},
        "9442": {"comment":"E = 0: the column"},
        "9444": {"comment":"Two passes"},
        "9446": {"synopsis":"The next pass.","comment":"Both done? The question"},
        "9447": {"comment":"Yes: PRN_ASK_OK"},
        "9449": {"comment":"From a space"},
        "9451": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"Count and character kept"},
        "9453": {"comment":"Sent (PRN_COUNTED)"},
        "9458": {"comment":"The next; past $7F?"},
        "9461": {"comment":"Yes: on from $A0"},
        "9463": {"comment":"Past $FF (0)? The next pass"},
        "9464": {"comment":"Yes: the next pass"},
        "9466": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "9468": {"synopsis":"$80-$9F skipped.","comment":"From $A0"},
        "9470": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "9472": {"synopsis":"Sends A to the printer (PRN_SEND) and counts it in E; after 72 an ENTER too, E = 0.\nKeeps A.","comment":"Sent (PRN_SEND)"},
        "9476": {"comment":"One more in the line"},
        "9477": {"comment":"72?"},
        "9480": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "9482": {"comment":"E = 0; an ENTER sent"},
        "9489": {"synopsis":"A back.","comment":"A back"},
        "9491": {"synopsis":"Sends A to the printer: waits while bit 0 of port $0FFD (BUSY) is 1, Q giving up (PRN_QUIT);\nA out to port $0FFD; then a strobe pulse on port $1FFD bit 4, from the copy at $5B67\n(cleared, then set again), with interrupts off.\nChanges: A, BC.","comment":"A kept"},
        "9492": {"synopsis":"Waiting while the printer is busy.","comment":"Q down? Then the printing stops"},
        "9494": {"comment":"Half-row $FBFE"},
        "9497": {"comment":"Q down: PRN_QUIT"},
        "9499": {"comment":"BUSY?"},
        "9502": {"comment":"Port $0FFD"},
        "9506": {"comment":"Busy: wait"},
        "9508": {"comment":"The byte out to port $0FFD"},
        "9511": {"comment":"Interrupts off for the pulse"},
        "9512": {"comment":"A = the $1FFD copy, strobe bit set"},
        "9515": {"synopsis":"The strobe bit toggled out: low, then high again.","comment":"Strobe bit toggled out"},
        "9520": {"comment":"Out to port $1FFD"},
        "9522": {"comment":"Low now? Then back high"},
        "9526": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "9527": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9528": {"synopsis":"Q stops the printing: five words dropped (PRN_SEND's AF and return, PRN_COUNTED's return,\nthe loop's AF and BC), then PRN_ASK_OK.","comment":"Five words off the stack"},
        "9533": {"synopsis":"Asks whether the characters printed well: ENTER (carry) or SPACE (TEST_ENTER_SPACE); the\nanswer is the result bit.","comment":"'If characters printed OK, ...'"},
        "9539": {"comment":"ENTER: carry; SPACE: none"},
        "9542": {"comment":"The result bit"},
        "9545": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9546": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key: FLAGS bit 5 cleared, waited for until the interrupt sets it, cleared again.\nChanges: HL.","comment":"FLAGS"},
        "9549": {"comment":"No new key"},
        "9551": {"synopsis":"Until bit 5 is set.","comment":"A key yet?"},
        "9553": {"comment":"No: wait"},
        "9555": {"comment":"Taken"},
        "9557": {"comment":"Done"},
        "9558": {"synopsis":"AT 4,4, \"Printer data test\", $FF at its end."},
        "9579": {"synopsis":"AT 8,1, \"Make sure printer is ready\", AT 10,1, \"Press Q to quit printing\", $FF."},
        "9636": {"synopsis":"AT 12,1, \"If characters printed OK,\", ENTER, \"Press [ENTER], otherwise [SPACE]\",\n$FF at its end."},
        "9698": {"synopsis":"OVER 0, AT 4,4, \"Printer BUSY signal test\", $FF at its end."},
        "9728": {"synopsis":"AT 8,8, \"Turn the printer \", $FF at its end."},
        "9749": {"synopsis":"AT 10,12, \"ONLINE \", $FF at its end."},
        "9760": {"synopsis":"AT 10,12, \"OFFLINE\", $FF at its end."},
        "9771": {"synopsis":"AT 12,4, \"Press any key to continue\", $FF at its end."},
        "9800": {"synopsis":"AT 16,5, \"Passed - press [ENTER]\", $FF at its end. No LD in this ROM's code points at it."},
        "9826": {"synopsis":"AT 16,5, \"Failed - press [SPACE]\", $FF at its end. No LD in this ROM's code points at it."},
        "9852": {"synopsis":"Runs the start-up again from $016C (the routines at $5B00, the system variables and so on)\nwith A' = 'R' ($52), which makes it end at TEST_RESTARTED instead; the stack is kept, as the\nstart-up from $016C does not set SP, so the RET there comes back to this routine's caller.\nChanges: all registers.","comment":"'R': back by TEST_RESTARTED"},
        "9855": {"comment":"The start-up from $016C"},
        "9858": {"synopsis":"Where the start-up goes on when A' is 'R' (from $0261): stream 2 selected (ROM 3's\nSTREAM_SELECT), then COLOUR_RESET, whose RET goes back to TEST_REINIT's caller.","comment":"Stream 2: the upper screen"},
        "9860": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "9863": {"synopsis":"Prints COLOUR_RESET_SEQ: INK 0, PAPER 7, BRIGHT, INVERSE, OVER and FLASH 0.","comment":"INK 0, PAPER 7, the rest 0"},
        "9866": {"comment":"Printed (TEST_PRINT_TEXT)"},
        "9870": {"synopsis":"COLOUR_RESET's codes: INK 0, PAPER 7, BRIGHT 0, INVERSE 0, OVER 0, FLASH 0, then $FF."},
        "9883": {"synopsis":"Waits 25 frames (HALT with interrupts on), then interrupts off. No call or jump in this\nROM's code reaches it.\nKeeps BC, HL.","comment":"BC and HL kept"},
        "9885": {"comment":"25 frames"},
        "9887": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "9888": {"synopsis":"One frame.","comment":"One frame"},
        "9889": {"comment":"25 of them"},
        "9893": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "9895": {"synopsis":"Waits 40 frames (HALT with interrupts on), then interrupts off. Changes: B.","comment":"40 frames"},
        "9897": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "9898": {"synopsis":"One frame.","comment":"One frame"},
        "9899": {"comment":"40 of them"},
        "9901": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "9903": {"synopsis":"A delay: HL counted down from $3000.\nChanges: A, HL.","comment":"$3000 rounds"},
        "9906": {"synopsis":"One round.","comment":"One round"},
        "9907": {"comment":"Time spent"},
        "9911": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "9913": {"comment":"No: again"},
        "9916": {"synopsis":"Waits until no key is down, then for ENTER or SPACE (TEST_KEY_WAIT), then beeps\n(TEST_BEEP).\nExit: carry for ENTER, no carry for SPACE; interrupts off.\nKeeps BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL, DE and BC kept"},
        "9919": {"comment":"All half-rows (port $00FE)"},
        "9922": {"synopsis":"Until every key is up.","comment":"No key down?"},
        "9928": {"comment":"Not yet: again"},
        "9930": {"synopsis":"Until ENTER or SPACE.","comment":"A key (TEST_KEY_WAIT)"},
        "9933": {"comment":"ENTER ($21)? Carry"},
        "9936": {"comment":"ENTER: done"},
        "9938": {"comment":"SPACE ($20)?"},
        "9940": {"comment":"Neither: another key"},
        "9942": {"synopsis":"The answer's flags kept over a beep.","comment":"Flags kept; a beep (TEST_BEEP)"},
        "9943": {"comment":"The beep (TEST_BEEP)"},
        "9951": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key: TEST_KEY_SCAN.","comment":"Scanned until a key is down"},
        "9955": {"synopsis":"Scans the keyboard until a key is down. Each key gets a number from its half-row and bit:\nhalf-row $FEFE gives $27, $1F, $17, $0F, $07 for bits 0-4 and each later half-row one less\n($BFFE bit 0, ENTER, is $21; $7FFE gives SPACE $20, SYMBOL SHIFT $18). A third key starts\nthe scan again.\nExit: A = E = the last key found; D = the one before, $FF when only one.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"L = $2F: the first half-row's number"},
        "9957": {"comment":"No key yet: D and E = $FF"},
        "9960": {"comment":"Half-row $FEFE first"},
        "9963": {"synopsis":"One half-row.","comment":"Keys down in it?"},
        "9968": {"comment":"None: the next half-row"},
        "9970": {"comment":"H = them"},
        "9971": {"comment":"A = the half-row's number"},
        "9972": {"synopsis":"A key found: a third one starts again.","comment":"A third key? Then again from the start"},
        "9973": {"comment":"Yes: again from the start"},
        "9975": {"synopsis":"The key's bit found, its number worked out.","comment":"Less 8 for each bit"},
        "9977": {"comment":"This bit?"},
        "9979": {"comment":"Not this bit: the next"},
        "9981": {"comment":"D = the key before, E = this one"},
        "9983": {"comment":"More keys in the half-row?"},
        "9985": {"synopsis":"The next half-row, up to $7FFE.","comment":"The next half-row's number"},
        "9986": {"comment":"The next half-row; all eight?"},
        "9988": {"comment":"Not the last: again"},
        "9990": {"comment":"A key found? A = it"},
        "9993": {"comment":"Yes: back"},
        "9994": {"comment":"None? Scan again"},
        "10000": {"synopsis":"Prints the bytes at HL up to an $FF (RST $10).\nExit: HL at the $FF.\nChanges: A.","comment":"The end?"},
        "10003": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "10004": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "10005": {"comment":"The next"},
        "10006": {"comment":"Again"},
        "10008": {"synopsis":"Prints INK B and PAPER C.\nChanges: A.","comment":"INK B"},
        "10010": {"comment":"INK"},
        "10012": {"comment":"Colour B"},
        "10013": {"comment":"PAPER C"},
        "10015": {"comment":"PAPER"},
        "10017": {"comment":"Colour C"},
        "10019": {"synopsis":"Prints A (ROM 3's PRINT_A at $0010).","comment":"Printed (ROM 3's PRINT_A)"},
        "10023": {"synopsis":"Clears the screen (ROM 3's CLEAR_SCREEN) and prints COLOUR_RESET_SEQ.","comment":"Screen cleared (ROM 3's CLEAR_SCREEN)"},
        "10026": {"comment":"Plain colours (COLOUR_RESET)"},
        "10029": {"synopsis":"A short beep: the tone routine at $34F6 with HL = $0100 and DE = $00A0; interrupts\noff after it.","comment":"The tone's HL and DE"},
        "10035": {"synopsis":"The tone at $34F6 with HL and DE as given (from $281A and $2C93); interrupts off after it.","comment":"The tone ($34F6)"},
        "10038": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "10040": {"synopsis":"Carry when SPACE is up (port $7FFE bit 0). No call or jump in this ROM's code reaches it.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Half-row $7FFE"},
        "10044": {"comment":"Carry: SPACE up"},
        "10046": {"synopsis":"As SPACE_UP, through RR A (from $2A05).\nChanges: A.","comment":"Half-row $7FFE"},
        "10050": {"comment":"Carry: SPACE up"},
        "10053": {"synopsis":"Z when, in half-row $7FFE, SPACE and SYMBOL SHIFT are down and M, N and B up. No call or\njump in this ROM's code reaches it.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Half-row $7FFE"},
        "10057": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 1 down, 2-4 up?"},
        "10062": {"synopsis":"Prints D spaces; A' = $38. No call or jump in this ROM's code reaches it.\nExit: D = 0.","comment":"A' = $38"},
        "10065": {"synopsis":"One space.","comment":"A space"},
        "10067": {"comment":"Printed (TEST_PRINT_A)"},
        "10070": {"comment":"D of them"},
        "10071": {"comment":"Until D is 0"},
        "10074": {"synopsis":"Tests the keys: screen cleared, BORDCR = $38, border white, the text at $2F24 printed, a\ndelay (TEST_DELAY), then KEY_TEST_KEYS.","comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "10077": {"comment":"BORDCR: paper white, ink black"},
        "10082": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "10084": {"comment":"Border white"},
        "10086": {"comment":"The text at $2F24"},
        "10092": {"comment":"A delay (TEST_DELAY)"},
        "10095": {"comment":"The keys (KEY_TEST_KEYS)"},
        "10099": {"synopsis":"Asks for the keys listed at $284E in turn ($FF at its end): each a key number as\nTEST_KEY_SCAN gives it, or a code for a pair of keys (KEY_CAPS_PAIR, KEY_SYM_PAIR). Any\nother\nkey or pair is passed over; the code in E goes on to the comparison at $2806.","comment":"The list of keys expected"},
        "10103": {"synopsis":"The next key expected.","comment":"The list's place"},
        "10104": {"comment":"A = the key expected"},
        "10105": {"comment":"The end ($FF)?"},
        "10106": {"comment":"The list done"},
        "10107": {"comment":"The place kept"},
        "10108": {"comment":"A key (TEST_KEY_WAIT)"},
        "10111": {"comment":"A pause of $1000 rounds"},
        "10114": {"synopsis":"The pause.","comment":"Down to 0"},
        "10117": {"comment":"Not yet"},
        "10119": {"comment":"One key only?"},
        "10122": {"comment":"Single: KEY_CODE_READY"},
        "10124": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT ($27) and another?"},
        "10126": {"comment":"Yes: KEY_CAPS_PAIR"},
        "10128": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT ($18) first?"},
        "10130": {"comment":"Yes: KEY_SYM_PAIR"},
        "10132": {"comment":"D and E swapped: SYMBOL SHIFT last?"},
        "10137": {"comment":"Yes: KEY_SYM_PAIR"},
        "10139": {"comment":"Another pair: passed over"},
        "10141": {"synopsis":"CAPS SHIFT and E's key: 0 gives $28, 1 $29, 2 $2A, 3 $2B, 4 $2C, 5 $2D, 6 $2E, 7 $2F, 8 $30,\n9 $31, SPACE $32, SYMBOL SHIFT $37; any other is passed over.","comment":"E = the other key: 0?"},
        "10148": {"comment":"1?"},
        "10154": {"comment":"2?"},
        "10160": {"comment":"3?"},
        "10166": {"comment":"4?"},
        "10172": {"comment":"5?"},
        "10178": {"comment":"6?"},
        "10184": {"comment":"7?"},
        "10190": {"comment":"8?"},
        "10196": {"comment":"9?"},
        "10202": {"comment":"SPACE?"},
        "10208": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "10214": {"comment":"Any other: passed over"},
        "10216": {"synopsis":"SYMBOL SHIFT and E's key: M gives $33, N $34, O $35, P $36; any other is passed over.","comment":"E = the other key: M?"},
        "10221": {"synopsis":"The code in E (a single key comes here with Z set): on to the comparison at $2806.","comment":"Matched: to the comparison"},
        "10223": {"comment":"N?"},
        "10229": {"comment":"O?"},
        "10235": {"comment":"P?"},
        "10241": {"comment":"Not one of them: wait again"},
        "10243": {"comment":"Always taken: NZ from the CP"},
        "10246": {"synopsis":"The keyboard test's check of one key (from the combining at $279D-$27FF): code E against the\nexpected one at HL, which is kept on the stack.\n1. Different: back to the wait at $2777 for\nthe same key.\n2. The same: the next entry stacked in its place; a short tone (TONE_OUT\nthrough $2733, HL = DE = $0080).\n3. The key's square in the picture painted red: its place\nfrom KEY_TEST_PLACES, $3B bytes on, gives the row (high nibble x 2 + 5) and the column (low\nnibble x 2 + 1), and a space is printed there with PAPER 2.\n4. On to the next key at $2777.","comment":"The code"},
        "10247": {"comment":"Expected one at HL, still stacked"},
        "10249": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "10250": {"comment":"No: wait again"},
        "10253": {"comment":"Next entry stacked instead"},
        "10256": {"comment":"A short tone: HL = DE = $0080"},
        "10262": {"comment":"Registers kept around it"},
        "10266": {"comment":"TONE_OUT, then DI"},
        "10269": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "10273": {"comment":"HL = the next entry, still stacked"},
        "10275": {"comment":"PAPER 2: red"},
        "10278": {"comment":"Colour 2"},
        "10281": {"comment":"Back to the matched entry"},
        "10282": {"comment":"Its place, $3B bytes on"},
        "10286": {"comment":"High nibble x 2"},
        "10289": {"comment":"Down three bits: the nibble x 2"},
        "10292": {"comment":"B = that + 6"},
        "10296": {"comment":"Low nibble x 2 + 1"},
        "10297": {"comment":"Low nibble only"},
        "10300": {"comment":"+ 1"},
        "10303": {"comment":"C = the column"},
        "10304": {"comment":"AT B - 1, C"},
        "10307": {"comment":"Row B - 1"},
        "10310": {"comment":"Column C"},
        "10312": {"comment":"A red space over the key"},
        "10315": {"comment":"Next key"},
        "10318": {"synopsis":"The keyboard test's keys in the order the picture (KEY_TEST_PIC) shows them, row by row:\n58 key codes as the scan at $26E3 numbers them ($27 CAPS SHIFT, $18 SYMBOL SHIFT, $26 A,\n$21 ENTER, $20 SPACE, ...), with $28-$32 and $37 for a key pressed with CAPS SHIFT and\n$33-$37 for one with SYMBOL SHIFT, as $279D-$2806 combine them. CAPS SHIFT and SYMBOL SHIFT\nare each in it twice. $FF ends it. Read at $2778 and $2807."},
        "10377": {"synopsis":"Where each key of KEY_TEST_CODES is drawn, one byte per key at the same index ($3B bytes\non): the high nibble gives the row (x 2 + 5), the low one the column (x 2 + 1). Read at\n$282E."},
        "10435": {"synopsis":"The SYMBOL SHIFT and A test: the screen cleared ($2727), border cyan, INK 6 and PAPER 0\n($2718), the instructions (SYMA_TEST_MSG); then the wait until SYMBOL SHIFT and A are both\ndown (SYMA_HELD), and $0200 more scans that must all find them still down.\nExit: through $242E, the result into IX: carry when they were held throughout.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "10438": {"comment":"Border 5: cyan"},
        "10442": {"comment":"INK 6, PAPER 0"},
        "10448": {"comment":"Title and instructions"},
        "10454": {"synopsis":"Waits until both keys are down.","comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT and A down?"},
        "10457": {"comment":"Not yet: again"},
        "10459": {"comment":"$0200 scans with both held"},
        "10462": {"synopsis":"One more scan with both held.","comment":"Count kept round the scan"},
        "10463": {"comment":"Still both down?"},
        "10467": {"comment":"Let go: failed"},
        "10469": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "10472": {"comment":"More to go"},
        "10474": {"comment":"Held throughout: passed"},
        "10475": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "10478": {"synopsis":"Let go too soon: no carry.","comment":"Failed: no carry"},
        "10482": {"synopsis":"Whether the keys down are SYMBOL SHIFT ($18) and A ($26), in either order, by the scan at\n$26DF.\nExit: Z when they are.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"D, E = the keys down"},
        "10485": {"comment":"The first SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "10490": {"comment":"No: the two swapped"},
        "10493": {"comment":"The other SYMBOL SHIFT?"},
        "10495": {"comment":"Neither: NZ"},
        "10496": {"synopsis":"SYMBOL SHIFT found: is the other key A?","comment":"Then the other A?"},
        "10499": {"comment":"Z when it is"},
        "10500": {"synopsis":"The test program's first test (from $21F0): $267C (on through the start-up code at $016C),\nthe colour bars and a tone (COLOUR_BARS), the title, the instructions and the warning\n(TITLE_MSG), the answer read ($26BC: ENTER passes, SPACE fails) and recorded in IX ($242E);\nthen the sound chip's mixer (register 7) set to $FF, all off.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Start-up's set-up at $016C, A' = $52"},
        "10503": {"comment":"Colour bars and a tone"},
        "10506": {"comment":"BC = 0 (not read by the printer)"},
        "10509": {"comment":"Title, instructions, warning"},
        "10515": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "10518": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "10521": {"comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "10527": {"comment":"Register 7 (mixer) = $FF: all off"},
        "10529": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "10534": {"comment":"$FF written"},
        "10538": {"synopsis":"The colour test's picture and tone: the top attribute row gets 16 pairs of cells with\nattribute 0, 8, 16 ... 120 (PAPER 0-7, then the same with BRIGHT 1) and is copied down the\nwhole screen; the sound chip's registers are set from AY_SETTINGS; the mixer (register 7) =\n$FB, the tone on channel C only.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Attribute 0 first"},
        "10539": {"comment":"Top attribute row"},
        "10542": {"comment":"16 pairs"},
        "10544": {"synopsis":"One pair of cells.","comment":"Two cells alike"},
        "10547": {"comment":"Next paper colour; BRIGHT from the 9th"},
        "10550": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "10552": {"comment":"The row copied down the screen"},
        "10555": {"comment":"The other 23 rows"},
        "10560": {"comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "10566": {"comment":"Register/value pairs"},
        "10569": {"synopsis":"One register/value pair, until a byte with bit 7 set.","comment":"Register number"},
        "10571": {"comment":"The end marker?"},
        "10573": {"comment":"Yes: the mixer next"},
        "10575": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "10578": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "10580": {"comment":"Written"},
        "10583": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "10585": {"synopsis":"The mixer: tone C only.","comment":"AY ports again"},
        "10591": {"comment":"$FB: only channel C's tone on"},
        "10593": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "10598": {"comment":"Written"},
        "10602": {"synopsis":"The ULA test: the screen cleared, the title (ULA_TEST_MSG); OUT_LOOP copied to $6000 and\nrun there, in contended RAM; then, when a byte at $8000 keeps $AA, copied to $8000 and run\nthere too; border yellow. It always passes.\nExit: through $242E, carry into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "10605": {"comment":"ULA TEST title"},
        "10611": {"comment":"OUT_LOOP to $6000"},
        "10617": {"comment":"Run in contended RAM"},
        "10620": {"comment":"Does $8000 keep a byte?"},
        "10625": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "10628": {"comment":"Kept?"},
        "10630": {"comment":"No: skip"},
        "10632": {"comment":"OUT_LOOP to $8000 too"},
        "10638": {"comment":"Run in uncontended RAM"},
        "10641": {"synopsis":"Border yellow; passed.","comment":"Border 6: yellow"},
        "10645": {"comment":"Always passed"},
        "10646": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "10649": {"synopsis":"Copies OUT_LOOP's $3B bytes to DE.\nEntry: DE = the place.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"From OUT_LOOP"},
        "10652": {"comment":"$3B bytes"},
        "10658": {"synopsis":"Copied to $6000 and $8000 by ULA_TEST and run there: $2000 rounds of 16 writes to port\n$FE, A flipping between $00 and $FF (border black and white, the MIC and speaker bits\ntoggling). Its only jump is relative, so it runs anywhere.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"$2000 rounds"},
        "10661": {"synopsis":"One round of 16 writes.","comment":"Border 0 first"},
        "10665": {"comment":"Flipped between the writes"},
        "10711": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "10714": {"comment":"More rounds"},
        "10716": {"comment":"Done"},
        "10717": {"synopsis":"The joystick test: the screen cleared and the instructions and picture (JOY_TEST_MSG); then\nscan after scan of the keyboard rows the joysticks read as, $EFFE (joystick 1, kept in D)\nand $F7FE (joystick 2, in E): each direction seen clears its bit, and when the bits change\nevery label seen so far is painted out (JOY_WIPE). All ten seen: passed; SPACE gives up:\nfailed.\nExit: through $242E, the result into IX: carry when all ten were seen.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "10720": {"comment":"Instructions and picture"},
        "10726": {"comment":"Five directions each, all unseen"},
        "10729": {"synopsis":"One scan of both joysticks.","comment":"The state kept for the next scan"},
        "10730": {"comment":"Row $EFFE: joystick 1"},
        "10733": {"comment":"Bits 0-4: 0 when pressed"},
        "10735": {"comment":"Pressed bits as 1s"},
        "10736": {"comment":"Cleared from D"},
        "10738": {"comment":"D = what is still unseen"},
        "10739": {"comment":"Row $F7FE: joystick 2"},
        "10742": {"comment":"Bits 0-4: 0 when pressed"},
        "10744": {"comment":"Pressed bits as 1s"},
        "10745": {"comment":"Cleared from E"},
        "10747": {"comment":"E = what is still unseen"},
        "10748": {"comment":"BC = the last state"},
        "10749": {"comment":"Joystick 1 changed?"},
        "10753": {"comment":"Joystick 2 changed?"},
        "10757": {"comment":"SPACE pressed? (carry: no)"},
        "10760": {"comment":"Not pressed: again"},
        "10762": {"comment":"A zero byte read: again"},
        "10764": {"comment":"Given up: failed"},
        "10765": {"comment":"To the record"},
        "10767": {"synopsis":"Every direction seen: carry.","comment":"All seen: passed"},
        "10768": {"synopsis":"The result into IX.","comment":"Result into IX"},
        "10771": {"synopsis":"The bits changed: the label of every direction seen so far painted out, joystick 1's\nfrom D's bits 0-4, then joystick 2's from E's, with their places from JOY_PLACES.","comment":"New state kept"},
        "10772": {"comment":"Joystick 1's label places"},
        "10775": {"comment":"Five directions"},
        "10777": {"synopsis":"One direction of joystick 1.","comment":"Next bit: seen?"},
        "10779": {"comment":"Seen: its label painted out"},
        "10782": {"comment":"Next place"},
        "10784": {"comment":"Next of five"},
        "10786": {"comment":"Joystick 2's five"},
        "10788": {"synopsis":"One direction of joystick 2.","comment":"Next bit: seen?"},
        "10790": {"comment":"Seen: its label painted out"},
        "10793": {"comment":"Next place"},
        "10795": {"comment":"Next of five"},
        "10797": {"comment":"State back"},
        "10798": {"comment":"Everything seen?"},
        "10800": {"comment":"Yes: passed"},
        "10802": {"comment":"Not yet: again"},
        "10805": {"synopsis":"Paints one label out: two spaces with PAPER 2 at the place HL points to (a row, 3 below\nthe screen row, then a column), then PAPER 7.\nEntry: HL = the place's row byte.\nExit: HL as it came.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Counter kept"},
        "10806": {"comment":"B = row, C = column"},
        "10809": {"comment":"AT B - 3, C"},
        "10812": {"comment":"Row - 3"},
        "10817": {"comment":"Column"},
        "10819": {"comment":"PAPER 2: red"},
        "10825": {"comment":"Two red spaces"},
        "10828": {"comment":"Second space"},
        "10831": {"comment":"PAPER 7"},
        "10837": {"comment":"HL back to the row byte"},
        "10838": {"comment":"Counter back"},
        "10840": {"synopsis":"The second screen test: with interrupts off, the attributes all 0 (black on black); the\ntitle and 'Passed - press [ENTER]' printed; RAM bank 7 paged in at $C000 and the screen\ncopied to its screen ($C000-$D7FF); the title and 'Failed - press [SPACE]' printed over the\nnormal screen; bit 3 of port $7FFD set, which shows bank 7's screen, and both screens'\nattributes set to $38 so the text shows. The answer ($26BC: ENTER passes) is recorded in IX;\nthen the screen cleared, the paging byte put back, cleared again, interrupts on.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "10843": {"comment":"No interrupts while paging"},
        "10844": {"comment":"Attributes all 0: black on black"},
        "10850": {"comment":"All $0300 attribute bytes"},
        "10857": {"comment":"Title, not yet visible"},
        "10863": {"comment":"'Passed - press [ENTER]'"},
        "10869": {"comment":"Paging byte kept"},
        "10873": {"comment":"RAM bank 7 at $C000"},
        "10875": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "10878": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "10883": {"comment":"The screen copied to bank 7's"},
        "10889": {"comment":"$1800 bytes: the pixels"},
        "10894": {"comment":"Title again, on the normal screen"},
        "10900": {"comment":"'Failed - press [SPACE]' over it"},
        "10906": {"comment":"Bit 3: bank 7's screen shown"},
        "10911": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "10914": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "10919": {"comment":"Normal screen's attributes $38"},
        "10928": {"comment":"$38: black INK on white PAPER"},
        "10932": {"comment":"Bank 7's too"},
        "10941": {"comment":"$38 there too"},
        "10945": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "10948": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "10951": {"comment":"Screen cleared"},
        "10954": {"comment":"Paging byte back"},
        "10955": {"comment":"Its copy"},
        "10958": {"comment":"Port $7FFD: bank and screen as before"},
        "10963": {"comment":"Cleared again, the normal screen"},
        "10966": {"comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "10968": {"synopsis":"SCREEN_TEST's title: AT 8,3, PAPER 0, INK 0, 'Screen switching test'."},
        "10997": {"synopsis":"AT 12,3, PAPER 0, INK 0, 'Passed - press [ENTER]': seen on the second screen."},
        "11027": {"synopsis":"The same place: 'Failed - press [SPACE]', seen on the normal screen."},
        "11057": {"synopsis":"The cassette output test: the screen cleared, border red, BORDCR = $08, the title\n(CASS_OUT_MSG); a tone of $0A00 cycles with HL = $0100 sent to the MIC output (port $FE bit\n3) by an inline copy of TONE_OUT's loop that flips bit 3 and holds the speaker bit set;\nthen HEARD_TONE_MSG and the answer ($26BC: ENTER passes).\nExit: through $242E, the result into IX.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11060": {"comment":"Border 2: red"},
        "11064": {"comment":"BORDCR = $08: border 1 in the tone"},
        "11069": {"comment":"CASSETTE OUTPUT TEST title"},
        "11075": {"comment":"HL = $0100, DE = $0A00 cycles"},
        "11081": {"comment":"No interrupts: exact timing"},
        "11082": {"comment":"IX kept (the results)"},
        "11084": {"comment":"L's low bits: 0-3 extra NOPs"},
        "11085": {"comment":"L / 4: the inner count"},
        "11089": {"comment":"IX = MIC_TONE_NOPS + 3 - low bits"},
        "11095": {"comment":"From MIC_TONE_NOPS"},
        "11099": {"comment":"+ 3 - low bits"},
        "11101": {"comment":"Border from BORDCR"},
        "11104": {"comment":"Bits 3-5: the border colour"},
        "11106": {"comment":"Down to bits 0-2"},
        "11109": {"comment":"Speaker bit 4 held set"},
        "11111": {"synopsis":"The entry JP (IX) uses: 0 to 3 NOPs, then the delay.","comment":"0-3 of these run, by IX"},
        "11114": {"comment":"B, C one more for the first DEC"},
        "11116": {"synopsis":"A half-cycle's delay: C inner rounds, B outer ones.","comment":"Inner delay"},
        "11117": {"comment":"Inner rounds"},
        "11119": {"comment":"C = $3F for the later rounds"},
        "11121": {"comment":"Outer count"},
        "11122": {"comment":"Outer rounds"},
        "11125": {"comment":"MIC bit 3 flipped"},
        "11127": {"comment":"Out: MIC flipped"},
        "11129": {"comment":"Outer count again; port byte in C"},
        "11131": {"comment":"MIC bit now set?"},
        "11133": {"comment":"Rising edge: the longer half"},
        "11135": {"comment":"Cycles left?"},
        "11137": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "11139": {"comment":"Port byte back, inner count from L"},
        "11141": {"comment":"One cycle fewer"},
        "11142": {"comment":"Next half-cycle"},
        "11144": {"synopsis":"After a rising edge: the second half-cycle, one inner count longer.","comment":"One inner count longer"},
        "11148": {"synopsis":"The cycles done: IX back; the question and the answer.","comment":"IX back"},
        "11150": {"comment":"BC = $1200 (not read by the printer)"},
        "11153": {"comment":"Heard the tone?"},
        "11159": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11162": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11166": {"synopsis":"The test program's verdict (jumped to after the last test): the 16 results in IX, a bit\neach. All set: border green, ALL_PASSED_MSG. Otherwise border red, TEST_FAILED_MSG and, for\nevery bit that is 0, its message from FAIL_MSGS (E's bits 0-7, then D's). Then REPEAT_MSG\nand a wait: ENTER is ignored, SPACE (BREAK) restarts the machine at $0000.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11169": {"comment":"DE = the 16 results"},
        "11172": {"comment":"All bits set?"},
        "11174": {"comment":"$FF only when both are"},
        "11176": {"comment":"No: something failed"},
        "11178": {"comment":"Border 4: green"},
        "11182": {"comment":"'ALL TESTS PASSED'"},
        "11188": {"comment":"On to the repeat prompt"},
        "11190": {"synopsis":"Something failed: the failed tests listed.","comment":"Border 2: red"},
        "11192": {"comment":"Border written"},
        "11194": {"comment":"'TEST FAILED, because:-'"},
        "11200": {"comment":"BC = $0807 (B counted, not read)"},
        "11203": {"comment":"The results again"},
        "11205": {"comment":"Results again"},
        "11206": {"comment":"Kept for D's turn"},
        "11207": {"comment":"FAIL_MSGS: E's bits first"},
        "11210": {"comment":"Eight bits"},
        "11212": {"synopsis":"One bit of E: its message when it is 0.","comment":"Next bit: passed?"},
        "11214": {"comment":"Yes: no message"},
        "11216": {"comment":"Entry and count kept"},
        "11218": {"comment":"The message's address"},
        "11220": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "11222": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "11225": {"comment":"Count and entry back"},
        "11227": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "11229": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11230": {"comment":"More bits"},
        "11232": {"comment":"D's bits now"},
        "11233": {"comment":"E = D's results"},
        "11234": {"comment":"Eight bits"},
        "11236": {"synopsis":"One bit of D: its message when it is 0.","comment":"Next bit: passed?"},
        "11238": {"comment":"Yes: no message"},
        "11240": {"comment":"Entry, count, BC kept"},
        "11243": {"comment":"The message's address"},
        "11244": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "11247": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "11250": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "11253": {"comment":"D's failures counted in B"},
        "11254": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "11256": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11257": {"comment":"More bits"},
        "11259": {"synopsis":"The repeat prompt and the wait.","comment":"'Hold [BREAK] to repeat tests'"},
        "11262": {"comment":"BC = $1000 (not read by the printer)"},
        "11268": {"synopsis":"Waits for SPACE; ENTER is ignored.","comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11271": {"comment":"ENTER: wait again"},
        "11273": {"comment":"SPACE: restart the machine"},
        "11274": {"comment":"$0000: the machine starts again"},
        "11277": {"synopsis":"Two new lines and 'Hold [BREAK] to repeat tests'."},
        "11308": {"synopsis":"The RS232 test, through the sound chip's register 14 (its I/O port) and a loopback\nconnector: $FF, $FE, $FD, $FB and $F7 are written and must read back as $FF, $7E, $BD, $DB\nand $E7, so bit 0 must come back on bit 7, 1 on 6, 2 on 5 and 3 on 4. Nothing is printed.\nExit: through $242E, the result into IX: carry when every value read back right.","comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "11314": {"comment":"Register 14 selected"},
        "11315": {"comment":"Register 14"},
        "11319": {"comment":"$FF written"},
        "11321": {"comment":"B = $BF: write"},
        "11324": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11327": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "11329": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11331": {"comment":"Bit 0 low"},
        "11334": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11336": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11339": {"comment":"Bits 0 and 7 low: $7E?"},
        "11341": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11343": {"comment":"Bit 1 low"},
        "11346": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11348": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11351": {"comment":"Bits 1 and 6 low: $BD?"},
        "11353": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11355": {"comment":"Bit 2 low"},
        "11358": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11360": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11363": {"comment":"Bits 2 and 5 low: $DB?"},
        "11365": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11367": {"comment":"Bit 3 low"},
        "11370": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11372": {"comment":"Read back"},
        "11375": {"comment":"Bits 3 and 4 low: $E7?"},
        "11377": {"comment":"No: failed"},
        "11379": {"comment":"All right: passed"},
        "11383": {"synopsis":"A value read back wrong: no carry.","comment":"Failed: no carry"},
        "11387": {"synopsis":"The ULA sound test: the screen cleared, border red, BORDCR = $08, the title\n(ULA_SOUND_MSG); a tone on the speaker (TONE_OUT through $2733: HL = $0100, DE = $0A00);\nHEARD_TONE_MSG and the answer ($26BC: ENTER passes).\nExit: through $242E, the result into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11390": {"comment":"Border 2: red"},
        "11394": {"comment":"BORDCR = $08: border 1 in the tone"},
        "11399": {"comment":"ULA SOUND TEST title"},
        "11405": {"comment":"HL = $0100, DE = $0A00 cycles"},
        "11408": {"comment":"$0A00 cycles"},
        "11411": {"comment":"TONE_OUT, then DI"},
        "11414": {"comment":"BC = $1200 (not read by the printer)"},
        "11417": {"comment":"Heard the tone?"},
        "11423": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11426": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11430": {"synopsis":"The sound chip test: the screen cleared, border cyan, the title (GI_SOUND_MSG); the\nregisters set from AY_SETTINGS; the tones of channels A, B and C each alone for 40 frames\n(mixer $FE, $FD, $FB), then all three together (mixer $F8) for 40 more, then the mixer $FF\n(all off); FOUR_SOUNDS_MSG and the answer ($26BC: ENTER passes).\nExit: through $242E, the result into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "11433": {"comment":"Border 5: cyan"},
        "11437": {"comment":"GI SOUND TEST title"},
        "11443": {"comment":"AY: C = $FD; B = $FF selects, $BF writes"},
        "11449": {"comment":"Register/value pairs"},
        "11452": {"synopsis":"One register/value pair, until a byte with bit 7 set.","comment":"Register number"},
        "11454": {"comment":"The end marker?"},
        "11456": {"comment":"Yes: the mixer next"},
        "11458": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "11459": {"comment":"Out"},
        "11461": {"comment":"Its value"},
        "11463": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11464": {"comment":"Out"},
        "11466": {"comment":"Next pair"},
        "11468": {"synopsis":"The four sounds.","comment":"AY ports again"},
        "11474": {"comment":"Three channels, one at a time"},
        "11476": {"comment":"Mixer $FE: tone A only"},
        "11478": {"synopsis":"One channel's tone alone for 40 frames.","comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "11479": {"comment":"Register 7"},
        "11483": {"comment":"Mixer written"},
        "11484": {"comment":"Out: mixer value H"},
        "11486": {"comment":"Kept round the wait"},
        "11489": {"comment":"40 frames"},
        "11495": {"comment":"Next channel: $FD, then $FB"},
        "11496": {"comment":"Carry into bit 0, next bit out"},
        "11498": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11499": {"comment":"More channels"},
        "11501": {"comment":"Mixer $F8: all three tones"},
        "11503": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "11508": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11511": {"comment":"Kept round the wait"},
        "11514": {"comment":"40 frames"},
        "11517": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "11520": {"comment":"Mixer $FF: all off"},
        "11522": {"comment":"Register 7 selected"},
        "11527": {"comment":"$FF written"},
        "11528": {"comment":"Written"},
        "11530": {"comment":"BC = $0A00 (not read by the printer)"},
        "11533": {"comment":"Heard four sounds?"},
        "11539": {"comment":"ENTER (carry) or SPACE"},
        "11542": {"comment":"Result into IX"},
        "11545": {"synopsis":"The sound chip's registers for COLOUR_BARS and GI_SOUND_TEST, as register/value pairs\nended by $80: tone periods A $0040, B $0080, C $0100; noise period $1F; volumes A, B and C\n15. Read at $2949 and $2CBC."},
        "11566": {"synopsis":"The question after the ULA sound and cassette output tones: 'Press [ENTER] if you heard\nthe tone, else press [SPACE]'."},
        "11623": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 15 (D bit 7 of the results): the colour test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "11643": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 7 (E bit 7 of the results): the ULA sound test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11666": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 10 (D bit 2 of the results): the SYMBOL SHIFT/A test's failure line, ended\nby a new line."},
        "11693": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 9 (D bit 1 of the results): the ULA test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "11710": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 8 (D bit 0 of the results): the RS232 test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "11729": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 11 (D bit 3 of the results): the sound chip test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11751": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 12 (D bit 4 of the results): the RAM paging test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11777": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 6 (E bit 6 of the results): the joystick test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "11799": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 14 (D bit 6 of the results): the IC 7 checksum's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11821": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 13 (D bit 5 of the results): the IC 8 checksum's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11843": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 1 (E bit 1 of the results): the disk test's failure line, ended by a new\nline."},
        "11862": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 4 (E bit 4 of the results): the second screen test's failure line, ended by\na new line."},
        "11889": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 5 (E bit 5 of the results): the cassette output test's failure line, ended\nby a new line."},
        "11913": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 0 (E bit 0 of the results): the cassette input test's failure line, ended by\na new line."},
        "11936": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 3 (E bit 3 of the results): the printer BUSY test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11962": {"synopsis":"FAIL_MSGS entry 2 (E bit 2 of the results): the printer DATA test's failure line, ended by a\nnew line."},
        "11988": {"synopsis":"TEST_REPORT's failure lines, one word per result bit: entries 0-7 for E's bits 0-7 (IX's\nlow byte), 8-15 for D's. In order: cassette input, disk, printer DATA, printer BUSY, second\nscreen, cassette output, joystick, ULA sound; RS232, ULA, SYMBOL SHIFT/A, sound chip, RAM\npaging, IC 8, IC 7, colour. The first test shifted into IX ends up in D's bit 7, the last\nin E's bit 0. Read at $2BD2 and $2BEB."},
        "12020": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, FLASH 1, 'ROM TEST FAILED', FLASH 0 and a new line. No code in this ROM loads its\naddress."},
        "12044": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, FLASH 1, 'RAM TEST FAILED', FLASH 0 and a new line. No code in this ROM loads its\naddress."},
        "12068": {"synopsis":"The keyboard test's screen (printed at $2769): AT 2,0, the title, then INVERSE 1 and the\nkeyboard drawn row by row as letters two columns apart, a lower-case letter for each key\nwithout a single character of its own (the CAPS SHIFT and SYMBOL SHIFT combinations of\nKEY_TEST_CODES, the two shifts, ENTER, BREAK); INVERSE 0, then AT 20,5, FLASH 1, 'TEST ALL\nTHE KEYS'."},
        "12518": {"synopsis":"SYMA_TEST's screen: AT 5,5, INVERSE 1 ' SYM SHFT/A  TEST ', and at rows 10-14 'Press',\n'SYM SHFT/A' (flashing) and 'for 1 sec'."},
        "12587": {"synopsis":"COLOUR_TEST's screen: AT 9,0, INVERSE 1, the test program's title and version line, 'Check\nTV tuning', a reminder to fit the loopback connector, the ENTER/SPACE question about the\ncolours, and a flashing warning that the tests corrupt disks and need factory equipment."},
        "12891": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, ' ULA TEST ', INVERSE 0, a new line."},
        "12910": {"synopsis":"AT 5,7, INVERSE 1, 'RAM DATA TESTS', AT 10,5, '.. STARTING NOW ..', INVERSE 0, a new line."},
        "12954": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, ' GI SOUND TEST ', two new lines, INVERSE 0."},
        "12979": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, ' ULA SOUND TEST ', two new lines, INVERSE 0."},
        "13005": {"synopsis":"A 0 before CASS_OUT_MSG; the print starts after it."},
        "13006": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, INVERSE 1, 'CASSETTE OUTPUT TEST', INVERSE 0, two new lines."},
        "13036": {"synopsis":"A 0 before JOY_TEST_MSG; the print starts after it."},
        "13037": {"synopsis":"JOYSTICK_TEST's screen: AT 0,10, INVERSE 1 'JOYSTICK TEST', the instructions (move both\njoysticks and press fire until the letters are wiped out; SPACE gives up) and a box drawn\nwith + - ! holding the J1 and J2 labels UP, LF, FI, RI and DN."},
        "13436": {"synopsis":"AT 5,5, ' ALL TESTS PASSED ', a new line."},
        "13459": {"synopsis":"AT 0,0, FLASH 1, ' TEST FAILED, because:- ', FLASH 0, two new lines."},
        "13493": {"synopsis":"GI_SOUND_TEST's question: 'press [ENTER] if you heard four sounds, else press [SPACE].'"},
        "13558": {"synopsis":"Makes a tone on the speaker (port $FE bit 4) for the test program, with the border in\nBORDCR's colour (its bits 3-5) and the MIC bit 3 set in every write: about DE cycles, each\nhalf-cycle a delay set by HL (H counts the outer loop, L / 4 the inner one, and L's low two\nbits pick an entry into TONE_NOPS for the finest step). Interrupts are off while it runs and\nturned on at the end. $2733 calls it.\nEntry: HL = the pitch, DE = the cycles.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"No interrupts: exact timing"},
        "13559": {"comment":"IX kept (the results)"},
        "13561": {"comment":"L's low bits: 0-3 extra NOPs"},
        "13562": {"comment":"L / 4: the inner count"},
        "13564": {"comment":"Inner count in L"},
        "13566": {"comment":"IX = TONE_NOPS + 3 - low bits"},
        "13567": {"comment":"3 - low bits"},
        "13572": {"comment":"From TONE_NOPS"},
        "13576": {"comment":"+ 3 - low bits"},
        "13578": {"comment":"Border from BORDCR"},
        "13581": {"comment":"Bits 3-5: the border colour"},
        "13583": {"comment":"Down to bits 0-2"},
        "13586": {"comment":"MIC bit 3 held set"},
        "13588": {"synopsis":"The entry JP (IX) uses: 0 to 3 NOPs, then the delay.","comment":"0-3 of these run, by IX"},
        "13591": {"comment":"B, C one more for the first DEC"},
        "13593": {"synopsis":"A half-cycle's delay: C inner rounds, B outer ones.","comment":"Inner delay"},
        "13594": {"comment":"Inner rounds"},
        "13596": {"comment":"C = $3F for the later rounds"},
        "13598": {"comment":"Outer count"},
        "13599": {"comment":"Outer rounds"},
        "13602": {"comment":"Speaker bit 4 flipped"},
        "13604": {"comment":"Out: speaker flipped"},
        "13606": {"comment":"Outer count again; port byte in C"},
        "13608": {"comment":"Speaker bit now set?"},
        "13610": {"comment":"Rising edge: the longer half"},
        "13612": {"comment":"Cycles left?"},
        "13614": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "13616": {"comment":"Port byte back, inner count from L"},
        "13618": {"comment":"One cycle fewer"},
        "13619": {"comment":"Next half-cycle"},
        "13621": {"synopsis":"After a rising edge: the second half-cycle, one inner count longer.","comment":"One inner count longer"},
        "13623": {"comment":"Next half-cycle"},
        "13625": {"synopsis":"The cycles done: interrupts on, IX back.","comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "13626": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "13629": {"synopsis":"Where JOYSTICK_TEST's ten labels are, as row/column pairs with the row 3 more than the\nscreen row: joystick 1's FI, UP, DN, RI, LF (D's bits 0-4), then joystick 2's LF, RI, DN,\nUP, FI (E's bits 0-4). Read at $2A14 and $2A36."},
        "13649": {"synopsis":"The ten labels' names in JOY_PLACES's order, two letters each, no end marker. Nothing in\nthis ROM reads them."},
        "13669": {"synopsis":"The disk test: DISK_TEST_RAM copied to $5F00 and run there, since it pages this ROM out.\nExit: through $242E, the drive test's carry into IX.","comment":"From DISK_TEST_RAM"},
        "13672": {"comment":"To $5F00"},
        "13675": {"comment":"$3D bytes"},
        "13680": {"comment":"Run there"},
        "13683": {"synopsis":"Runs at $5F00 (DISK_TEST copies it):\n1. Port $1FFD = 4: ROM 2 paged in.\n2. $0C00 bytes of\nROM 2 from $2492 (its drive test program, DT_START) copied to $6000.\n3. Port $1FFD = 0 and\nport $7FFD = $10, with their copies $5B67 and $5B5C: ROM 1 and RAM bank 0.\n4. Interrupts\non, the copy called at $6000, IX kept round it.\n5. Port $7FFD = 0 ($5B5C too): this ROM\nback; the copy's carry into IX through $242E.","comment":"$1FFD bit 2: ROM 2 in"},
        "13685": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "13690": {"comment":"ROM 2's drive test program"},
        "13693": {"comment":"To $6000"},
        "13696": {"comment":"$0C00 bytes"},
        "13699": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "13701": {"comment":"Port $1FFD = 0"},
        "13703": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "13708": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "13711": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = $10: ROM 1, bank 0"},
        "13713": {"comment":"B = $7F: port $7FFD"},
        "13717": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "13720": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "13721": {"comment":"IX kept (the results)"},
        "13723": {"comment":"The drive test"},
        "13726": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "13728": {"comment":"Its result kept"},
        "13729": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = 0: this ROM back"},
        "13731": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "13736": {"comment":"And its copy"},
        "13739": {"comment":"The result"},
        "13740": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "13744": {"synopsis":"The cassette input test: the instructions (TAPE_TEST_MSG) and a 25-frame pause (CI_WAIT);\nwith interrupts off, six black marks across attribute row 7 (columns 1, 7, ... 31); then,\nround after round, the EAR input (port $FE bit 6) polled $1000 times and its changes\ncounted, the count / 32 (at most 32) shown as a bright cyan cell over a bright blue row 8;\nuntil ENTER (passed) or SPACE (failed) is pressed.\nExit: through CI_WAIT after the result went into IX.","comment":"Screen cleared, colours reset"},
        "13747": {"comment":"Instructions"},
        "13750": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "13753": {"comment":"25 frames' pause"},
        "13756": {"comment":"No interrupts while counting"},
        "13757": {"comment":"Row 7, column 1"},
        "13760": {"comment":"Every sixth cell"},
        "13763": {"comment":"Six marks, attribute 0"},
        "13765": {"synopsis":"One mark.","comment":"A black cell"},
        "13766": {"comment":"Six cells on"},
        "13767": {"comment":"Next mark"},
        "13769": {"synopsis":"One round: $1000 polls of the EAR input and the keys, then the reading shown.","comment":"Changes counted in HL"},
        "13772": {"comment":"$1000 polls"},
        "13775": {"comment":"C = $FE: no level yet"},
        "13777": {"comment":"SPACE pressed?"},
        "13779": {"comment":"Row $7FFE"},
        "13781": {"comment":"Bit 0: SPACE"},
        "13783": {"comment":"Yes: failed"},
        "13786": {"comment":"ENTER pressed?"},
        "13789": {"comment":"Row $BFFE"},
        "13791": {"comment":"Bit 0: ENTER"},
        "13793": {"comment":"Yes: passed"},
        "13796": {"synopsis":"One poll of the EAR input.","comment":"Count the polls down"},
        "13799": {"comment":"Done: show the reading"},
        "13801": {"comment":"EAR level (bit 6)"},
        "13803": {"comment":"Only bit 6"},
        "13805": {"comment":"Same as last time?"},
        "13806": {"comment":"Same: next poll"},
        "13808": {"comment":"Changed: counted"},
        "13809": {"comment":"New level kept"},
        "13810": {"comment":"Next poll"},
        "13812": {"synopsis":"The reading: the changes / 32, at most 32.","comment":"HL x 8: H = changes / 32"},
        "13824": {"comment":"L = the reading"},
        "13825": {"comment":"Over 32?"},
        "13827": {"comment":"Compared with H"},
        "13830": {"comment":"Kept at 32"},
        "13832": {"synopsis":"Row 8 redrawn after a frame and the marker set at the reading's column.","comment":"HL = the reading"},
        "13833": {"comment":"H = 0"},
        "13834": {"comment":"Row 8's last cell"},
        "13837": {"comment":"32 cells"},
        "13839": {"comment":"$48: bright blue paper"},
        "13841": {"comment":"Wait for a frame"},
        "13842": {"comment":"One frame"},
        "13843": {"comment":"Interrupts off again"},
        "13844": {"synopsis":"One cell.","comment":"Row 8 filled, right to left"},
        "13846": {"comment":"32 cells"},
        "13848": {"comment":"DE = row 8's first cell"},
        "13849": {"comment":"The reading's cell"},
        "13850": {"comment":"$68: bright cyan marker"},
        "13852": {"comment":"Marker written"},
        "13853": {"comment":"Next round"},
        "13855": {"synopsis":"A 25-frame pause with interrupts on, then FLAGS bit 5 (a new key) cleared.\nExit: carry; interrupts on.\nChanges: B, HL, F.","comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "13856": {"comment":"25 frames"},
        "13858": {"synopsis":"One frame."},
        "13859": {"comment":"25 times"},
        "13861": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5 cleared: no key waiting"},
        "13866": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "13867": {"comment":"Done"},
        "13868": {"synopsis":"SPACE: no carry into IX (failed); the pause; out of CASS_IN_TEST.","comment":"No carry: failed"},
        "13869": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "13872": {"comment":"Pause, then out"},
        "13874": {"synopsis":"ENTER: carry into IX (passed); the pause; out of CASS_IN_TEST.","comment":"Carry: passed"},
        "13875": {"comment":"Into IX"},
        "13878": {"comment":"Pause, then out"},
        "13880": {"synopsis":"CASS_IN_TEST's instructions: AT 0,0, insert the test tape and press PLAY, adjust the\nazimuth screw for the largest reading, then ENTER for success or SPACE for failure."},
        "14023": {"synopsis":"Bytes nothing in this ROM reads, up to $37BA. Each byte XORed with $30 and with bit 7\ndropped gives, for most of them, a credits text with lines ended by $0D: who did the test\nprogram, thanks, and the machines and tools it was written with. Some bytes, mostly near\nthe end, do not decode that way."},
        "14267": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3DFF."},
        "15872": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's CALL_ROM0, of which these are the same bytes: it parks AF and HL at $5B56 and\n$5B52, reads the word after the CALL into HL (stepping the return address past it) and\nclears bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) with interrupts off. That OUT, at $3E1C, pages this\nROM in, so the code goes on here at $3E1E: CALL_ROM0_BACK is pushed as the return, AF and\nHL are restored and the RET jumps to the address. Nothing in this ROM calls it.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "15875": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "15877": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "15880": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "15881": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "15885": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "15886": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "15888": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "15894": {"comment":"Bit 2 cleared"},
        "15897": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "15900": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3E1E here"},
        "15902": {"comment":"From here in this ROM"},
        "15903": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "15907": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "15908": {"comment":"AF and HL back"},
        "15912": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "15913": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "15916": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "15917": {"synopsis":"Where a routine called through CALL_ROM0 returns: bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67) set\nagain with interrupts off, keeping AF and BC; after the OUT at $3E3B the code goes on in ROM\n2's copy.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "15919": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD set: ROM 2"},
        "15925": {"comment":"Bit 2 set"},
        "15928": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "15931": {"comment":"ROM 2 in: on at $3E3D there"},
        "15933": {"comment":"From here in ROM 2"},
        "15934": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "15937": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3E7F."},
        "16000": {"synopsis":"Calls the address in the word after the CALL in ROM 1, keeping AF, BC and HL (parked at\n$5B56, $5B54 and $5B52): the word is read into HL and the return address stepped past it;\nbit 4 of the paging byte $5B5C (port $7FFD) is set with interrupts off, which pages ROM 1\nin, and the code goes on at $3EA2 in ROM 1's copy; CALL_ROM1_BACK is pushed as the return,\nAF, BC and HL are restored and the RET jumps to the address. The return runs ROM 1's\n$3EB5, which clears the bit again. ROM 1 has the same routine here with the bit cleared,\nfor its calls into this ROM. Called at $028A, $08E7, $0916, $0930, $0D99 and $2113.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16003": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16007": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16009": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "16012": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16013": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16017": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "16018": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "16020": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD set: ROM 1"},
        "16023": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16026": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16032": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3EA2 there"},
        "16034": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16035": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "16039": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "16040": {"comment":"AF, BC and HL back"},
        "16044": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "16045": {"comment":"BC from $5B54"},
        "16049": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "16052": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16053": {"synopsis":"Where a routine of this ROM called through ROM 1's copy of CALL_ROM1 returns: bit 4 of\n$5B5C (port $7FFD) set again with interrupts off, which pages ROM 1 back in, keeping AF and\nBC; the code after the OUT at $3EC3 runs in ROM 1.","comment":"AF and BC kept"},
        "16055": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD set: ROM 1"},
        "16058": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16061": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16067": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3EC5 there"},
        "16069": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16070": {"comment":"BC and AF back"},
        "16073": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3EFF."},
        "16128": {"synopsis":"ROM 1's CALL_ROM2, of which these are the same bytes, and of which this ROM runs the middle:\nROM 1 parks HL, BC and AF at $5B52, $5B54 and $5B56, reads the word after the CALL and\nclears bit 4 of port $7FFD (and $5B5C); that OUT, at $3F20, pages this ROM in, so\n$3F22-$3F2D\nrun here and set bit 2 of port $1FFD (and $5B67), which pages ROM 2 in, where the code goes\non at $3F2F. Nothing in this ROM calls it.","comment":"HL parked"},
        "16131": {"comment":"BC parked"},
        "16135": {"comment":"AF parked"},
        "16137": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "16140": {"comment":"The word after the CALL"},
        "16141": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16145": {"comment":"Return address stepped past it"},
        "16146": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "16148": {"comment":"Bit 4 of port $7FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16151": {"comment":"Bit 4 cleared"},
        "16154": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16160": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3F22 here"},
        "16162": {"comment":"From here in this ROM: bit 2 of $1FFD set"},
        "16165": {"comment":"Bit 2 set"},
        "16170": {"comment":"Port $1FFD"},
        "16173": {"comment":"ROM 2 in: on at $3F2F there"},
        "16175": {"comment":"From here in ROM 2"},
        "16176": {"comment":"The way back first"},
        "16180": {"comment":"Then the address"},
        "16181": {"comment":"AF, BC and HL back"},
        "16185": {"comment":"AF from $5B56"},
        "16186": {"comment":"BC from $5B54"},
        "16190": {"comment":"HL from $5B52"},
        "16193": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16194": {"synopsis":"The way back from ROM 2 to ROM 1, keeping AF and BC: ROM 2 clears bit 2 of port $1FFD (and\n$5B67), which pages this ROM in, so $3F52-$3F5D run here and set bit 4 of port $7FFD (and\n$5B5C), which pages ROM 1 back in for the RET.","comment":"BC and AF kept"},
        "16196": {"comment":"Bit 2 of port $1FFD cleared: ROM 0"},
        "16199": {"comment":"Bit 2 cleared"},
        "16202": {"comment":"Copy and port, no interrupts"},
        "16208": {"comment":"ROM 0 in: on at $3F52 here"},
        "16210": {"comment":"From here in this ROM: bit 4 set"},
        "16213": {"comment":"Bit 4 set"},
        "16218": {"comment":"Port $7FFD"},
        "16221": {"comment":"ROM 1 in: on at $3F5F there"},
        "16223": {"comment":"From here in ROM 1"},
        "16224": {"comment":"AF and BC back"},
        "16227": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3FEF."},
        "16368": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's way into this ROM: its ROM0_HOOK_A0 and ROM0_HOOK_A call $3FF0 through CALL_ROM0.\nIt jumps to $218C, which takes the zero flag, A and HL as ROM 2 passes them.","comment":"On to $218C"},
        "16371": {"synopsis":"Unused: $FF up to $3FFE."},
        "16383": {"synopsis":"The last byte, $1F. Nothing in this ROM's code reads it."}
      }
    }
  },
